{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017iKKoZuCW7iBjyP46Dnnyk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"GOV.PO.3 -- deterministic local orchestration of an approved movement\n2\t(docs/design/GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md, FROZEN).\n3\t\n4\t    py scripts/orchestrator.py start      --movement <relay-id> [options]\n5\t    py scripts/orchestrator.py status     [--movement <relay-id>] [options]\n6\t    py scripts/orchestrator.py stop       --movement <relay-id> [--force] [options]\n7\t    py scripts/orchestrator.py merge-lock {acquire|release} --movement <relay-id> [options]\n8\t    py scripts/orchestrator.py watch      [--interval SECONDS] [options]\n9\t\n10\t`<relay-id>` is the relay file's own id (`NXS-LOCAL-NNNN`), unambiguous and\n11\tresolvable to exactly one file (`relay/<relay-id>-*.json`).\n12\t\n13\t`start` reads the movement's already-approved `SESSION_START` (`entries[0]`\n14\tof its canonical relay file), computes its SHA-256 content hash, creates one\n15\tgit worktree from the packet's own `report.git.base`/`report.git.lane`\n16\tfields, writes the canonical bytes to `.nexus/approved_task.json` inside\n17\tthat worktree, and spawns a detached `claude -p` engineer process there\n18\tusing the engineer permission profile\n19\t(`.claude/nexus-engineer.settings.json`) -- then returns immediately. It\n20\tdoes not review, decide, or merge anything; merge authority stays with the\n21\tengineer's own session under the standing authorization\n22\t(`ozandurmus/nexus-agent-relay#13`). `merge-lock` is the cross-movement\n23\tserialization primitive that profile's `PreToolUse` hook\n24\t(`scripts/nexus_engineer_tool_gate.py`) calls before a `gh pr merge`.\n25\t\n26\tEvery subprocess this module spawns is built as an argument list\n27\t(`subprocess.run`/`Popen` with the default `shell=False`), never a\n28\tformatted/interpolated shell string -- the approved-task content itself is\n29\tnever placed in an argv element; it is written to a file the engineer\n30\tprocess reads with its own `Read` tool (section 3.2/3.5 of the FROZEN\n31\tamendment).\n32\t\n33\tProcess records are persistent but outside the relay file (one JSON file\n34\tper movement under `NEXUS_ORCHESTRATOR_STATE_DIR`, default a fixed\n35\tsubdirectory of the system temp root -- runtime bookkeeping, not durable\n36\tgovernance history). Liveness is always checked live (`os.kill(pid, 0)`),\n37\tnever inferred from a stale timestamp: this is stricter and simpler than a\n38\tstaleness-threshold heuristic and removes any dependency on clock skew.\n39\t\n40\tOffline except for the subprocesses it spawns (`git`, `claude`, `gh`\n41\tindirectly via the engineer session). No device, credential, or vendor\n42\tcollector access; stdlib only.\n43\t\n44\tExit codes: 0 success, 1 invalid/refused (wrong turn, duplicate start, no\n45\tfree worker slot, lock held by another movement), 2 usage error (bad\n46\targuments, missing/invalid relay file).\n47\t\"\"\"\n48\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n49\t\n50\timport argparse\n51\timport hashlib\n52\timport json\n53\timport os\n54\timport shutil\n55\timport signal\n56\timport subprocess\n57\timport sys\n58\timport tempfile\n59\timport time\n60\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n61\tfrom pathlib import Path\n62\tfrom typing import Any\n63\t\n64\tREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n65\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO_ROOT / \"scripts\"))\n66\timport local_relay as lr  # noqa: E402\n67\t\n68\tEXIT_OK, EXIT_REFUSED, EXIT_USAGE = 0, 1, 2\n69\t\n70\t#: Runtime bookkeeping lives outside the repository, mirroring\n71\t#: nexus_po_tool_gate.py's NEXUS_PO_HOOK_LOG precedent -- process records\n72\t#: are not durable governance history and must not spam the git-tracked\n73\t#: relay file with per-invocation diffs.\n74\tDEFAULT_STATE_DIR = Path(\n75\t    os.environ.get(\"NEXUS_ORCHESTRATOR_STATE_DIR\")\n76\t    or os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), \"nexus_orchestrator\")\n77\t)\n78\tDEFAULT_WORKTREES_DIR = REPO_ROOT.parent / f\"{REPO_ROOT.name}-nexus-worktrees\"\n79\tDEFAULT_MAX_WORKERS = 3\n80\tDEFAULT_RETRY_LIMIT = 2\n81\tDEFAULT_MERGE_LOCK_TTL = 600\n82\tDEFAULT_ENGINEER_PROFILE = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"nexus-engineer.settings.json\"\n83\t#: An unattended spawn has no human watching live spend; bound it. Not part\n84\t#: of the FROZEN amendment's own text -- a safety addition made before the\n85\t#: first real dispatch, named as such in this movement's own evidence.\n86\tDEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET_USD = 3.0\n87\t\n88\t#: AC-3's dashboard default poll interval, and AC-2's engineer-log summary\n89\t#: line/argument truncation widths -- short enough that `watch`'s table\n90\t#: stays legible without wrapping on an ordinary terminal.\n91\tWATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT = 5\n92\tSUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT = 100\n93\tSUMMARY_ARG_LIMIT = 60\n94\t#: How often the summary tailer companion process (spawned alongside the\n95\t#: engineer process, see _spawn_engineer) re-polls engineer.log for growth.\n96\tTAIL_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT = 1.0\n97\t\n98\tPHASE_RUNNING = \"running\"\n99\tPHASE_DONE = \"done\"\n100\tPHASE_FAILED = \"failed\"\n101\tPHASE_CANCELLED = \"cancelled\"\n102\tTERMINAL_PHASES = frozenset({PHASE_DONE, PHASE_FAILED, PHASE_CANCELLED})\n103\t\n104\t#: The fixed prompt handed to every engineer process, identical for every\n105\t#: movement -- never task-content-dependent (section 3.5 of the FROZEN\n106\t#: amendment: the approved task itself is never interpolated into an argv\n107\t#: element; the engineer reads it with its own Read tool).\n108\tENGINEER_PROMPT = (\n109\t    \"Read .nexus/approved_task.json in the current directory -- it is your \"\n110\t    \"SESSION_START for this movement, delivered verbatim by the orchestrator \"\n111\t    \"and content-hash-verified against the Product Owner's own relay entry. \"\n112\t    \"Immediately before opening your PR, re-read the canonical relay file \"\n113\t    \"(NEXUS_RELAY_FILE) and act on any RELAY_CORRECTION or RELAY_DECISION \"\n114\t    \"entries appended after dispatch. Proceed as the engineer role under \"\n115\t    \"AGENTS.md, AI_START_HERE.md, and CLAUDE.md exactly as an interactively \"\n116\t    \"started session would.\"\n117\t)\n118\t\n119\t\n120\tclass OrchestratorError(Exception):\n121\t    \"\"\"A CLI-level request could not be satisfied.\"\"\"\n122\t\n123\t\n124\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n125\t# Pure helpers (unit-testable without spawning anything)\n126\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n127\t\n128\tdef canonical_json(obj: Any) -> str:\n129\t    \"\"\"The exact serialization used both to hash the approved task and to\n130\t    write it to disk -- reusing local_relay.py's own `_dump` convention so\n131\t    the hash matches the bytes actually written, never a re-derived\n132\t    approximation of them.\"\"\"\n133\t    return json.dumps(obj, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n134\t\n135\t\n136\tdef task_hash(session_start_entry: dict) -> str:\n137\t    return hashlib.sha256(canonical_json(session_start_entry).encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n138\t\n139\t\n140\tdef validate_git_refs(base: str, lane: str) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n141\t    \"\"\"Mirrors, and does not relax, the two argument-shape restrictions\n142\t    GOV_PO_1_GATE_5 already puts on the PO role's own `git worktree add`:\n143\t    the base commit-ish must be an `origin/` ref, the branch must be a\n144\t    `feature/*` lane -- `gov/po-*` stays reserved for the PO's own\n145\t    governance branch.\"\"\"\n146\t    if not base or not base.startswith(\"origin/\"):\n147\t        return False, f\"report.git.base must start with 'origin/' (got {base!r})\"\n148\t    if not lane or not lane.startswith(\"feature/\"):\n149\t        return False, f\"report.git.lane must start with 'feature/' (got {lane!r})\"\n150\t    return True, \"ok\"\n151\t\n152\t\n153\tdef pid_alive(pid: int) -> bool:\n154\t    if not pid:\n155\t        return False\n156\t    try:\n157\t        os.kill(pid, 0)\n158\t    except ProcessLookupError:\n159\t        return False\n160\t    except PermissionError:\n161\t        return True  # exists, owned by someone else -- still alive\n162\t    except OSError:\n163\t        return False\n164\t    return True\n165\t\n166\t\n167\tdef decide_start(\n168\t    *, relay_obj: dict, existing_record: dict | None, is_pid_alive: bool,\n169\t    active_count: int, max_workers: int,\n170\t) -> tuple[str, str]:\n171\t    \"\"\"Pure dispatch decision. Returns (action, reason); action is one of\n172\t    \"dispatch\" (fresh worktree + spawn), \"resume\" (same worktree/branch/\n173\t    session, no new worktree), or \"refuse\".\"\"\"\n174\t    next_actor = relay_obj.get(\"next_actor\")\n175\t    if next_actor != \"engineer\":\n176\t        return \"refuse\", f\"not engineer's turn (next_actor is {next_actor!r})\"\n177\t\n178\t    if existing_record is not None and existing_record.get(\"phase\") not in TERMINAL_PHASES:\n179\t        if is_pid_alive:\n180\t            return \"refuse\", (\n181\t                f\"movement already running (pid {existing_record.get('pid')}, \"\n182\t                f\"phase {existing_record.get('phase')})\"\n183\t            )\n184\t        return \"resume\", \"recovering an interrupted run (same worktree, branch, and session)\"\n185\t\n186\t    # No record, or the prior run ended terminally: a fresh dispatch, which\n187\t    # needs a free worker slot. (A resume above is not a NEW slot -- it is\n188\t    # already occupying the one it was given originally.)\n189\t    if active_count >= max_workers:\n190\t        return \"refuse\", f\"max_workers ({max_workers}) reached; no free slot\"\n191\t    return \"dispatch\", \"fresh dispatch\"\n192\t\n193\t\n194\tdef decide_merge_lock_acquire(\n195\t    *, lock_record: dict | None, requester_movement: str, requester_pid: int,\n196\t    now: float, ttl: int, is_pid_alive=pid_alive,\n197\t) -> tuple[bool, dict | None, str]:\n198\t    \"\"\"Pure lock-acquisition decision (section 3.8 of the FROZEN amendment):\n199\t    a lock whose holder is dead or whose TTL elapsed is treated as\n200\t    abandoned and reclaimed, so a crash mid-merge cannot wedge every other\n201\t    movement's integration permanently.\"\"\"\n202\t    if lock_record is None:\n203\t        return True, {\"movement_id\": requester_movement, \"pid\": requester_pid, \"acquired_at\": now}, \"lock free\"\n204\t    if lock_record.get(\"movement_id\") == requester_movement:\n205\t        return True, {**lock_record, \"pid\": requester_pid, \"acquired_at\": now}, \"already held by this movement (re-entrant)\"\n206\t    holder_alive = is_pid_alive(lock_record.get(\"pid\"))\n207\t    stale = (now - lock_record.get(\"acquired_at\", 0)) > ttl\n208\t    if not holder_alive or stale:\n209\t        return True, {\"movement_id\": requester_movement, \"pid\": requester_pid, \"acquired_at\": now}, (\n210\t            \"reclaimed an abandoned/stale lock\"\n211\t        )\n212\t    return False, lock_record, f\"held by {lock_record.get('movement_id')} (pid {lock_record.get('pid')})\"\n213\t\n214\t\n215\tdef reconcile_phase(record: dict, is_pid_alive_now: bool, relay_status: str | None, retry_limit: int) -> str:\n216\t    \"\"\"Opportunistic phase reconciliation, run whenever `status`/`start`\n217\t    observes a record: never the sole source of truth (the relay file and a\n218\t    live PID check always are), just keeps the persisted `phase` field from\n219\t    silently lying to a human reading `status` output.\"\"\"\n220\t    phase = record.get(\"phase\", PHASE_RUNNING)\n221\t    if phase in TERMINAL_PHASES:\n222\t        return phase\n223\t    if relay_status == \"CLOSED\":\n224\t        return PHASE_DONE\n225\t    if not is_pid_alive_now and record.get(\"retry_count\", 0) >= retry_limit:\n226\t        return PHASE_FAILED\n227\t    return phase\n228\t\n229\t\n230\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n231\t# AC-2: stream-json engineer.log -> engineer.summary.log line parser\n232\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n233\t\n234\tdef _truncate(text: str, limit: int) -> str:\n235\t    \"\"\"Collapse internal whitespace (a stream-json line's own text/thinking\n236\t    fields are frequently multi-line) then hard-truncate -- never raise on\n237\t    an over-long field, one of AC-6's own required behaviors.\"\"\"\n238\t    collapsed = \" \".join(str(text).split())\n239\t    if len(collapsed) <= limit:\n240\t        return collapsed\n241\t    return collapsed[: max(limit - 1, 0)].rstrip() + \"\\u2026\"\n242\t\n243\t\n244\tdef _tool_arg_summary(tool_input: dict) -> str:\n245\t    \"\"\"The short argument summary half of AC-2's \"tool name + short argument\n246\t    summary\" -- prefers whichever field a human would actually want to see\n247\t    at a glance, falling back to the whole (truncated) input for a tool\n248\t    shape this list does not name explicitly.\"\"\"\n249\t    if not isinstance(tool_input, dict):\n250\t        return \"\"\n251\t    for key in (\"command\", \"file_path\", \"path\", \"pattern\", \"description\", \"prompt\", \"query\", \"url\"):\n252\t        value = tool_input.get(key)\n253\t        if isinstance(value, str) and value:\n254\t            return _truncate(value, SUMMARY_ARG_LIMIT)\n255\t    if tool_input:\n256\t        return _truncate(json.dumps(tool_input, sort_keys=True), SUMMARY_ARG_LIMIT)\n257\t    return \"\"\n258\t\n259\t\n260\tdef _tool_result_text(content: Any) -> str:\n261\t    if isinstance(content, str):\n262\t        return content\n263\t    if isinstance(content, list):\n264\t        parts = [c.get(\"text\", \"\") for c in content if isinstance(c, dict)]\n265\t        return \" \".join(p for p in parts if p)\n266\t    return json.dumps(content) if content is not None else \"\"\n267\t\n268\t\n269\tdef summarize_stream_json_line(raw_line: str) -> str | None:\n270\t    \"\"\"One raw `claude -p --output-format stream-json` line -> one short\n271\t    human-readable summary line, or `None` if the line should be skipped\n272\t    (blank, or invalid JSON). Invalid JSON is deliberately treated as \"not\n273\t    yet a complete line\" rather than an error: the tailer (`_drain_log_once`)\n274\t    re-reads from the same offset once more bytes are appended, so a line\n275\t    truncated mid-write at read time is silently retried, never dropped or\n276\t    crashed on (AC-6). A syntactically valid but unrecognized event shape\n277\t    still produces a line -- a truncated raw-JSON fallback -- because that\n278\t    case is a real event this parser simply does not know how to summarize\n279\t    yet, not an incomplete read (the risk this movement's own approved task\n280\t    calls out explicitly: never silently drop a real event).\"\"\"\n281\t    line = raw_line.strip()\n282\t    if not line:\n283\t        return None\n284\t    try:\n285\t        obj = json.loads(line)\n286\t    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n287\t        return None\n288\t    if not isinstance(obj, dict):\n289\t        return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n290\t\n291\t    kind = obj.get(\"type\")\n292\t    if kind == \"assistant\":\n293\t        blocks = ((obj.get(\"message\") or {}).get(\"content\")) or []\n294\t        parts = []\n295\t        for block in blocks:\n296\t            if not isinstance(block, dict):\n297\t                continue\n298\t            btype = block.get(\"type\")\n299\t            if btype == \"text\":\n300\t                parts.append(f\"assistant: {_truncate(block.get('text', ''), SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)}\")\n301\t            elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n302\t                name = block.get(\"name\", \"?\")\n303\t                arg = _tool_arg_summary(block.get(\"input\") or {})\n304\t                parts.append(f\"tool_use: {name} {arg}\".rstrip())\n305\t            elif btype == \"thinking\":\n306\t                parts.append(\"assistant: (thinking)\")\n307\t        if parts:\n308\t            return \" | \".join(parts)\n309\t        return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n310\t    if kind == \"user\":\n311\t        blocks = ((obj.get(\"message\") or {}).get(\"content\")) or []\n312\t        for block in blocks:\n313\t            if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_result\":\n314\t                status = \"error\" if block.get(\"is_error\") else \"ok\"\n315\t                text = _tool_result_text(block.get(\"content\"))\n316\t                return f\"tool_result ({status}): {_truncate(text, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)}\"\n317\t        return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n318\t    if kind == \"result\":\n319\t        subtype = obj.get(\"subtype\", \"?\")\n320\t        result = obj.get(\"result\")\n321\t        suffix = f\": {_truncate(result, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)}\" if isinstance(result, str) and result else \"\"\n322\t        return f\"result ({subtype}){suffix}\"\n323\t    if kind == \"system\":\n324\t        return f\"system: {obj.get('subtype', '?')}\"\n325\t    if kind == \"rate_limit_event\":\n326\t        status = (obj.get(\"rate_limit_info\") or {}).get(\"status\", \"?\")\n327\t        return f\"rate_limit: {status}\"\n328\t    # Recognized JSON, unrecognized shape -- fall back rather than drop it.\n329\t    return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n330\t\n331\t\n332\tdef _drain_log_once(log_path: Path, summary_fh, offset: int) -> int:\n333\t    \"\"\"Read whatever complete lines have been appended to `log_path` since\n334\t    byte `offset`, append their summaries to the already-open `summary_fh`,\n335\t    and return the new offset. A line with no trailing newline yet (the\n336\t    writer is mid-write) is left unconsumed -- the next call re-reads it\n337\t    once it is complete, per AC-6's truncated-last-line requirement. Binary\n338\t    mode throughout so the byte offset this function returns is always\n339\t    exactly re-seekable, regardless of any single line's own encoding.\"\"\"\n340\t    if not log_path.is_file():\n341\t        return offset\n342\t    with open(log_path, \"rb\") as log_fh:\n343\t        log_fh.seek(offset)\n344\t        data = log_fh.read()\n345\t    if not data:\n346\t        return offset\n347\t    pieces = data.split(b\"\\n\")\n348\t    complete = pieces[:-1]\n349\t    consumed = len(data) if data.endswith(b\"\\n\") else len(data) - len(pieces[-1])\n350\t    wrote = False\n351\t    for raw in complete:\n352\t        summary = summarize_stream_json_line(raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"))\n353\t        if summary is not None:\n354\t            summary_fh.write(summary + \"\\n\")\n355\t            wrote = True\n356\t    if wrote:\n357\t        summary_fh.flush()\n358\t    return offset + consumed\n359\t\n360\t\n361\tdef _tail_engineer_log(\n362\t    log_path: Path, summary_path: Path, pid: int, poll_interval: float = TAIL_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT,\n363\t) -> None:\n364\t    \"\"\"AC-2's companion process: `_spawn_engineer` returns immediately\n365\t    (section 3.4 of the FROZEN amendment), so nothing in the orchestrator's\n366\t    own `start` invocation lives long enough to keep tailing `engineer.log`\n367\t    -- this runs detached, independently of the parent that spawned it,\n368\t    for exactly as long as the engineer pid it was given stays alive (plus\n369\t    one final drain after it exits, to catch whatever was written between\n370\t    the last poll and process exit).\"\"\"\n371\t    summary_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n372\t    offset = 0\n373\t    with open(summary_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as summary_fh:\n374\t        while True:\n375\t            offset = _drain_log_once(log_path, summary_fh, offset)\n376\t            if not pid_alive(pid):\n377\t                offset = _drain_log_once(log_path, summary_fh, offset)\n378\t                return\n379\t            time.sleep(poll_interval)\n380\t\n381\t\n382\tdef _read_last_activity(worktree_path: str | None) -> str | None:\n383\t    \"\"\"AC-4/AC-5: the most recent non-blank `engineer.summary.log` line for\n384\t    a movement's worktree, or `None` -- never an exception -- when the\n385\t    worktree path is unknown, the file does not exist yet (a movement\n386\t    dispatched before this change, or one whose tailer has not written\n387\t    anything yet), or it is empty.\"\"\"\n388\t    if not worktree_path:\n389\t        return None\n390\t    summary_path = Path(worktree_path) / \".nexus\" / \"engineer.summary.log\"\n391\t    try:\n392\t        text = summary_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n393\t    except OSError:\n394\t        return None\n395\t    for line in reversed(text.splitlines()):\n396\t        if line.strip():\n397\t            return line.strip()\n398\t    return None\n399\t\n400\t\n401\tdef _heartbeat_age_seconds(record: dict, now: float | None = None) -> float | None:\n402\t    ts = record.get(\"heartbeat_at\")\n403\t    if not ts:\n404\t        return None\n405\t    try:\n406\t        started = datetime.strptime(ts, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc).timestamp()\n407\t    except ValueError:\n408\t        return None\n409\t    return (time.time() if now is None else now) - started\n410\t\n411\t\n412\tdef _format_age(seconds: float | None) -> str:\n413\t    if seconds is None or seconds < 0:\n414\t        return \"-\"\n415\t    total = int(seconds)\n416\t    if total < 60:\n417\t        return f\"{total}s\"\n418\t    minutes, secs = divmod(total, 60)\n419\t    if minutes < 60:\n420\t        return f\"{minutes}m{secs:02d}s\"\n421\t    hours, minutes = divmod(minutes, 60)\n422\t    return f\"{hours}h{minutes:02d}m\"\n423\t\n424\t\n425\tdef _truncate_to_width(text: str, width: int) -> str:\n426\t    if width <= 0 or len(text) <= width:\n427\t        return text\n428\t    return text[: max(width - 1, 0)] + \"\\u2026\"\n429\t\n430\t\n431\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n432\t# State-file IO (reuses local_relay.py's own atomic-write discipline)\n433\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n434\t\n435\tdef _state_path(state_dir: Path, movement_id: str) -> Path:\n436\t    return state_dir / f\"{movement_id}.json\"\n437\t\n438\t\n439\tdef _load_state(state_dir: Path, movement_id: str) -> dict | None:\n440\t    path = _state_path(state_dir, movement_id)\n441\t    if not path.is_file():\n442\t        return None\n443\t    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n444\t\n445\t\n446\tdef _save_state(state_dir: Path, movement_id: str, record: dict) -> None:\n447\t    lr._atomic_write(_state_path(state_dir, movement_id), lr._dump(record))\n448\t\n449\t\n450\tdef _list_state_records(state_dir: Path) -> list[dict]:\n451\t    if not state_dir.is_dir():\n452\t        return []\n453\t    records = []\n454\t    for path in sorted(state_dir.glob(\"NXS-LOCAL-*.json\")):\n455\t        try:\n456\t            records.append(json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")))\n457\t        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n458\t            continue\n459\t    return records\n460\t\n461\t\n462\tdef _active_count(state_dir: Path, exclude_movement: str | None = None) -> int:\n463\t    count = 0\n464\t    for record in _list_state_records(state_dir):\n465\t        if record.get(\"movement_id\") == exclude_movement:\n466\t            continue\n467\t        if record.get(\"phase\") not in TERMINAL_PHASES and pid_alive(record.get(\"pid\")):\n468\t            count += 1\n469\t    return count\n470\t\n471\t\n472\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n473\t# Relay file resolution\n474\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n475\t\n476\tdef _resolve_relay_file(relay_dir: Path, movement_id: str) -> Path:\n477\t    matches = sorted(relay_dir.glob(f\"{movement_id}-*.json\"))\n478\t    if not matches:\n479\t        raise OrchestratorError(f\"no relay file found for {movement_id} under {relay_dir}\")\n480\t    if len(matches) > 1:\n481\t        raise OrchestratorError(f\"more than one relay file matches {movement_id} under {relay_dir}: {matches}\")\n482\t    return matches[0]\n483\t\n484\t\n485\tdef _load_relay(relay_file: Path) -> dict:\n486\t    obj = json.loads(relay_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n487\t    errors = lr.validate_relay_object(obj)\n488\t    if errors:\n489\t        raise OrchestratorError(f\"{relay_file} fails validation: {'; '.join(errors)}\")\n490\t    return obj\n491\t\n492\t\n493\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n494\t# Git / subprocess side effects (argument lists only -- never shell text)\n495\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n496\t\n497\tdef _git_rev_parse(ref: str, cwd: Path) -> str:\n498\t    result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", ref], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)\n499\t    if result.returncode != 0:\n500\t        raise OrchestratorError(f\"git rev-parse {ref} failed: {result.stderr.strip()}\")\n501\t    return result.stdout.strip()\n502\t\n503\t\n504\tdef _git_worktree_add(worktree_path: Path, base: str, branch: str, cwd: Path) -> None:\n505\t    result = subprocess.run(\n506\t        # <path> <commit-ish> -b <branch> -- matches the exact order\n507\t        # GOV_PO_1_GATE_5 already validated for the PO role's own\n508\t        # `git worktree add` calls (nexus_po_tool_gate.py, tests/test_gov_po_role.py).\n509\t        [\"git\", \"worktree\", \"add\", str(worktree_path), base, \"-b\", branch],\n510\t        cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60,\n511\t    )\n512\t    if result.returncode != 0:\n513\t        raise OrchestratorError(f\"git worktree add failed: {result.stderr.strip()}\")\n514\t\n515\t\n516\tdef _git_worktree_remove(worktree_path: Path, cwd: Path) -> None:\n517\t    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"worktree\", \"remove\", str(worktree_path)], cwd=str(cwd),\n518\t                    capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)\n519\t\n520\t\n521\tdef _spawn_summary_tailer(log_path: Path, summary_path: Path, pid: int) -> None:\n522\t    \"\"\"AC-2: a second detached process, independent of both the engineer\n523\t    process and of `start`'s own (immediately-returning) invocation, that\n524\t    keeps `engineer.summary.log` growing for as long as the engineer pid it\n525\t    was given stays alive. Never awaited/joined -- `_tail-summary` is an\n526\t    internal subcommand, not part of the documented CLI surface.\"\"\"\n527\t    subprocess.Popen(\n528\t        [sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), \"_tail-summary\",\n529\t         \"--log\", str(log_path), \"--summary\", str(summary_path), \"--pid\", str(pid)],\n530\t        stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n531\t        start_new_session=True,\n532\t    )\n533\t\n534\t\n535\tdef _spawn_engineer(\n536\t    *, worktree_path: Path, profile_path: Path, canonical_relay_dir: Path,\n537\t    relay_file: Path, resume_session_id: str | None = None,\n538\t    max_budget_usd: float = DEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET_USD,\n539\t) -> subprocess.Popen:\n540\t    env = dict(os.environ)\n541\t    env[lr.ENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR] = str(canonical_relay_dir)\n542\t    env[lr.ENV_RELAY_FILE] = str(relay_file)\n543\t    # AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0015): with --permission-prompts none\n544\t    # there is no human to answer a Read/Edit/Write-tool permission prompt\n545\t    # for a path outside the worktree, so any such prompt is denied\n546\t    # automatically -- and, once denied, stays denied for the rest of the\n547\t    # session, no retries. A fresh dispatch only ever appeared to work\n548\t    # because the engineer session happened to reach the canonical relay\n549\t    # file through a Bash-invoked scripts/local_relay.py call, which this\n550\t    # per-tool directory allowlist does not gate; nothing guarantees an\n551\t    # engineer session -- fresh or resumed -- will choose Bash over its own\n552\t    # Read/Edit tools for a \"read the relay file\" instruction. --add-dir\n553\t    # pre-authorizes exactly the canonical relay directory for every tool,\n554\t    # identically for a fresh dispatch and a resume, so access no longer\n555\t    # depends on which tool the session happens to pick.\n556\t    # AC-1 (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0013): --output-format stream-json requires\n557\t    # --verbose alongside --print (confirmed against the installed claude\n558\t    # version's own --help/runtime error before writing this, per that\n559\t    # movement's own requirement) -- engineer.log now fills incrementally,\n560\t    # one JSON object per line, instead of only at process exit.\n561\t    argv = [\"claude\", \"-p\", ENGINEER_PROMPT, \"--settings\", str(profile_path),\n562\t            \"--add-dir\", str(canonical_relay_dir),\n563\t            \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--verbose\",\n564\t            \"--permission-prompts\", \"none\", \"--max-budget-usd\", str(max_budget_usd)]\n565\t    if resume_session_id:\n566\t        argv += [\"--resume\", resume_session_id]\n567\t    log_path = worktree_path / \".nexus\" / \"engineer.log\"\n568\t    log_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n569\t    log_fh = open(log_path, \"ab\")\n570\t    proc = subprocess.Popen(\n571\t        argv, cwd=str(worktree_path), env=env,\n572\t        stdout=log_fh, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n573\t        start_new_session=True,\n574\t    )\n575\t    summary_path = log_path.parent / \"engineer.summary.log\"\n576\t    _spawn_summary_tailer(log_path, summary_path, proc.pid)\n577\t    return proc\n578\t\n579\t\n580\tdef _kill_pid(pid: int, force: bool = False, grace_seconds: float = 5.0) -> None:\n581\t    if not pid_alive(pid):\n582\t        return\n583\t    try:\n584\t        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL if force else signal.SIGTERM)\n585\t    except OSError:\n586\t        return\n587\t    if force:\n588\t        return\n589\t    deadline = time.monotonic() + grace_seconds\n590\t    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\n591\t        if not pid_alive(pid):\n592\t            return\n593\t        time.sleep(0.2)\n594\t    try:\n595\t        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n596\t    except OSError:\n597\t        pass\n598\t\n599\t\n600\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n601\t# start\n602\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n603\t\n604\tdef _cmd_start(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n605\t    relay_dir = Path(args.relay_dir).resolve()\n606\t    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n607\t    worktrees_dir = Path(args.worktrees_dir)\n608\t    try:\n609\t        relay_file = _resolve_relay_file(relay_dir, args.movement)\n610\t        relay_obj = _load_relay(relay_file)\n611\t    except OrchestratorError as exc:\n612\t        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n613\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n614\t\n615\t    existing = _load_state(state_dir, args.movement)\n616\t    is_alive = pid_alive(existing.get(\"pid\")) if existing else False\n617\t    active = _active_count(state_dir, exclude_movement=args.movement)\n618\t    action, reason = decide_start(\n619\t        relay_obj=relay_obj, existing_record=existing, is_pid_alive=is_alive,\n620\t        active_count=active, max_workers=args.max_workers,\n621\t    )\n622\t    if action == \"refuse\":\n623\t        print(f\"error: {reason}\", file=sys.stderr)\n624\t        return EXIT_REFUSED\n625\t\n626\t    session_start = relay_obj[\"entries\"][0]\n627\t    report = session_start.get(\"report\", {})\n628\t    git_cfg = report.get(\"git\", {})\n629\t    base, lane = git_cfg.get(\"base\"), git_cfg.get(\"lane\")\n630\t    ok, ref_reason = validate_git_refs(base, lane)\n631\t    if not ok:\n632\t        print(f\"error: {ref_reason}\", file=sys.stderr)\n633\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n634\t\n635\t    hash_hex = task_hash(session_start)\n636\t\n637\t    if action == \"resume\":\n638\t        worktree_path = Path(existing[\"worktree_path\"])\n639\t        branch = existing[\"branch\"]\n640\t        base_sha = existing[\"base_sha\"]\n641\t        revision = existing[\"revision\"]\n642\t        session_id = existing.get(\"session_id\")\n643\t        proc = _spawn_engineer(\n644\t            worktree_path=worktree_path, profile_path=Path(args.profile),\n645\t            canonical_relay_dir=relay_dir, relay_file=relay_file,\n646\t            resume_session_id=session_id, max_budget_usd=args.max_budget_usd,\n647\t        )\n648\t        record = {**existing, \"pid\": proc.pid, \"phase\": PHASE_RUNNING,\n649\t                  \"last_action\": \"resumed\", \"task_hash\": hash_hex,\n650\t                  \"dispatch_seq\": len(relay_obj[\"entries\"])}\n651\t        _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, record)\n652\t        print(json.dumps({\"action\": \"resume\", \"movement_id\": args.movement, \"pid\": proc.pid,\n653\t                           \"worktree_path\": str(worktree_path), \"revision\": revision}))\n654\t        return EXIT_OK\n655\t\n656\t    # action == \"dispatch\"\n657\t    revision = 1 if existing is None else existing.get(\"revision\", 0) + 1\n658\t    worktree_path = worktrees_dir / args.movement\n659\t    if worktree_path.exists():\n660\t        print(f\"error: worktree path already exists: {worktree_path}\", file=sys.stderr)\n661\t        return EXIT_REFUSED\n662\t    try:\n663\t        base_sha = _git_rev_parse(base, relay_dir.parent)\n664\t        _git_worktree_add(worktree_path, base, lane, relay_dir.parent)\n665\t    except OrchestratorError as exc:\n666\t        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n667\t        return EXIT_REFUSED\n668\t\n669\t    nexus_dir = worktree_path / \".nexus\"\n670\t    nexus_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n671\t    (nexus_dir / \"approved_task.json\").write_text(canonical_json(session_start), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n672\t    (nexus_dir / \"movement_id.txt\").write_text(args.movement + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n673\t\n674\t    proc = _spawn_engineer(\n675\t        worktree_path=worktree_path, profile_path=Path(args.profile),\n676\t        canonical_relay_dir=relay_dir, relay_file=relay_file,\n677\t        max_budget_usd=args.max_budget_usd,\n678\t    )\n679\t    record = {\n680\t        \"movement_id\": args.movement, \"revision\": revision, \"base_sha\": base_sha,\n681\t        \"task_hash\": hash_hex, \"worktree_path\": str(worktree_path), \"branch\": lane,\n682\t        \"pid\": proc.pid, \"session_id\": None, \"phase\": PHASE_RUNNING,\n683\t        \"started_at\": lr._utc_now_iso(), \"heartbeat_at\": lr._utc_now_iso(),\n684\t        \"retry_count\": 0, \"last_error\": None, \"last_action\": \"dispatched\",\n685\t        \"dispatch_seq\": len(relay_obj[\"entries\"]),\n686\t    }\n687\t    _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, record)\n688\t    print(json.dumps({\"action\": \"dispatch\", \"movement_id\": args.movement, \"pid\": proc.pid,\n689\t                       \"worktree_path\": str(worktree_path), \"branch\": lane, \"revision\": revision}))\n690\t    return EXIT_OK\n691\t\n692\t\n693\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n694\t# status\n695\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n696\t\n697\tdef _status_row(record: dict, relay_dir: Path, retry_limit: int) -> dict:\n698\t    is_alive = pid_alive(record.get(\"pid\"))\n699\t    relay_status = None\n700\t    last_marker, last_timestamp = None, None\n701\t    try:\n702\t        relay_file = _resolve_relay_file(relay_dir, record[\"movement_id\"])\n703\t        relay_obj = _load_relay(relay_file)\n704\t        relay_status = relay_obj.get(\"status\")\n705\t        entries = relay_obj.get(\"entries\") or []\n706\t        dispatch_seq = record.get(\"dispatch_seq\")\n707\t        if dispatch_seq is not None and len(entries) > dispatch_seq:\n708\t            last_marker = \"REVISION_CHANGED_SINCE_DISPATCH\"\n709\t        if entries:\n710\t            last_marker = last_marker or entries[-1].get(\"marker\")\n711\t            last_timestamp = entries[-1].get(\"timestamp\")\n712\t    except OrchestratorError:\n713\t        pass\n714\t    phase = reconcile_phase(record, is_alive, relay_status, retry_limit)\n715\t    if phase != record.get(\"phase\"):\n716\t        record = {**record, \"phase\": phase}\n717\t    return {\n718\t        \"movement_id\": record[\"movement_id\"], \"phase\": phase, \"pid\": record.get(\"pid\"),\n719\t        \"pid_alive\": is_alive, \"revision\": record.get(\"revision\"), \"branch\": record.get(\"branch\"),\n720\t        \"worktree_path\": record.get(\"worktree_path\"), \"started_at\": record.get(\"started_at\"),\n721\t        \"retry_count\": record.get(\"retry_count\", 0), \"relay_status\": relay_status,\n722\t        \"last_marker\": last_marker, \"last_timestamp\": last_timestamp,\n723\t        # AC-4: the most recent engineer.summary.log line, or None -- never\n724\t        # an exception -- for a movement dispatched before AC-1/AC-2 landed\n725\t        # (AC-5's own backward-compatibility requirement).\n726\t        \"last_activity\": _read_last_activity(record.get(\"worktree_path\")),\n727\t        \"heartbeat_age_seconds\": _heartbeat_age_seconds(record),\n728\t    }\n729\t\n730\t\n731\tdef _cmd_status(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n732\t    relay_dir = Path(args.relay_dir).resolve()\n733\t    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n734\t    if args.movement:\n735\t        record = _load_state(state_dir, args.movement)\n736\t        if record is None:\n737\t            print(f\"error: no state record for {args.movement}\", file=sys.stderr)\n738\t            return EXIT_USAGE\n739\t        row = _status_row(record, relay_dir, args.retry_limit)\n740\t        _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, {**record, \"phase\": row[\"phase\"]})\n741\t        print(json.dumps(row, sort_keys=True))\n742\t        return EXIT_OK\n743\t\n744\t    rows = []\n745\t    for record in _list_state_records(state_dir):\n746\t        row = _status_row(record, relay_dir, args.retry_limit)\n747\t        _save_state(state_dir, record[\"movement_id\"], {**record, \"phase\": row[\"phase\"]})\n748\t        rows.append(row)\n749\t    print(json.dumps(sorted(rows, key=lambda r: r[\"movement_id\"]), sort_keys=True))\n750\t    return EXIT_OK\n751\t\n752\t\n753\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n754\t# stop\n755\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n756\t\n757\tdef _cmd_stop(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n758\t    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n759\t    record = _load_state(state_dir, args.movement)\n760\t    if record is None:\n761\t        print(f\"error: no state record for {args.movement}\", file=sys.stderr)\n762\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n763\t    _kill_pid(record.get(\"pid\"), force=args.force)\n764\t    record = {**record, \"phase\": PHASE_CANCELLED, \"last_action\": \"stopped\"}\n765\t    _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, record)\n766\t    print(json.dumps({\"movement_id\": args.movement, \"phase\": PHASE_CANCELLED}))\n767\t    return EXIT_OK\n768\t\n769\t\n770\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n771\t# merge-lock\n772\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n773\t\n774\tdef _lock_path(state_dir: Path) -> Path:\n775\t    return state_dir / \"merge.lock.json\"\n776\t\n777\t\n778\tdef _cmd_merge_lock(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n779\t    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n780\t    state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n781\t    path = _lock_path(state_dir)\n782\t    with lr._FileLock(path, timeout=args.wait):\n783\t        if args.action == \"release\":\n784\t            if path.is_file():\n785\t                record = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n786\t                if record.get(\"movement_id\") == args.movement:\n787\t                    path.unlink()\n788\t                    print(json.dumps({\"released\": True}))\n789\t                    return EXIT_OK\n790\t            print(json.dumps({\"released\": False, \"reason\": \"not held by this movement\"}))\n791\t            return EXIT_REFUSED\n792\t\n793\t        lock_record = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if path.is_file() else None\n794\t        granted, new_record, reason = decide_merge_lock_acquire(\n795\t            lock_record=lock_record, requester_movement=args.movement,\n796\t            requester_pid=args.pid, now=time.time(), ttl=args.ttl,\n797\t        )\n798\t        if granted:\n799\t            lr._atomic_write(path, json.dumps(new_record, sort_keys=True, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n800\t            print(json.dumps({\"acquired\": True, \"reason\": reason}))\n801\t            return EXIT_OK\n802\t        print(json.dumps({\"acquired\": False, \"reason\": reason}))\n803\t        return EXIT_REFUSED\n804\t\n805\t\n806\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n807\t# _tail-summary (internal -- spawned by _spawn_engineer, not user-facing)\n808\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n809\t\n810\tdef _cmd_tail_summary(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n811\t    _tail_engineer_log(Path(args.log), Path(args.summary), args.pid, poll_interval=args.poll_interval)\n812\t    return EXIT_OK\n813\t\n814\t\n815\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n816\t# watch (AC-3)\n817\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n818\t\n819\tdef _gather_watch_rows(state_dir: Path, relay_dir: Path, retry_limit: int) -> list[dict]:\n820\t    \"\"\"The exact per-movement rows `status` computes, reused verbatim (AC-3:\n821\t    \"polls the same data orchestrator status already computes\") -- but\n822\t    never written back to `state_dir`, unlike `_cmd_status`'s own\n823\t    reconciliation write. `watch` is read-only by its own explicit\n824\t    invariant; `status` is not.\"\"\"\n825\t    rows = [_status_row(record, relay_dir, retry_limit) for record in _list_state_records(state_dir)]\n826\t    return sorted(rows, key=lambda r: r[\"movement_id\"])\n827\t\n828\t\n829\tdef _render_watch_screen(rows: list[dict], terminal_width: int = 80) -> str:\n830\t    lines = [f\"neXus orchestrator watch -- {len(rows)} known movement(s)\"]\n831\t    if not rows:\n832\t        lines.append(\"(no movements known)\")\n833\t        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n834\t    header = f\"{'MOVEMENT':<22}{'PHASE':<12}{'ALIVE':<7}{'AGE':<8}{'BRANCH':<26}{'LAST RELAY'}\"\n835\t    lines.append(_truncate_to_width(header, terminal_width))\n836\t    lines.append(\"-\" * min(len(header), terminal_width if terminal_width > 0 else len(header)))\n837\t    for row in rows:\n838\t        alive = \"yes\" if row.get(\"pid_alive\") else \"no\"\n839\t        age = _format_age(row.get(\"heartbeat_age_seconds\"))\n840\t        branch = row.get(\"branch\") or \"-\"\n841\t        last_relay = f\"{row.get('last_marker') or '-'}@{row.get('last_timestamp') or '-'}\"\n842\t        main_line = (\n843\t            f\"{row['movement_id']:<22}{(row.get('phase') or '-'):<12}{alive:<7}{age:<8}{branch:<26}{last_relay}\"\n844\t        )\n845\t        lines.append(_truncate_to_width(main_line, terminal_width))\n846\t        worktree = row.get(\"worktree_path\") or \"-\"\n847\t        lines.append(_truncate_to_width(f\"  worktree: {worktree}\", terminal_width))\n848\t        # AC-4/AC-5: last_activity is None for a movement dispatched before\n849\t        # AC-1/AC-2 landed (old-format engineer.log, no summary.log yet) --\n850\t        # render as \"n/a\", never raise.\n851\t        activity = row.get(\"last_activity\") or \"n/a\"\n852\t        lines.append(_truncate_to_width(f\"  last activity: {activity}\", terminal_width))\n853\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n854\t\n855\t\n856\tdef _cmd_watch(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n857\t    \"\"\"Human-facing dashboard loop. Deliberately distinct from\n858\t    `local_relay.py watch`'s own bounded, single-wait design: that command\n859\t    is an unattended primitive a script polls once for one specific\n860\t    next_actor flip, with a hard timeout ceiling so it can never become a\n861\t    silent daemon. This command is the opposite kind of tool -- a live\n862\t    display a human keeps open and reads continuously -- so it loops until\n863\t    the human interrupts it (Ctrl-C) rather than returning after one\n864\t    bounded wait; that is a real design difference, not an oversight.\n865\t    Read-only throughout: every call below is a read (`_gather_watch_rows`\n866\t    never calls `_save_state`), and it mutates no on-disk state.\"\"\"\n867\t    relay_dir = Path(args.relay_dir).resolve()\n868\t    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n869\t    try:\n870\t        while True:\n871\t            rows = _gather_watch_rows(state_dir, relay_dir, args.retry_limit)\n872\t            width = shutil.get_terminal_size(fallback=(100, 24)).columns\n873\t            os.system(\"cls\" if os.name == \"nt\" else \"clear\")\n874\t            print(_render_watch_screen(rows, width))\n875\t            time.sleep(args.interval)\n876\t    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n877\t        return EXIT_OK\n878\t\n879\t\n880\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n881\t# CLI\n882\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n883\t\n884\tdef _add_common(parser: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\n885\t    parser.add_argument(\"--relay-dir\", default=\"relay\")\n886\t    parser.add_argument(\"--state-dir\", default=str(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR))\n887\t\n888\t\n889\tdef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n890\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"orchestrator\", description=__doc__)\n891\t    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n892\t\n893\t    p_start = sub.add_parser(\"start\", help=\"dispatch (or resume) one approved movement\")\n894\t    p_start.add_argument(\"--movement\", required=True)\n895\t    _add_common(p_start)\n896\t    p_start.add_argument(\"--worktrees-dir\", default=str(DEFAULT_WORKTREES_DIR))\n897\t    p_start.add_argument(\"--profile\", default=str(DEFAULT_ENGINEER_PROFILE))\n898\t    p_start.add_argument(\"--max-workers\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MAX_WORKERS)\n899\t    p_start.add_argument(\"--max-budget-usd\", type=float, default=DEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET_USD)\n900\t    p_start.set_defaults(func=_cmd_start)\n901\t\n902\t    p_status = sub.add_parser(\"status\", help=\"report one movement, or every known movement\")\n903\t    p_status.add_argument(\"--movement\", default=None)\n904\t    _add_common(p_status)\n905\t    p_status.add_argument(\"--retry-limit\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RETRY_LIMIT)\n906\t    p_status.set_defaults(func=_cmd_status)\n907\t\n908\t    p_stop = sub.add_parser(\"stop\", help=\"cancel one movement's engineer process\")\n909\t    p_stop.add_argument(\"--movement\", required=True)\n910\t    _add_common(p_stop)\n911\t    p_stop.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"SIGKILL immediately, skip the SIGTERM grace period\")\n912\t    p_stop.set_defaults(func=_cmd_stop)\n913\t\n914\t    p_lock = sub.add_parser(\"merge-lock\", help=\"acquire/release the cross-movement merge-serialization lock\")\n915\t    p_lock.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"acquire\", \"release\"))\n916\t    p_lock.add_argument(\"--movement\", required=True)\n917\t    p_lock.add_argument(\"--pid\", type=int, default=os.getpid())\n918\t    p_lock.add_argument(\"--ttl\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MERGE_LOCK_TTL)\n919\t    p_lock.add_argument(\"--wait\", type=float, default=30.0)\n920\t    p_lock.add_argument(\"--state-dir\", default=str(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR))\n921\t    p_lock.set_defaults(func=_cmd_merge_lock)\n922\t\n923\t    p_watch = sub.add_parser(\n924\t        \"watch\", help=\"read-only terminal dashboard: phase, liveness, and last activity for every movement\"\n925\t    )\n926\t    _add_common(p_watch)\n927\t    p_watch.add_argument(\"--interval\", type=int, default=WATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT)\n928\t    p_watch.add_argument(\"--retry-limit\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RETRY_LIMIT)\n929\t    p_watch.set_defaults(func=_cmd_watch)\n930\t\n931\t    # Internal only -- spawned by _spawn_engineer, never invoked directly by\n932\t    # a human or documented in this module's own CLI docstring.\n933\t    p_tail = sub.add_parser(\"_tail-summary\")\n934\t    p_tail.add_argument(\"--log\", required=True)\n935\t    p_tail.add_argument(\"--summary\", required=True)\n936\t    p_tail.add_argument(\"--pid\", type=int, required=True)\n937\t    p_tail.add_argument(\"--poll-interval\", type=float, default=TAIL_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT)\n938\t    p_tail.set_defaults(func=_cmd_tail_summary)\n939\t\n940\t    return parser\n941\t\n942\t\n943\tdef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n944\t    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)\n945\t    return args.func(args)\n946\t\n947\t\n948\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n949\t    sys.exit(main())\n950\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02bbb3c2-9ec8-432c-ae72-fb22e59d93cf","uuid":"5c935097-29d4-410f-b3b6-d69095d187f6","timestamp":"2026-09-08T16:42:10.918Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/OzanDur/Codo/neXus-nexus-worktrees/NXS-LOCAL-0021/scripts/orchestrator.py","content":"\"\"\"GOV.PO.3 -- deterministic local orchestration of an approved movement\n(docs/design/GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md, FROZEN).\n\n    py scripts/orchestrator.py start      --movement <relay-id> [options]\n    py scripts/orchestrator.py status     [--movement <relay-id>] [options]\n    py scripts/orchestrator.py stop       --movement <relay-id> [--force] [options]\n    py scripts/orchestrator.py merge-lock {acquire|release} --movement <relay-id> [options]\n    py scripts/orchestrator.py watch      [--interval SECONDS] [options]\n\n`<relay-id>` is the relay file's own id (`NXS-LOCAL-NNNN`), unambiguous and\nresolvable to exactly one file (`relay/<relay-id>-*.json`).\n\n`start` reads the movement's already-approved `SESSION_START` (`entries[0]`\nof its canonical relay file), computes its SHA-256 content hash, creates one\ngit worktree from the packet's own `report.git.base`/`report.git.lane`\nfields, writes the canonical bytes to `.nexus/approved_task.json` inside\nthat worktree, and spawns a detached `claude -p` engineer process there\nusing the engineer permission profile\n(`.claude/nexus-engineer.settings.json`) -- then returns immediately. It\ndoes not review, decide, or merge anything; merge authority stays with the\nengineer's own session under the standing authorization\n(`ozandurmus/nexus-agent-relay#13`). `merge-lock` is the cross-movement\nserialization primitive that profile's `PreToolUse` hook\n(`scripts/nexus_engineer_tool_gate.py`) calls before a `gh pr merge`.\n\nEvery subprocess this module spawns is built as an argument list\n(`subprocess.run`/`Popen` with the default `shell=False`), never a\nformatted/interpolated shell string -- the approved-task content itself is\nnever placed in an argv element; it is written to a file the engineer\nprocess reads with its own `Read` tool (section 3.2/3.5 of the FROZEN\namendment).\n\nProcess records are persistent but outside the relay file (one JSON file\nper movement under `NEXUS_ORCHESTRATOR_STATE_DIR`, default a fixed\nsubdirectory of the system temp root -- runtime bookkeeping, not durable\ngovernance history). Liveness is always checked live (`os.kill(pid, 0)`),\nnever inferred from a stale timestamp: this is stricter and simpler than a\nstaleness-threshold heuristic and removes any dependency on clock skew.\n\nOffline except for the subprocesses it spawns (`git`, `claude`, `gh`\nindirectly via the engineer session). No device, credential, or vendor\ncollector access; stdlib only.\n\nExit codes: 0 success, 1 invalid/refused (wrong turn, duplicate start, no\nfree worker slot, lock held by another movement), 2 usage error (bad\narguments, missing/invalid relay file).\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO_ROOT / \"scripts\"))\nimport local_relay as lr  # noqa: E402\n\nEXIT_OK, EXIT_REFUSED, EXIT_USAGE = 0, 1, 2\n\n#: Runtime bookkeeping lives outside the repository, mirroring\n#: nexus_po_tool_gate.py's NEXUS_PO_HOOK_LOG precedent -- process records\n#: are not durable governance history and must not spam the git-tracked\n#: relay file with per-invocation diffs.\nDEFAULT_STATE_DIR = Path(\n    os.environ.get(\"NEXUS_ORCHESTRATOR_STATE_DIR\")\n    or os.path.join(tempfile.gettempdir(), \"nexus_orchestrator\")\n)\nDEFAULT_WORKTREES_DIR = REPO_ROOT.parent / f\"{REPO_ROOT.name}-nexus-worktrees\"\nDEFAULT_MAX_WORKERS = 3\nDEFAULT_RETRY_LIMIT = 2\nDEFAULT_MERGE_LOCK_TTL = 600\nDEFAULT_ENGINEER_PROFILE = REPO_ROOT / \".claude\" / \"nexus-engineer.settings.json\"\n#: An unattended spawn has no human watching live spend; bound it. Not part\n#: of the FROZEN amendment's own text -- a safety addition made before the\n#: first real dispatch, named as such in this movement's own evidence.\nDEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET_USD = 3.0\n\n#: AC-3's dashboard default poll interval, and AC-2's engineer-log summary\n#: line/argument truncation widths -- short enough that `watch`'s table\n#: stays legible without wrapping on an ordinary terminal.\nWATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT = 5\nSUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT = 100\nSUMMARY_ARG_LIMIT = 60\n#: How often the summary tailer companion process (spawned alongside the\n#: engineer process, see _spawn_engineer) re-polls engineer.log for growth.\nTAIL_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT = 1.0\n\nPHASE_RUNNING = \"running\"\nPHASE_DONE = \"done\"\nPHASE_FAILED = \"failed\"\nPHASE_CANCELLED = \"cancelled\"\nTERMINAL_PHASES = frozenset({PHASE_DONE, PHASE_FAILED, PHASE_CANCELLED})\n\n#: The fixed prompt handed to every engineer process, identical for every\n#: movement -- never task-content-dependent (section 3.5 of the FROZEN\n#: amendment: the approved task itself is never interpolated into an argv\n#: element; the engineer reads it with its own Read tool).\nENGINEER_PROMPT = (\n    \"Read .nexus/approved_task.json in the current directory -- it is your \"\n    \"SESSION_START for this movement, delivered verbatim by the orchestrator \"\n    \"and content-hash-verified against the Product Owner's own relay entry. \"\n    \"Immediately before opening your PR, re-read the canonical relay file \"\n    \"(NEXUS_RELAY_FILE) and act on any RELAY_CORRECTION or RELAY_DECISION \"\n    \"entries appended after dispatch. Proceed as the engineer role under \"\n    \"AGENTS.md, AI_START_HERE.md, and CLAUDE.md exactly as an interactively \"\n    \"started session would.\"\n)\n\n\nclass OrchestratorError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"A CLI-level request could not be satisfied.\"\"\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Pure helpers (unit-testable without spawning anything)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef canonical_json(obj: Any) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The exact serialization used both to hash the approved task and to\n    write it to disk -- reusing local_relay.py's own `_dump` convention so\n    the hash matches the bytes actually written, never a re-derived\n    approximation of them.\"\"\"\n    return json.dumps(obj, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef task_hash(session_start_entry: dict) -> str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(canonical_json(session_start_entry).encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef validate_git_refs(base: str, lane: str) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n    \"\"\"Mirrors, and does not relax, the two argument-shape restrictions\n    GOV_PO_1_GATE_5 already puts on the PO role's own `git worktree add`:\n    the base commit-ish must be an `origin/` ref, the branch must be a\n    `feature/*` lane -- `gov/po-*` stays reserved for the PO's own\n    governance branch.\"\"\"\n    if not base or not base.startswith(\"origin/\"):\n        return False, f\"report.git.base must start with 'origin/' (got {base!r})\"\n    if not lane or not lane.startswith(\"feature/\"):\n        return False, f\"report.git.lane must start with 'feature/' (got {lane!r})\"\n    return True, \"ok\"\n\n\ndef pid_alive(pid: int) -> bool:\n    if not pid:\n        return False\n    try:\n        os.kill(pid, 0)\n    except ProcessLookupError:\n        return False\n    except PermissionError:\n        return True  # exists, owned by someone else -- still alive\n    except OSError:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n\ndef decide_start(\n    *, relay_obj: dict, existing_record: dict | None, is_pid_alive: bool,\n    active_count: int, max_workers: int,\n) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"Pure dispatch decision. Returns (action, reason); action is one of\n    \"dispatch\" (fresh worktree + spawn), \"resume\" (same worktree/branch/\n    session, no new worktree), or \"refuse\".\"\"\"\n    next_actor = relay_obj.get(\"next_actor\")\n    if next_actor != \"engineer\":\n        return \"refuse\", f\"not engineer's turn (next_actor is {next_actor!r})\"\n\n    if existing_record is not None and existing_record.get(\"phase\") not in TERMINAL_PHASES:\n        if is_pid_alive:\n            return \"refuse\", (\n                f\"movement already running (pid {existing_record.get('pid')}, \"\n                f\"phase {existing_record.get('phase')})\"\n            )\n        return \"resume\", \"recovering an interrupted run (same worktree, branch, and session)\"\n\n    # No record, or the prior run ended terminally: a fresh dispatch, which\n    # needs a free worker slot. (A resume above is not a NEW slot -- it is\n    # already occupying the one it was given originally.)\n    if active_count >= max_workers:\n        return \"refuse\", f\"max_workers ({max_workers}) reached; no free slot\"\n    return \"dispatch\", \"fresh dispatch\"\n\n\ndef decide_merge_lock_acquire(\n    *, lock_record: dict | None, requester_movement: str, requester_pid: int,\n    now: float, ttl: int, is_pid_alive=pid_alive,\n) -> tuple[bool, dict | None, str]:\n    \"\"\"Pure lock-acquisition decision (section 3.8 of the FROZEN amendment):\n    a lock whose holder is dead or whose TTL elapsed is treated as\n    abandoned and reclaimed, so a crash mid-merge cannot wedge every other\n    movement's integration permanently.\"\"\"\n    if lock_record is None:\n        return True, {\"movement_id\": requester_movement, \"pid\": requester_pid, \"acquired_at\": now}, \"lock free\"\n    if lock_record.get(\"movement_id\") == requester_movement:\n        return True, {**lock_record, \"pid\": requester_pid, \"acquired_at\": now}, \"already held by this movement (re-entrant)\"\n    holder_alive = is_pid_alive(lock_record.get(\"pid\"))\n    stale = (now - lock_record.get(\"acquired_at\", 0)) > ttl\n    if not holder_alive or stale:\n        return True, {\"movement_id\": requester_movement, \"pid\": requester_pid, \"acquired_at\": now}, (\n            \"reclaimed an abandoned/stale lock\"\n        )\n    return False, lock_record, f\"held by {lock_record.get('movement_id')} (pid {lock_record.get('pid')})\"\n\n\ndef reconcile_phase(record: dict, is_pid_alive_now: bool, relay_status: str | None, retry_limit: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Opportunistic phase reconciliation, run whenever `status`/`start`\n    observes a record: never the sole source of truth (the relay file and a\n    live PID check always are), just keeps the persisted `phase` field from\n    silently lying to a human reading `status` output.\"\"\"\n    phase = record.get(\"phase\", PHASE_RUNNING)\n    if phase in TERMINAL_PHASES:\n        return phase\n    if relay_status == \"CLOSED\":\n        return PHASE_DONE\n    if not is_pid_alive_now and record.get(\"retry_count\", 0) >= retry_limit:\n        return PHASE_FAILED\n    return phase\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# AC-2: stream-json engineer.log -> engineer.summary.log line parser\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _truncate(text: str, limit: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Collapse internal whitespace (a stream-json line's own text/thinking\n    fields are frequently multi-line) then hard-truncate -- never raise on\n    an over-long field, one of AC-6's own required behaviors.\"\"\"\n    collapsed = \" \".join(str(text).split())\n    if len(collapsed) <= limit:\n        return collapsed\n    return collapsed[: max(limit - 1, 0)].rstrip() + \"\\u2026\"\n\n\ndef _tool_arg_summary(tool_input: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The short argument summary half of AC-2's \"tool name + short argument\n    summary\" -- prefers whichever field a human would actually want to see\n    at a glance, falling back to the whole (truncated) input for a tool\n    shape this list does not name explicitly.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tool_input, dict):\n        return \"\"\n    for key in (\"command\", \"file_path\", \"path\", \"pattern\", \"description\", \"prompt\", \"query\", \"url\"):\n        value = tool_input.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value:\n            return _truncate(value, SUMMARY_ARG_LIMIT)\n    if tool_input:\n        return _truncate(json.dumps(tool_input, sort_keys=True), SUMMARY_ARG_LIMIT)\n    return \"\"\n\n\ndef _tool_result_text(content: Any) -> str:\n    if isinstance(content, str):\n        return content\n    if isinstance(content, list):\n        parts = [c.get(\"text\", \"\") for c in content if isinstance(c, dict)]\n        return \" \".join(p for p in parts if p)\n    return json.dumps(content) if content is not None else \"\"\n\n\ndef summarize_stream_json_line(raw_line: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"One raw `claude -p --output-format stream-json` line -> one short\n    human-readable summary line, or `None` if the line should be skipped\n    (blank, or invalid JSON). Invalid JSON is deliberately treated as \"not\n    yet a complete line\" rather than an error: the tailer (`_drain_log_once`)\n    re-reads from the same offset once more bytes are appended, so a line\n    truncated mid-write at read time is silently retried, never dropped or\n    crashed on (AC-6). A syntactically valid but unrecognized event shape\n    still produces a line -- a truncated raw-JSON fallback -- because that\n    case is a real event this parser simply does not know how to summarize\n    yet, not an incomplete read (the risk this movement's own approved task\n    calls out explicitly: never silently drop a real event).\"\"\"\n    line = raw_line.strip()\n    if not line:\n        return None\n    try:\n        obj = json.loads(line)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return None\n    if not isinstance(obj, dict):\n        return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n\n    kind = obj.get(\"type\")\n    if kind == \"assistant\":\n        blocks = ((obj.get(\"message\") or {}).get(\"content\")) or []\n        parts = []\n        for block in blocks:\n            if not isinstance(block, dict):\n                continue\n            btype = block.get(\"type\")\n            if btype == \"text\":\n                parts.append(f\"assistant: {_truncate(block.get('text', ''), SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)}\")\n            elif btype == \"tool_use\":\n                name = block.get(\"name\", \"?\")\n                arg = _tool_arg_summary(block.get(\"input\") or {})\n                parts.append(f\"tool_use: {name} {arg}\".rstrip())\n            elif btype == \"thinking\":\n                parts.append(\"assistant: (thinking)\")\n        if parts:\n            return \" | \".join(parts)\n        return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n    if kind == \"user\":\n        blocks = ((obj.get(\"message\") or {}).get(\"content\")) or []\n        for block in blocks:\n            if isinstance(block, dict) and block.get(\"type\") == \"tool_result\":\n                status = \"error\" if block.get(\"is_error\") else \"ok\"\n                text = _tool_result_text(block.get(\"content\"))\n                return f\"tool_result ({status}): {_truncate(text, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)}\"\n        return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n    if kind == \"result\":\n        subtype = obj.get(\"subtype\", \"?\")\n        result = obj.get(\"result\")\n        suffix = f\": {_truncate(result, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)}\" if isinstance(result, str) and result else \"\"\n        return f\"result ({subtype}){suffix}\"\n    if kind == \"system\":\n        return f\"system: {obj.get('subtype', '?')}\"\n    if kind == \"rate_limit_event\":\n        status = (obj.get(\"rate_limit_info\") or {}).get(\"status\", \"?\")\n        return f\"rate_limit: {status}\"\n    # Recognized JSON, unrecognized shape -- fall back rather than drop it.\n    return _truncate(line, SUMMARY_TEXT_LIMIT)\n\n\ndef _drain_log_once(log_path: Path, summary_fh, offset: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Read whatever complete lines have been appended to `log_path` since\n    byte `offset`, append their summaries to the already-open `summary_fh`,\n    and return the new offset. A line with no trailing newline yet (the\n    writer is mid-write) is left unconsumed -- the next call re-reads it\n    once it is complete, per AC-6's truncated-last-line requirement. Binary\n    mode throughout so the byte offset this function returns is always\n    exactly re-seekable, regardless of any single line's own encoding.\"\"\"\n    if not log_path.is_file():\n        return offset\n    with open(log_path, \"rb\") as log_fh:\n        log_fh.seek(offset)\n        data = log_fh.read()\n    if not data:\n        return offset\n    pieces = data.split(b\"\\n\")\n    complete = pieces[:-1]\n    consumed = len(data) if data.endswith(b\"\\n\") else len(data) - len(pieces[-1])\n    wrote = False\n    for raw in complete:\n        summary = summarize_stream_json_line(raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\"))\n        if summary is not None:\n            summary_fh.write(summary + \"\\n\")\n            wrote = True\n    if wrote:\n        summary_fh.flush()\n    return offset + consumed\n\n\ndef _tail_engineer_log(\n    log_path: Path, summary_path: Path, pid: int, poll_interval: float = TAIL_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"AC-2's companion process: `_spawn_engineer` returns immediately\n    (section 3.4 of the FROZEN amendment), so nothing in the orchestrator's\n    own `start` invocation lives long enough to keep tailing `engineer.log`\n    -- this runs detached, independently of the parent that spawned it,\n    for exactly as long as the engineer pid it was given stays alive (plus\n    one final drain after it exits, to catch whatever was written between\n    the last poll and process exit).\"\"\"\n    summary_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    offset = 0\n    with open(summary_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as summary_fh:\n        while True:\n            offset = _drain_log_once(log_path, summary_fh, offset)\n            if not pid_alive(pid):\n                offset = _drain_log_once(log_path, summary_fh, offset)\n                return\n            time.sleep(poll_interval)\n\n\ndef _read_last_activity(worktree_path: str | None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"AC-4/AC-5: the most recent non-blank `engineer.summary.log` line for\n    a movement's worktree, or `None` -- never an exception -- when the\n    worktree path is unknown, the file does not exist yet (a movement\n    dispatched before this change, or one whose tailer has not written\n    anything yet), or it is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not worktree_path:\n        return None\n    summary_path = Path(worktree_path) / \".nexus\" / \"engineer.summary.log\"\n    try:\n        text = summary_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n    for line in reversed(text.splitlines()):\n        if line.strip():\n            return line.strip()\n    return None\n\n\ndef _heartbeat_age_seconds(record: dict, now: float | None = None) -> float | None:\n    ts = record.get(\"heartbeat_at\")\n    if not ts:\n        return None\n    try:\n        started = datetime.strptime(ts, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\").replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc).timestamp()\n    except ValueError:\n        return None\n    return (time.time() if now is None else now) - started\n\n\ndef _format_age(seconds: float | None) -> str:\n    if seconds is None or seconds < 0:\n        return \"-\"\n    total = int(seconds)\n    if total < 60:\n        return f\"{total}s\"\n    minutes, secs = divmod(total, 60)\n    if minutes < 60:\n        return f\"{minutes}m{secs:02d}s\"\n    hours, minutes = divmod(minutes, 60)\n    return f\"{hours}h{minutes:02d}m\"\n\n\ndef _truncate_to_width(text: str, width: int) -> str:\n    if width <= 0 or len(text) <= width:\n        return text\n    return text[: max(width - 1, 0)] + \"\\u2026\"\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# State-file IO (reuses local_relay.py's own atomic-write discipline)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _state_path(state_dir: Path, movement_id: str) -> Path:\n    return state_dir / f\"{movement_id}.json\"\n\n\ndef _load_state(state_dir: Path, movement_id: str) -> dict | None:\n    path = _state_path(state_dir, movement_id)\n    if not path.is_file():\n        return None\n    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef _save_state(state_dir: Path, movement_id: str, record: dict) -> None:\n    lr._atomic_write(_state_path(state_dir, movement_id), lr._dump(record))\n\n\ndef _list_state_records(state_dir: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    if not state_dir.is_dir():\n        return []\n    records = []\n    for path in sorted(state_dir.glob(\"NXS-LOCAL-*.json\")):\n        try:\n            records.append(json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")))\n        except (OSError, json.JSONDecodeError):\n            continue\n    return records\n\n\ndef _active_count(state_dir: Path, exclude_movement: str | None = None) -> int:\n    count = 0\n    for record in _list_state_records(state_dir):\n        if record.get(\"movement_id\") == exclude_movement:\n            continue\n        if record.get(\"phase\") not in TERMINAL_PHASES and pid_alive(record.get(\"pid\")):\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Relay file resolution\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _resolve_relay_file(relay_dir: Path, movement_id: str) -> Path:\n    matches = sorted(relay_dir.glob(f\"{movement_id}-*.json\"))\n    if not matches:\n        raise OrchestratorError(f\"no relay file found for {movement_id} under {relay_dir}\")\n    if len(matches) > 1:\n        raise OrchestratorError(f\"more than one relay file matches {movement_id} under {relay_dir}: {matches}\")\n    return matches[0]\n\n\ndef _load_relay(relay_file: Path) -> dict:\n    obj = json.loads(relay_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    errors = lr.validate_relay_object(obj)\n    if errors:\n        raise OrchestratorError(f\"{relay_file} fails validation: {'; '.join(errors)}\")\n    return obj\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Git / subprocess side effects (argument lists only -- never shell text)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _git_rev_parse(ref: str, cwd: Path) -> str:\n    result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", ref], cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        raise OrchestratorError(f\"git rev-parse {ref} failed: {result.stderr.strip()}\")\n    return result.stdout.strip()\n\n\ndef _git_worktree_add(worktree_path: Path, base: str, branch: str, cwd: Path) -> None:\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        # <path> <commit-ish> -b <branch> -- matches the exact order\n        # GOV_PO_1_GATE_5 already validated for the PO role's own\n        # `git worktree add` calls (nexus_po_tool_gate.py, tests/test_gov_po_role.py).\n        [\"git\", \"worktree\", \"add\", str(worktree_path), base, \"-b\", branch],\n        cwd=str(cwd), capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60,\n    )\n    if result.returncode != 0:\n        raise OrchestratorError(f\"git worktree add failed: {result.stderr.strip()}\")\n\n\ndef _git_worktree_remove(worktree_path: Path, cwd: Path) -> None:\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"worktree\", \"remove\", str(worktree_path)], cwd=str(cwd),\n                    capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)\n\n\ndef _spawn_summary_tailer(log_path: Path, summary_path: Path, pid: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"AC-2: a second detached process, independent of both the engineer\n    process and of `start`'s own (immediately-returning) invocation, that\n    keeps `engineer.summary.log` growing for as long as the engineer pid it\n    was given stays alive. Never awaited/joined -- `_tail-summary` is an\n    internal subcommand, not part of the documented CLI surface.\"\"\"\n    subprocess.Popen(\n        [sys.executable, str(Path(__file__).resolve()), \"_tail-summary\",\n         \"--log\", str(log_path), \"--summary\", str(summary_path), \"--pid\", str(pid)],\n        stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n        start_new_session=True,\n    )\n\n\ndef _spawn_engineer(\n    *, worktree_path: Path, profile_path: Path, canonical_relay_dir: Path,\n    relay_file: Path, resume_session_id: str | None = None,\n    max_budget_usd: float = DEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET_USD,\n) -> subprocess.Popen:\n    env = dict(os.environ)\n    env[lr.ENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR] = str(canonical_relay_dir)\n    env[lr.ENV_RELAY_FILE] = str(relay_file)\n    # AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0015): with --permission-prompts none\n    # there is no human to answer a Read/Edit/Write-tool permission prompt\n    # for a path outside the worktree, so any such prompt is denied\n    # automatically -- and, once denied, stays denied for the rest of the\n    # session, no retries. A fresh dispatch only ever appeared to work\n    # because the engineer session happened to reach the canonical relay\n    # file through a Bash-invoked scripts/local_relay.py call, which this\n    # per-tool directory allowlist does not gate; nothing guarantees an\n    # engineer session -- fresh or resumed -- will choose Bash over its own\n    # Read/Edit tools for a \"read the relay file\" instruction. --add-dir\n    # pre-authorizes exactly the canonical relay directory for every tool,\n    # identically for a fresh dispatch and a resume, so access no longer\n    # depends on which tool the session happens to pick.\n    # AC-1 (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0013): --output-format stream-json requires\n    # --verbose alongside --print (confirmed against the installed claude\n    # version's own --help/runtime error before writing this, per that\n    # movement's own requirement) -- engineer.log now fills incrementally,\n    # one JSON object per line, instead of only at process exit.\n    argv = [\"claude\", \"-p\", ENGINEER_PROMPT, \"--settings\", str(profile_path),\n            \"--add-dir\", str(canonical_relay_dir),\n            \"--output-format\", \"stream-json\", \"--verbose\",\n            \"--permission-prompts\", \"none\", \"--max-budget-usd\", str(max_budget_usd)]\n    if resume_session_id:\n        argv += [\"--resume\", resume_session_id]\n    log_path = worktree_path / \".nexus\" / \"engineer.log\"\n    log_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    log_fh = open(log_path, \"ab\")\n    proc = subprocess.Popen(\n        argv, cwd=str(worktree_path), env=env,\n        stdout=log_fh, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n        start_new_session=True,\n    )\n    summary_path = log_path.parent / \"engineer.summary.log\"\n    _spawn_summary_tailer(log_path, summary_path, proc.pid)\n    return proc\n\n\ndef _kill_pid(pid: int, force: bool = False, grace_seconds: float = 5.0) -> None:\n    if not pid_alive(pid):\n        return\n    try:\n        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL if force else signal.SIGTERM)\n    except OSError:\n        return\n    if force:\n        return\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + grace_seconds\n    while time.monotonic() < deadline:\n        if not pid_alive(pid):\n            return\n        time.sleep(0.2)\n    try:\n        os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)\n    except OSError:\n        pass\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# start\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _cmd_start(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    relay_dir = Path(args.relay_dir).resolve()\n    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n    worktrees_dir = Path(args.worktrees_dir)\n    try:\n        relay_file = _resolve_relay_file(relay_dir, args.movement)\n        relay_obj = _load_relay(relay_file)\n    except OrchestratorError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n\n    existing = _load_state(state_dir, args.movement)\n    is_alive = pid_alive(existing.get(\"pid\")) if existing else False\n    active = _active_count(state_dir, exclude_movement=args.movement)\n    action, reason = decide_start(\n        relay_obj=relay_obj, existing_record=existing, is_pid_alive=is_alive,\n        active_count=active, max_workers=args.max_workers,\n    )\n    if action == \"refuse\":\n        print(f\"error: {reason}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_REFUSED\n\n    session_start = relay_obj[\"entries\"][0]\n    report = session_start.get(\"report\", {})\n    git_cfg = report.get(\"git\", {})\n    base, lane = git_cfg.get(\"base\"), git_cfg.get(\"lane\")\n    ok, ref_reason = validate_git_refs(base, lane)\n    if not ok:\n        print(f\"error: {ref_reason}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n\n    hash_hex = task_hash(session_start)\n\n    if action == \"resume\":\n        worktree_path = Path(existing[\"worktree_path\"])\n        branch = existing[\"branch\"]\n        base_sha = existing[\"base_sha\"]\n        revision = existing[\"revision\"]\n        session_id = existing.get(\"session_id\")\n        proc = _spawn_engineer(\n            worktree_path=worktree_path, profile_path=Path(args.profile),\n            canonical_relay_dir=relay_dir, relay_file=relay_file,\n            resume_session_id=session_id, max_budget_usd=args.max_budget_usd,\n        )\n        record = {**existing, \"pid\": proc.pid, \"phase\": PHASE_RUNNING,\n                  \"last_action\": \"resumed\", \"task_hash\": hash_hex,\n                  \"dispatch_seq\": len(relay_obj[\"entries\"])}\n        _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, record)\n        print(json.dumps({\"action\": \"resume\", \"movement_id\": args.movement, \"pid\": proc.pid,\n                           \"worktree_path\": str(worktree_path), \"revision\": revision}))\n        return EXIT_OK\n\n    # action == \"dispatch\"\n    revision = 1 if existing is None else existing.get(\"revision\", 0) + 1\n    worktree_path = worktrees_dir / args.movement\n    if worktree_path.exists():\n        print(f\"error: worktree path already exists: {worktree_path}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_REFUSED\n    try:\n        base_sha = _git_rev_parse(base, relay_dir.parent)\n        _git_worktree_add(worktree_path, base, lane, relay_dir.parent)\n    except OrchestratorError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_REFUSED\n\n    nexus_dir = worktree_path / \".nexus\"\n    nexus_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    (nexus_dir / \"approved_task.json\").write_text(canonical_json(session_start), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    (nexus_dir / \"movement_id.txt\").write_text(args.movement + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    proc = _spawn_engineer(\n        worktree_path=worktree_path, profile_path=Path(args.profile),\n        canonical_relay_dir=relay_dir, relay_file=relay_file,\n        max_budget_usd=args.max_budget_usd,\n    )\n    record = {\n        \"movement_id\": args.movement, \"revision\": revision, \"base_sha\": base_sha,\n        \"task_hash\": hash_hex, \"worktree_path\": str(worktree_path), \"branch\": lane,\n        \"pid\": proc.pid, \"session_id\": None, \"phase\": PHASE_RUNNING,\n        \"started_at\": lr._utc_now_iso(), \"heartbeat_at\": lr._utc_now_iso(),\n        \"retry_count\": 0, \"last_error\": None, \"last_action\": \"dispatched\",\n        \"dispatch_seq\": len(relay_obj[\"entries\"]),\n    }\n    _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, record)\n    print(json.dumps({\"action\": \"dispatch\", \"movement_id\": args.movement, \"pid\": proc.pid,\n                       \"worktree_path\": str(worktree_path), \"branch\": lane, \"revision\": revision}))\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# status\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _status_row(record: dict, relay_dir: Path, retry_limit: int) -> dict:\n    is_alive = pid_alive(record.get(\"pid\"))\n    relay_status = None\n    last_marker, last_timestamp = None, None\n    try:\n        relay_file = _resolve_relay_file(relay_dir, record[\"movement_id\"])\n        relay_obj = _load_relay(relay_file)\n        relay_status = relay_obj.get(\"status\")\n        entries = relay_obj.get(\"entries\") or []\n        dispatch_seq = record.get(\"dispatch_seq\")\n        if dispatch_seq is not None and len(entries) > dispatch_seq:\n            last_marker = \"REVISION_CHANGED_SINCE_DISPATCH\"\n        if entries:\n            last_marker = last_marker or entries[-1].get(\"marker\")\n            last_timestamp = entries[-1].get(\"timestamp\")\n    except OrchestratorError:\n        pass\n    phase = reconcile_phase(record, is_alive, relay_status, retry_limit)\n    if phase != record.get(\"phase\"):\n        record = {**record, \"phase\": phase}\n    return {\n        \"movement_id\": record[\"movement_id\"], \"phase\": phase, \"pid\": record.get(\"pid\"),\n        \"pid_alive\": is_alive, \"revision\": record.get(\"revision\"), \"branch\": record.get(\"branch\"),\n        \"worktree_path\": record.get(\"worktree_path\"), \"started_at\": record.get(\"started_at\"),\n        \"retry_count\": record.get(\"retry_count\", 0), \"relay_status\": relay_status,\n        \"last_marker\": last_marker, \"last_timestamp\": last_timestamp,\n        # AC-4: the most recent engineer.summary.log line, or None -- never\n        # an exception -- for a movement dispatched before AC-1/AC-2 landed\n        # (AC-5's own backward-compatibility requirement).\n        \"last_activity\": _read_last_activity(record.get(\"worktree_path\")),\n        \"heartbeat_age_seconds\": _heartbeat_age_seconds(record),\n    }\n\n\ndef _cmd_status(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    relay_dir = Path(args.relay_dir).resolve()\n    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n    if args.movement:\n        record = _load_state(state_dir, args.movement)\n        if record is None:\n            print(f\"error: no state record for {args.movement}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return EXIT_USAGE\n        row = _status_row(record, relay_dir, args.retry_limit)\n        _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, {**record, \"phase\": row[\"phase\"]})\n        print(json.dumps(row, sort_keys=True))\n        return EXIT_OK\n\n    rows = []\n    for record in _list_state_records(state_dir):\n        row = _status_row(record, relay_dir, args.retry_limit)\n        _save_state(state_dir, record[\"movement_id\"], {**record, \"phase\": row[\"phase\"]})\n        rows.append(row)\n    print(json.dumps(sorted(rows, key=lambda r: r[\"movement_id\"]), sort_keys=True))\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# stop\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _cmd_stop(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n    record = _load_state(state_dir, args.movement)\n    if record is None:\n        print(f\"error: no state record for {args.movement}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    _kill_pid(record.get(\"pid\"), force=args.force)\n    record = {**record, \"phase\": PHASE_CANCELLED, \"last_action\": \"stopped\"}\n    _save_state(state_dir, args.movement, record)\n    print(json.dumps({\"movement_id\": args.movement, \"phase\": PHASE_CANCELLED}))\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# merge-lock\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _lock_path(state_dir: Path) -> Path:\n    return state_dir / \"merge.lock.json\"\n\n\ndef _cmd_merge_lock(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n    state_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path = _lock_path(state_dir)\n    with lr._FileLock(path, timeout=args.wait):\n        if args.action == \"release\":\n            if path.is_file():\n                record = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n                if record.get(\"movement_id\") == args.movement:\n                    path.unlink()\n                    print(json.dumps({\"released\": True}))\n                    return EXIT_OK\n            print(json.dumps({\"released\": False, \"reason\": \"not held by this movement\"}))\n            return EXIT_REFUSED\n\n        lock_record = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if path.is_file() else None\n        granted, new_record, reason = decide_merge_lock_acquire(\n            lock_record=lock_record, requester_movement=args.movement,\n            requester_pid=args.pid, now=time.time(), ttl=args.ttl,\n        )\n        if granted:\n            lr._atomic_write(path, json.dumps(new_record, sort_keys=True, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n            print(json.dumps({\"acquired\": True, \"reason\": reason}))\n            return EXIT_OK\n        print(json.dumps({\"acquired\": False, \"reason\": reason}))\n        return EXIT_REFUSED\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# _tail-summary (internal -- spawned by _spawn_engineer, not user-facing)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _cmd_tail_summary(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    _tail_engineer_log(Path(args.log), Path(args.summary), args.pid, poll_interval=args.poll_interval)\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# watch (AC-3)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _gather_watch_rows(state_dir: Path, relay_dir: Path, retry_limit: int) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"The exact per-movement rows `status` computes, reused verbatim (AC-3:\n    \"polls the same data orchestrator status already computes\") -- but\n    never written back to `state_dir`, unlike `_cmd_status`'s own\n    reconciliation write. `watch` is read-only by its own explicit\n    invariant; `status` is not.\"\"\"\n    rows = [_status_row(record, relay_dir, retry_limit) for record in _list_state_records(state_dir)]\n    return sorted(rows, key=lambda r: r[\"movement_id\"])\n\n\ndef _render_watch_screen(rows: list[dict], terminal_width: int = 80) -> str:\n    lines = [f\"neXus orchestrator watch -- {len(rows)} known movement(s)\"]\n    if not rows:\n        lines.append(\"(no movements known)\")\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n    header = f\"{'MOVEMENT':<22}{'PHASE':<12}{'ALIVE':<7}{'AGE':<8}{'BRANCH':<26}{'LAST RELAY'}\"\n    lines.append(_truncate_to_width(header, terminal_width))\n    lines.append(\"-\" * min(len(header), terminal_width if terminal_width > 0 else len(header)))\n    for row in rows:\n        alive = \"yes\" if row.get(\"pid_alive\") else \"no\"\n        age = _format_age(row.get(\"heartbeat_age_seconds\"))\n        branch = row.get(\"branch\") or \"-\"\n        last_relay = f\"{row.get('last_marker') or '-'}@{row.get('last_timestamp') or '-'}\"\n        main_line = (\n            f\"{row['movement_id']:<22}{(row.get('phase') or '-'):<12}{alive:<7}{age:<8}{branch:<26}{last_relay}\"\n        )\n        lines.append(_truncate_to_width(main_line, terminal_width))\n        worktree = row.get(\"worktree_path\") or \"-\"\n        lines.append(_truncate_to_width(f\"  worktree: {worktree}\", terminal_width))\n        # AC-4/AC-5: last_activity is None for a movement dispatched before\n        # AC-1/AC-2 landed (old-format engineer.log, no summary.log yet) --\n        # render as \"n/a\", never raise.\n        activity = row.get(\"last_activity\") or \"n/a\"\n        lines.append(_truncate_to_width(f\"  last activity: {activity}\", terminal_width))\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines)\n\n\ndef _cmd_watch(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Human-facing dashboard loop. Deliberately distinct from\n    `local_relay.py watch`'s own bounded, single-wait design: that command\n    is an unattended primitive a script polls once for one specific\n    next_actor flip, with a hard timeout ceiling so it can never become a\n    silent daemon. This command is the opposite kind of tool -- a live\n    display a human keeps open and reads continuously -- so it loops until\n    the human interrupts it (Ctrl-C) rather than returning after one\n    bounded wait; that is a real design difference, not an oversight.\n    Read-only throughout: every call below is a read (`_gather_watch_rows`\n    never calls `_save_state`), and it mutates no on-disk state.\"\"\"\n    relay_dir = Path(args.relay_dir).resolve()\n    state_dir = Path(args.state_dir)\n    try:\n        while True:\n            rows = _gather_watch_rows(state_dir, relay_dir, args.retry_limit)\n            width = shutil.get_terminal_size(fallback=(100, 24)).columns\n            os.system(\"cls\" if os.name == \"nt\" else \"clear\")\n            print(_render_watch_screen(rows, width))\n            time.sleep(args.interval)\n    except KeyboardInterrupt:\n        return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CLI\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _add_common(parser: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:\n    parser.add_argument(\"--relay-dir\", default=\"relay\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--state-dir\", default=str(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR))\n\n\ndef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"orchestrator\", description=__doc__)\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n\n    p_start = sub.add_parser(\"start\", help=\"dispatch (or resume) one approved movement\")\n    p_start.add_argument(\"--movement\", required=True)\n    _add_common(p_start)\n    p_start.add_argument(\"--worktrees-dir\", default=str(DEFAULT_WORKTREES_DIR))\n    p_start.add_argument(\"--profile\", default=str(DEFAULT_ENGINEER_PROFILE))\n    p_start.add_argument(\"--max-workers\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MAX_WORKERS)\n    p_start.add_argument(\"--max-budget-usd\", type=float, default=DEFAULT_MAX_BUDGET_USD)\n    p_start.set_defaults(func=_cmd_start)\n\n    p_status = sub.add_parser(\"status\", help=\"report one movement, or every known movement\")\n    p_status.add_argument(\"--movement\", default=None)\n    _add_common(p_status)\n    p_status.add_argument(\"--retry-limit\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RETRY_LIMIT)\n    p_status.set_defaults(func=_cmd_status)\n\n    p_stop = sub.add_parser(\"stop\", help=\"cancel one movement's engineer process\")\n    p_stop.add_argument(\"--movement\", required=True)\n    _add_common(p_stop)\n    p_stop.add_argument(\"--force\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"SIGKILL immediately, skip the SIGTERM grace period\")\n    p_stop.set_defaults(func=_cmd_stop)\n\n    p_lock = sub.add_parser(\"merge-lock\", help=\"acquire/release the cross-movement merge-serialization lock\")\n    p_lock.add_argument(\"action\", choices=(\"acquire\", \"release\"))\n    p_lock.add_argument(\"--movement\", required=True)\n    p_lock.add_argument(\"--pid\", type=int, default=os.getpid())\n    p_lock.add_argument(\"--ttl\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_MERGE_LOCK_TTL)\n    p_lock.add_argument(\"--wait\", type=float, default=30.0)\n    p_lock.add_argument(\"--state-dir\", default=str(DEFAULT_STATE_DIR))\n    p_lock.set_defaults(func=_cmd_merge_lock)\n\n    p_watch = sub.add_parser(\n        \"watch\", help=\"read-only terminal dashboard: phase, liveness, and last activity for every movement\"\n    )\n    _add_common(p_watch)\n    p_watch.add_argument(\"--interval\", type=int, default=WATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT)\n    p_watch.add_argument(\"--retry-limit\", type=int, default=DEFAULT_RETRY_LIMIT)\n    p_watch.set_defaults(func=_cmd_watch)\n\n    # Internal only -- spawned by _spawn_engineer, never invoked directly by\n    # a human or documented in this module's own CLI docstring.\n    p_tail = sub.add_parser(\"_tail-summary\")\n    p_tail.add_argument(\"--log\", required=True)\n    p_tail.add_argument(\"--summary\", required=True)\n    p_tail.add_argument(\"--pid\", type=int, required=True)\n    p_tail.add_argument(\"--poll-interval\", type=float, default=TAIL_POLL_INTERVAL_DEFAULT)\n    p_tail.set_defaults(func=_cmd_tail_summary)\n\n    return parser\n\n\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)\n    return args.func(args)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":950,"startLine":1,"totalLines":950}}}
