{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CerLeuTV1LmCiPPWL7wSm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YLCMGfMcm3XWFEdgbGBF5e","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/OzanDur/Codo/neXus-nexus-worktrees/NXS-LOCAL-0021/scripts/local_relay.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20652,"cache_read_input_tokens":66302,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20652},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a8dd4a7-31e7-434f-89b1-73b3ad9d3b22","uuid":"46f2d427-18ee-41b1-899b-cffb0fd29aa1","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:07:58.135Z","request_id":"req_011CerLetoYMre2iSE1pQRFJ"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YLCMGfMcm3XWFEdgbGBF5e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"GOV.PO.1 -- local, file-based relay transport (stdlib only).\n2\t\n3\t    py scripts/local_relay.py create   --role {po|engineer} --start FILE|- [--dir relay] [--slug SLUG]\n4\t    py scripts/local_relay.py append   --file FILE --role {po|engineer} --marker MARKER [...]\n5\t    py scripts/local_relay.py status   --file FILE\n6\t    py scripts/local_relay.py validate --file FILE\n7\t    py scripts/local_relay.py watch    --file FILE --for {po|engineer}\n8\t                                        [--interval SECONDS] [--timeout SECONDS]\n9\t\n10\tFull contract: docs/design/LOCAL_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md (DRAFT). This is an\n11\tADDITIONAL transport for same-machine, same-checkout Product-Owner/engineer\n12\tcoordination -- it does not amend or replace\n13\tdocs/design/NEXUS_AGENT_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md or the GitHub-based\n14\t`RELAY_READY owner/repository#issue` workflow, which stay exactly as they\n15\tare for cross-machine or human-external-visibility work.\n16\t\n17\tOne tracked JSON file per movement under `relay/`\n18\t(`relay/NXS-LOCAL-<4-digit-id>-<slug>.json`), an append-only `entries`\n19\tarray reusing `NEXUS_AGENT_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md`'s five markers\n20\t(`RELAY_ACK`/`RELAY_NOTE`/`RELAY_QUESTION`/`RELAY_DECISION`/\n21\t`RELAY_CORRECTION`) plus `GOV.SESSION.1`'s two packet types\n22\t(`SESSION_START`/`SESSION_CLOSE`), and a top-level `next_actor` field\n23\t(`\"po\"`/`\"engineer\"`/`null`) enforcing single-writer-at-a-time turn\n24\townership: `append --role <r>` is rejected unless `<r>` equals the file's\n25\tcurrent `next_actor`.\n26\t\n27\tThis module imports `scripts/gov_session_transfer.py` (same directory) to\n28\tvalidate `SESSION_START`/`SESSION_CLOSE` `report` objects against its\n29\texisting, unchanged schema (`_REPORT_SCHEMA_BY_TYPE`, `_validate_node`,\n30\t`OUTCOMES`) -- reused directly, never re-derived, so the two transports can\n31\tnever drift into two different ideas of what a valid report looks like.\n32\t\n33\t`watch` is a bounded, blocking, read-only poll of one relay file's\n34\t`next_actor` field -- never a background daemon (a hard `--timeout`\n35\tceiling makes that impossible by construction). It never writes, appends,\n36\tor mutates the watched file; a detected `next_actor` flip is only ever\n37\treported to the invoking session, which still needs the human's explicit\n38\twritten authorization before acting on any `RELAY_DECISION`-class content,\n39\texactly as today.\n40\t\n41\tCanonical-location resolver (GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md,\n42\tFROZEN, section 3.6): a git worktree checks out its own copy of `relay/`,\n43\tso a bare relative `--file`/`--dir` argument resolved against an engineer\n44\tworktree's own cwd would silently read/write that worktree's copy instead\n45\tof the one physical file the Product Owner's session reads -- never the\n46\tlive channel. Two environment variables let a caller omit `--dir`/`--file`\n47\tentirely and always resolve to the one canonical location the orchestrator\n48\tsets when it spawns an engineer process, with no change to behavior when\n49\tneither is set (today's cwd-relative default, unchanged byte-for-byte):\n50\t`NEXUS_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR` (an absolute path) is `create`'s `--dir`\n51\tdefault when `--dir` is omitted; `NEXUS_RELAY_FILE` (an absolute path to\n52\tone exact relay file) is `append`/`status`/`validate`/`watch`'s `--file`\n53\tdefault when `--file` is omitted. An explicit `--dir`/`--file` argument\n54\talways wins over either variable.\n55\t\n56\tShared append lock: `append`'s existing optimistic re-read-and-compare\n57\t(below) never corrupts or silently loses an entry, but leaves a losing\n58\tconcurrent writer to be retried by whoever called it -- fine when a human\n59\tis present, not when the orchestrator and an unattended engineer process\n60\tcan both legitimately touch the same canonical file for the same movement\n61\twhile both are alive. `append` now wraps its whole read-validate-build-\n62\twrite sequence in a real advisory file lock (`fcntl.flock` on POSIX,\n63\t`msvcrt.locking` on Windows -- stdlib only, no third-party dependency) on\n64\ta sidecar `<file>.lock`, bounded by a wait timeout; the existing hash\n65\tcompare stays as defense-in-depth underneath it, unchanged.\n66\t\n67\tOffline, synchronous. No network, daemon, credential, or device access.\n68\tExit codes: 0 success, 1 invalid/rejected (schema violation, wrong-turn\n69\tappend, concurrent-write conflict, append to a CLOSED movement), 2 usage\n70\terror (bad arguments, missing file, an out-of-range `watch` `--interval`/\n71\t`--timeout`), 3 `watch` timed out with no qualifying `next_actor` change --\n72\tthe same convention `gov_session_transfer.py` uses, extended with 3 for\n73\t`watch` only.\n74\t\"\"\"\n75\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n76\t\n77\timport argparse\n78\timport json\n79\timport os\n80\timport re\n81\timport sys\n82\timport tempfile\n83\timport time\n84\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n85\tfrom pathlib import Path\n86\tfrom typing import Any\n87\t\n88\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\n89\timport gov_session_transfer as gst  # noqa: E402\n90\t\n91\ttry:\n92\t    import fcntl as _fcntl\n93\texcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- Windows\n94\t    _fcntl = None\n95\ttry:\n96\t    import msvcrt as _msvcrt\n97\texcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- POSIX\n98\t    _msvcrt = None\n99\t\n100\tEXIT_OK, EXIT_INVALID, EXIT_USAGE, EXIT_TIMEOUT = 0, 1, 2, 3\n101\t\n102\t#: GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md section 3.6: an absolute\n103\t#: canonical relay directory / exact relay file, set by the orchestrator in\n104\t#: every engineer process it spawns so every worktree resolves to the one\n105\t#: physical location the Product Owner's own session reads -- never a\n106\t#: per-worktree copy. Unset in every session that does not opt in (the\n107\t#: Product Owner's own interactive session, today); default behavior is\n108\t#: then byte-for-byte unchanged from before this variable existed.\n109\tENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR = \"NEXUS_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR\"\n110\tENV_RELAY_FILE = \"NEXUS_RELAY_FILE\"\n111\t\n112\t#: How long `append` waits for the shared file lock before giving up.\n113\t#: Module-level so tests can shrink it rather than waiting out the real\n114\t#: default against a genuinely held lock.\n115\tAPPEND_LOCK_TIMEOUT = 30.0\n116\t\n117\t#: `watch` bounds (AC-1/AC-2): a floor on --interval and a ceiling on\n118\t#: --timeout so it can never approximate an unbounded background daemon.\n119\tWATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT = 20\n120\tWATCH_INTERVAL_FLOOR = 5\n121\tWATCH_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT = 1800\n122\tWATCH_TIMEOUT_CEILING = 3600\n123\t\n124\tSCHEMA_VERSION = 1\n125\tID_PREFIX = \"NXS-LOCAL-\"\n126\tID_RE = re.compile(r\"^NXS-LOCAL-(\\d{4})$\")\n127\tFILENAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^(NXS-LOCAL-\\d{4})-[a-z0-9-]+\\.json$\")\n128\t\n129\tROLES = (\"po\", \"engineer\")\n130\tSTATUSES = (\"OPEN\", \"IN_PROGRESS\", \"AWAITING_PO\", \"AWAITING_ENGINEER\", \"CLOSED\")\n131\t\n132\t#: The two GOV.SESSION.1 packet types plus NEXUS_AGENT_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md's\n133\t#: five intermediate markers -- seven total, closed, reused verbatim.\n134\tRELAY_MARKERS = (\"RELAY_ACK\", \"RELAY_NOTE\", \"RELAY_QUESTION\", \"RELAY_DECISION\", \"RELAY_CORRECTION\")\n135\tMARKERS = (\"SESSION_START\", \"SESSION_CLOSE\") + RELAY_MARKERS\n136\t#: Every marker except SESSION_START may be appended -- SESSION_START only\n137\t#: ever exists as entries[0], written by `create`.\n138\tAPPENDABLE_MARKERS = (\"SESSION_CLOSE\",) + RELAY_MARKERS\n139\t#: Markers whose only required fields are `subject`/`text` (RELAY_DECISION\n140\t#: additionally requires authorized_by/scope/supersedes; SESSION_CLOSE\n141\t#: requires report/outcome instead).\n142\tNARRATIVE_MARKERS = (\"RELAY_ACK\", \"RELAY_NOTE\", \"RELAY_QUESTION\", \"RELAY_CORRECTION\")\n143\t\n144\t_COMMON_ENTRY_FIELDS = {\n145\t    \"marker\": (\"enum\", frozenset(MARKERS)),\n146\t    \"actor\": (\"enum\", frozenset(ROLES)),\n147\t    \"timestamp\": (\"str\",),\n148\t}\n149\t\n150\t\n151\tdef _entry_schema(extra: dict) -> tuple:\n152\t    return (\"obj\", {**_COMMON_ENTRY_FIELDS, **extra})\n153\t\n154\t\n155\t#: One closed-shape schema per marker (gov_session_transfer.py's own generic\n156\t#: tuple-based schema kinds, reused directly -- see module docstring).\n157\tENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER = {\n158\t    \"SESSION_START\": _entry_schema({\"report\": gst.SESSION_START_REPORT_SCHEMA}),\n159\t    \"SESSION_CLOSE\": _entry_schema({\"report\": gst.SESSION_CLOSE_REPORT_SCHEMA, \"outcome\": (\"enum\", gst.OUTCOMES)}),\n160\t    \"RELAY_DECISION\": _entry_schema({\n161\t        \"subject\": (\"str\",), \"text\": (\"str\",),\n162\t        \"authorized_by\": (\"str\",), \"scope\": (\"str\",), \"supersedes\": (\"str\",),\n163\t    }),\n164\t}\n165\tfor _marker in (\"RELAY_ACK\", \"RELAY_NOTE\", \"RELAY_QUESTION\", \"RELAY_CORRECTION\"):\n166\t    ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER[_marker] = _entry_schema({\"subject\": (\"str\",), \"text\": (\"str\",)})\n167\t\n168\tTOP_LEVEL_FIELDS = {\n169\t    \"schema_version\", \"id\", \"movement\", \"refs\", \"status\", \"next_actor\",\n170\t    \"created_at\", \"updated_at\", \"entries\",\n171\t}\n172\t\n173\t\n174\tclass LocalRelayError(ValueError):\n175\t    \"\"\"A CLI-level request could not be satisfied (bad input, wrong turn,\n176\t    a closed movement, or a concurrent-write conflict).\"\"\"\n177\t\n178\t\n179\tdef _utc_now_iso() -> str:\n180\t    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n181\t\n182\t\n183\tdef _slugify(text: str) -> str:\n184\t    slug = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", text.strip().lower()).strip(\"-\")\n185\t    return (slug or \"movement\")[:40]\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n189\t# Structural validation (pure -- no filesystem access)\n190\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n191\t\n192\tdef _validate_entry(entry: Any, index: int, errors: list[str]) -> None:\n193\t    path = f\"entries[{index}]\"\n194\t    if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n195\t        errors.append(f\"{path}: must be an object\")\n196\t        return\n197\t    marker = entry.get(\"marker\")\n198\t    if marker not in ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER:\n199\t        errors.append(f\"{path}.marker: must be one of {sorted(ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER)}\")\n200\t        return\n201\t    working = dict(entry)\n202\t    seq = working.pop(\"seq\", None)\n203\t    good_to_go = working.pop(\"good_to_go\", None)\n204\t    if seq != index + 1 or isinstance(seq, bool) or not isinstance(seq, int):\n205\t        errors.append(f\"{path}.seq: must equal {index + 1}\")\n206\t    if good_to_go is not None and not isinstance(good_to_go, bool):\n207\t        errors.append(f\"{path}.good_to_go: must be a boolean\")\n208\t    gst._validate_node(working, ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER[marker], path, errors)\n209\t\n210\t\n211\tdef _validate_shape_and_order(entries: list, errors: list[str]) -> None:\n212\t    if not entries:\n213\t        errors.append(\"entries: must be a non-empty list\")\n214\t        return\n215\t    if not (isinstance(entries[0], dict) and entries[0].get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_START\"):\n216\t        errors.append(\"entries[0].marker: must be SESSION_START\")\n217\t    starts = sum(1 for e in entries if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_START\")\n218\t    if starts != 1:\n219\t        errors.append(f\"entries: exactly one SESSION_START required, found {starts}\")\n220\t    for i, entry in enumerate(entries):\n221\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_START\" and i != 0:\n222\t            errors.append(f\"entries[{i}]: SESSION_START may only appear at position 0\")\n223\t        if isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" and i != len(entries) - 1:\n224\t            errors.append(f\"entries[{i}]: SESSION_CLOSE may only be the last entry\")\n225\t    closes = sum(1 for e in entries if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_CLOSE\")\n226\t    if closes > 1:\n227\t        errors.append(f\"entries: at most one SESSION_CLOSE allowed, found {closes}\")\n228\t\n229\t\n230\tdef _validate_turn_state(obj: dict, errors: list[str]) -> None:\n231\t    entries = obj.get(\"entries\")\n232\t    if not isinstance(entries, list) or not entries or not isinstance(entries[-1], dict):\n233\t        return  # already reported by _validate_shape_and_order\n234\t    last = entries[-1]\n235\t    next_actor = obj.get(\"next_actor\")\n236\t    status = obj.get(\"status\")\n237\t    closed = last.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" or next_actor is None\n238\t    if closed:\n239\t        if next_actor is not None:\n240\t            errors.append(\"next_actor: must be null once the movement is closed\")\n241\t        if status != \"CLOSED\":\n242\t            errors.append(f\"status: must be CLOSED when next_actor is null, got {status!r}\")\n243\t        return\n244\t    if next_actor not in ROLES:\n245\t        errors.append(f\"next_actor: must be 'po', 'engineer', or null when CLOSED, got {next_actor!r}\")\n246\t        return\n247\t    if len(entries) == 1:\n248\t        if status != \"OPEN\":\n249\t            errors.append(f\"status: must be OPEN with only the SESSION_START entry present, got {status!r}\")\n250\t        return\n251\t    expected = \"AWAITING_PO\" if next_actor == \"po\" else \"AWAITING_ENGINEER\"\n252\t    if status not in (expected, \"IN_PROGRESS\"):\n253\t        errors.append(f\"status: must be {expected} or IN_PROGRESS when next_actor is {next_actor!r}, got {status!r}\")\n254\t\n255\t\n256\tdef validate_relay_object(obj: Any) -> list[str]:\n257\t    \"\"\"Structural + internal-consistency validation of one relay file's\n258\t    already-parsed JSON object. Pure -- takes no filesystem path, proves\n259\t    shape and internal consistency, never that a filename matches `id`\n260\t    (the CLI layer checks that separately, where it has a real path).\"\"\"\n261\t    if not isinstance(obj, dict):\n262\t        return [\"must be a JSON object\"]\n263\t\n264\t    errors: list[str] = []\n265\t    for field in sorted(set(obj) - TOP_LEVEL_FIELDS):\n266\t        errors.append(f\"{field}: unknown top-level field\")\n267\t    missing = TOP_LEVEL_FIELDS - set(obj)\n268\t    for field in sorted(missing):\n269\t        errors.append(f\"{field}: missing required field\")\n270\t\n271\t    # Only type-check a field that is actually present -- an absent field\n272\t    # was already reported above; re-checking its (nonexistent) type would\n273\t    # just double-report the same defect under two messages.\n274\t    if \"schema_version\" in obj and obj[\"schema_version\"] != SCHEMA_VERSION:\n275\t        errors.append(f\"schema_version: must be {SCHEMA_VERSION}\")\n276\t    if \"id\" in obj and not (isinstance(obj[\"id\"], str) and ID_RE.match(obj[\"id\"])):\n277\t        errors.append(f\"id: must match {ID_RE.pattern}\")\n278\t    if \"movement\" in obj and not (isinstance(obj[\"movement\"], str) and obj[\"movement\"]):\n279\t        errors.append(\"movement: must be a non-empty string\")\n280\t    if \"refs\" in obj:\n281\t        gst._validate_node(obj[\"refs\"], (\"list_str\", True), \"refs\", errors)\n282\t    if \"status\" in obj and obj[\"status\"] not in STATUSES:\n283\t        errors.append(f\"status: must be one of {STATUSES}\")\n284\t    for field in (\"created_at\", \"updated_at\"):\n285\t        if field in obj and not (isinstance(obj[field], str) and obj[field]):\n286\t            errors.append(f\"{field}: must be a non-empty string\")\n287\t\n288\t    if \"entries\" in obj:\n289\t        entries = obj[\"entries\"]\n290\t        if not isinstance(entries, list):\n291\t            errors.append(\"entries: must be a list\")\n292\t        else:\n293\t            _validate_shape_and_order(entries, errors)\n294\t            for i, entry in enumerate(entries):\n295\t                _validate_entry(entry, i, errors)\n296\t\n297\t    if not ({\"next_actor\", \"status\", \"entries\"} & missing):\n298\t        _validate_turn_state(obj, errors)\n299\t    return errors\n300\t\n301\t\n302\tdef _id_matches_filename(obj_id: str, path: Path) -> bool:\n303\t    match = FILENAME_RE.match(path.name)\n304\t    return bool(match) and match.group(1) == obj_id\n305\t\n306\t\n307\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n308\t# Filesystem helpers\n309\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n310\t\n311\tdef _next_id(relay_dir: Path) -> int:\n312\t    if not relay_dir.is_dir():\n313\t        return 1\n314\t    best = 0\n315\t    for candidate in relay_dir.glob(f\"{ID_PREFIX}*.json\"):\n316\t        match = re.match(r\"^NXS-LOCAL-(\\d{4})-\", candidate.name)\n317\t        if match:\n318\t            best = max(best, int(match.group(1)))\n319\t    return best + 1\n320\t\n321\t\n322\tdef _resolve_relay_dir(explicit: str | None) -> Path:\n323\t    \"\"\"`create --dir`'s effective value: the explicit flag always wins;\n324\t    otherwise `NEXUS_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR` when set; otherwise today's\n325\t    unchanged cwd-relative default.\"\"\"\n326\t    return Path(explicit or os.environ.get(ENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR) or \"relay\")\n327\t\n328\t\n329\tdef _resolve_relay_file(explicit: str | None) -> str | None:\n330\t    \"\"\"`append`/`status`/`validate`/`watch --file`'s effective value: the\n331\t    explicit flag always wins; otherwise `NEXUS_RELAY_FILE` when set;\n332\t    otherwise None (caller reports a usage error, exactly as an absent\n333\t    required argument would have before this resolver existed).\"\"\"\n334\t    return explicit or os.environ.get(ENV_RELAY_FILE)\n335\t\n336\t\n337\tdef _dump(obj: dict) -> str:\n338\t    return json.dumps(obj, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n339\t\n340\t\n341\tdef _atomic_write(path: Path, text: str) -> None:\n342\t    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n343\t    fd, tmp_name = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=str(path.parent), prefix=f\".{path.name}.\", suffix=\".tmp\")\n344\t    try:\n345\t        with os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n346\t            fh.write(text)\n347\t        os.replace(tmp_name, path)\n348\t    except BaseException:\n349\t        try:\n350\t            os.unlink(tmp_name)\n351\t        except OSError:\n352\t            pass\n353\t        raise\n354\t\n355\t\n356\tclass FileLockTimeout(LocalRelayError):\n357\t    \"\"\"A real advisory lock on a relay file could not be acquired in time --\n358\t    a genuinely concurrent writer (not merely the wrong-turn/hash checks\n359\t    above) is holding it.\"\"\"\n360\t\n361\t\n362\tclass _FileLock:\n363\t    \"\"\"Real, cross-platform (stdlib-only) advisory exclusive lock on a\n364\t    sidecar `<path>.lock` file, bounded by `timeout` seconds. `fcntl.flock`\n365\t    on POSIX, `msvcrt.locking` on Windows; degrades to a no-op (documented,\n366\t    not silent -- see module docstring) on a platform with neither, which\n367\t    leaves the existing optimistic hash-compare in `append` as the only\n368\t    concurrency guard, exactly as before this class existed.\"\"\"\n369\t\n370\t    def __init__(self, target: Path, timeout: float = 30.0) -> None:\n371\t        self._lock_path = Path(str(target) + \".lock\")\n372\t        self._timeout = timeout\n373\t        self._fh = None\n374\t\n375\t    def __enter__(self) -> \"_FileLock\":\n376\t        self._lock_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n377\t        self._fh = open(self._lock_path, \"a+b\")\n378\t        deadline = time.monotonic() + self._timeout\n379\t        while True:\n380\t            try:\n381\t                if _fcntl is not None:\n382\t                    _fcntl.flock(self._fh.fileno(), _fcntl.LOCK_EX | _fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n383\t                elif _msvcrt is not None:\n384\t                    self._fh.seek(0)\n385\t                    _msvcrt.locking(self._fh.fileno(), _msvcrt.LK_NBLCK, 1)\n386\t                else:  # pragma: no cover -- no known stdlib primitive on this platform\n387\t                    break\n388\t                return self\n389\t            except OSError:\n390\t                if time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n391\t                    self._fh.close()\n392\t                    raise FileLockTimeout(\n393\t                        f\"could not acquire lock {self._lock_path} within {self._timeout}s\")\n394\t                time.sleep(0.05)\n395\t\n396\t    def __exit__(self, *exc_info: object) -> None:\n397\t        try:\n398\t            if _fcntl is not None:\n399\t                _fcntl.flock(self._fh.fileno(), _fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n400\t            elif _msvcrt is not None:  # pragma: no cover -- exercised on Windows only\n401\t                self._fh.seek(0)\n402\t                _msvcrt.locking(self._fh.fileno(), _msvcrt.LK_UNLCK, 1)\n403\t        finally:\n404\t            self._fh.close()\n405\t\n406\t\n407\tdef _load_json_file(path: Path) -> Any:\n408\t    if not path.is_file():\n409\t        raise LocalRelayError(f\"no such file: {path}\")\n410\t    try:\n411\t        return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n412\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n413\t        raise LocalRelayError(f\"invalid JSON: {exc}\") from exc\n414\t\n415\t\n416\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n417\t# create\n418\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n419\t\n420\tdef _cmd_create(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n421\t    try:\n422\t        raw = gst._read_input(args.start)\n423\t    except gst.PacketError as exc:\n424\t        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n425\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n426\t    try:\n427\t        start_obj = json.loads(raw)\n428\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n429\t        print(f\"error: invalid JSON: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n430\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n431\t    if start_obj.get(\"message_type\") is None:\n432\t        start_obj = dict(start_obj)\n433\t        start_obj.setdefault(\"protocol_version\", 2)\n434\t        start_obj.setdefault(\"message_type\", \"SESSION_START\")\n435\t    errors = gst.validate_fields(start_obj)\n436\t    if start_obj.get(\"message_type\") != \"SESSION_START\":\n437\t        errors.append(\"message_type: must be SESSION_START (local relay files always open with one)\")\n438\t    if errors:\n439\t        print(f\"error: {'; '.join(errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n440\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n441\t\n442\t    relay_dir = _resolve_relay_dir(args.dir)\n443\t    next_id = _next_id(relay_dir)\n444\t    full_id = f\"{ID_PREFIX}{next_id:04d}\"\n445\t    slug = _slugify(args.slug or start_obj[\"movement\"])\n446\t    target = relay_dir / f\"{full_id}-{slug}.json\"\n447\t    if target.exists():\n448\t        print(f\"error: {target} already exists\", file=sys.stderr)\n449\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n450\t\n451\t    now = _utc_now_iso()\n452\t    other_role = \"engineer\" if args.role == \"po\" else \"po\"\n453\t    file_obj = {\n454\t        \"schema_version\": SCHEMA_VERSION,\n455\t        \"id\": full_id,\n456\t        \"movement\": start_obj[\"movement\"],\n457\t        \"refs\": start_obj[\"refs\"],\n458\t        \"status\": \"OPEN\",\n459\t        \"next_actor\": other_role,\n460\t        \"created_at\": now,\n461\t        \"updated_at\": now,\n462\t        \"entries\": [{\n463\t            \"seq\": 1, \"marker\": \"SESSION_START\", \"actor\": args.role,\n464\t            \"timestamp\": now, \"report\": start_obj[\"report\"],\n465\t        }],\n466\t    }\n467\t    internal_errors = validate_relay_object(file_obj)\n468\t    if internal_errors:  # pragma: no cover -- defensive; construction above should always be valid\n469\t        print(f\"error: internal consistency check failed: {'; '.join(internal_errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n470\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n471\t\n472\t    _atomic_write(target, _dump(file_obj))\n473\t    print(str(target))\n474\t    return EXIT_OK\n475\t\n476\t\n477\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n478\t# append\n479\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n480\t\n481\tdef _build_entry(args: argparse.Namespace, seq: int, timestamp: str) -> tuple[dict | None, str | None]:\n482\t    marker = args.marker\n483\t    entry: dict[str, Any] = {\"seq\": seq, \"marker\": marker, \"actor\": args.role, \"timestamp\": timestamp}\n484\t    if args.good_to_go:\n485\t        entry[\"good_to_go\"] = True\n486\t\n487\t    if marker == \"SESSION_CLOSE\":\n488\t        if not args.report:\n489\t            return None, \"--report is required for SESSION_CLOSE\"\n490\t        try:\n491\t            report_obj = json.loads(gst._read_input(args.report))\n492\t        except gst.PacketError as exc:\n493\t            return None, str(exc)\n494\t        except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n495\t            return None, f\"--report is not valid JSON: {exc}\"\n496\t        if not args.outcome:\n497\t            return None, \"--outcome is required for SESSION_CLOSE\"\n498\t        report_errors: list[str] = []\n499\t        gst._validate_node(report_obj, gst.SESSION_CLOSE_REPORT_SCHEMA, \"report\", report_errors)\n500\t        if report_errors:\n501\t            return None, \"; \".join(report_errors)\n502\t        entry[\"report\"] = report_obj\n503\t        entry[\"outcome\"] = args.outcome\n504\t        return entry, None\n505\t\n506\t    subject = args.subject or (\"good to go\" if args.good_to_go else None)\n507\t    text = args.text or (\"good to go\" if args.good_to_go else None)\n508\t    if not subject or not text:\n509\t        return None, \"--subject and --text are required (or pass --good-to-go for the fast path)\"\n510\t    entry[\"subject\"] = subject\n511\t    entry[\"text\"] = text\n512\t\n513\t    if marker == \"RELAY_DECISION\":\n514\t        for field, value in ((\"authorized_by\", args.authorized_by), (\"scope\", args.scope), (\"supersedes\", args.supersedes)):\n515\t            if not value:\n516\t                return None, f\"--{field.replace('_', '-')} is required for RELAY_DECISION\"\n517\t        entry[\"authorized_by\"] = args.authorized_by\n518\t        entry[\"scope\"] = args.scope\n519\t        entry[\"supersedes\"] = args.supersedes\n520\t    elif marker not in NARRATIVE_MARKERS:\n521\t        return None, f\"{marker} cannot be appended (SESSION_START only via create)\"\n522\t\n523\t    return entry, None\n524\t\n525\t\n526\tdef _cmd_append(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n527\t    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n528\t    if not resolved:\n529\t        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n530\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n531\t    path = Path(resolved)\n532\t    try:\n533\t        with _FileLock(path, timeout=APPEND_LOCK_TIMEOUT):\n534\t            return _cmd_append_locked(args, path)\n535\t    except FileLockTimeout as exc:\n536\t        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n537\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n538\t\n539\t\n540\tdef _cmd_append_locked(args: argparse.Namespace, path: Path) -> int:\n541\t    try:\n542\t        raw_before = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n543\t    except OSError as exc:\n544\t        print(f\"error: no such file: {path} ({exc})\", file=sys.stderr)\n545\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n546\t    try:\n547\t        obj = json.loads(raw_before)\n548\t    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n549\t        print(f\"error: {path} is not valid JSON: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n550\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n551\t    errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n552\t    if not _id_matches_filename(obj.get(\"id\", \"\"), path):\n553\t        errors.append(f\"id {obj.get('id')!r} does not match filename {path.name!r}\")\n554\t    if errors:\n555\t        print(f\"error: {path} fails validation, refusing to append: {'; '.join(errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n556\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n557\t\n558\t    if obj[\"status\"] == \"CLOSED\":\n559\t        print(f\"error: {path} is CLOSED; no further entries may be appended\", file=sys.stderr)\n560\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n561\t    if obj[\"next_actor\"] != args.role:\n562\t        print(f\"error: not {args.role}'s turn (next_actor is {obj['next_actor']!r})\", file=sys.stderr)\n563\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n564\t    if args.marker not in APPENDABLE_MARKERS:\n565\t        print(f\"error: {args.marker} cannot be appended (SESSION_START only via create)\", file=sys.stderr)\n566\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n567\t    if args.close and args.in_progress:\n568\t        print(\"error: --close and --in-progress are mutually exclusive\", file=sys.stderr)\n569\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n570\t    if args.marker != \"SESSION_CLOSE\" and not args.close and not args.next:\n571\t        print(\"error: --next {po|engineer} is required unless --close is passed\", file=sys.stderr)\n572\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n573\t    if args.marker == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" and (args.next or args.close):\n574\t        print(\"error: --next/--close are redundant with SESSION_CLOSE, which always closes\", file=sys.stderr)\n575\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n576\t\n577\t    now = _utc_now_iso()\n578\t    entry, build_error = _build_entry(args, len(obj[\"entries\"]) + 1, now)\n579\t    if build_error:\n580\t        print(f\"error: {build_error}\", file=sys.stderr)\n581\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n582\t\n583\t    closing = args.marker == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" or args.close\n584\t    obj[\"entries\"].append(entry)\n585\t    obj[\"updated_at\"] = now\n586\t    if closing:\n587\t        obj[\"next_actor\"] = None\n588\t        obj[\"status\"] = \"CLOSED\"\n589\t    else:\n590\t        obj[\"next_actor\"] = args.next\n591\t        obj[\"status\"] = \"IN_PROGRESS\" if args.in_progress else (\"AWAITING_PO\" if args.next == \"po\" else \"AWAITING_ENGINEER\")\n592\t\n593\t    internal_errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n594\t    if internal_errors:  # pragma: no cover -- defensive; construction above should always be valid\n595\t        print(f\"error: internal consistency check failed: {'; '.join(internal_errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n596\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n597\t\n598\t    try:\n599\t        raw_now = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n600\t    except OSError as exc:\n601\t        print(f\"error: file disappeared before write: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n602\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n603\t    if raw_now != raw_before:\n604\t        print(f\"error: {path} changed since it was read -- a concurrent write occurred; \"\n605\t              f\"re-run against the latest state\", file=sys.stderr)\n606\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n607\t\n608\t    _atomic_write(path, _dump(obj))\n609\t    print(json.dumps({\"status\": obj[\"status\"], \"next_actor\": obj[\"next_actor\"], \"seq\": entry[\"seq\"]}))\n610\t    return EXIT_OK\n611\t\n612\t\n613\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n614\t# status / validate\n615\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n616\t\n617\tdef _cmd_status(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n618\t    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n619\t    if not resolved:\n620\t        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n621\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n622\t    path = Path(resolved)\n623\t    try:\n624\t        obj = _load_json_file(path)\n625\t    except LocalRelayError as exc:\n626\t        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n627\t        return EXIT_USAGE if str(exc).startswith(\"no such file\") else EXIT_INVALID\n628\t    errors = validate_relay_object(obj) if isinstance(obj, dict) else [\"must be a JSON object\"]\n629\t    entries = obj.get(\"entries\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None\n630\t    last = entries[-1] if isinstance(entries, list) and entries and isinstance(entries[-1], dict) else {}\n631\t    print(json.dumps({\n632\t        \"valid\": not errors,\n633\t        \"errors\": errors,\n634\t        \"id\": obj.get(\"id\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n635\t        \"movement\": obj.get(\"movement\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n636\t        \"status\": obj.get(\"status\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n637\t        \"next_actor\": obj.get(\"next_actor\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n638\t        \"entry_count\": len(entries) if isinstance(entries, list) else 0,\n639\t        \"last_marker\": last.get(\"marker\"),\n640\t        \"last_actor\": last.get(\"actor\"),\n641\t        \"last_timestamp\": last.get(\"timestamp\"),\n642\t    }, sort_keys=True))\n643\t    return EXIT_OK\n644\t\n645\t\n646\tdef _cmd_validate(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n647\t    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n648\t    if not resolved:\n649\t        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n650\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n651\t    path = Path(resolved)\n652\t    try:\n653\t        obj = _load_json_file(path)\n654\t    except LocalRelayError as exc:\n655\t        if str(exc).startswith(\"no such file\"):\n656\t            print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n657\t            return EXIT_USAGE\n658\t        print(json.dumps({\"valid\": False, \"errors\": [str(exc)]}))\n659\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n660\t    errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n661\t    if isinstance(obj, dict) and not _id_matches_filename(obj.get(\"id\", \"\"), path):\n662\t        errors.append(f\"id {obj.get('id')!r} does not match filename {path.name!r}\")\n663\t    print(json.dumps({\"valid\": not errors, \"errors\": errors}, sort_keys=True))\n664\t    return EXIT_OK if not errors else EXIT_INVALID\n665\t\n666\t\n667\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n668\t# watch\n669\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n670\t\n671\tdef _cmd_watch(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n672\t    \"\"\"Bounded, blocking, read-only poll of `--file`'s `next_actor` field.\n673\t    Never a daemon (AC-2): `--timeout` has a hard ceiling and this function\n674\t    always returns once it elapses. Never writes (AC-3): every filesystem\n675\t    touch below is a read.\"\"\"\n676\t    if args.interval < WATCH_INTERVAL_FLOOR:\n677\t        print(f\"error: --interval must be at least {WATCH_INTERVAL_FLOOR} seconds\", file=sys.stderr)\n678\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n679\t    if args.timeout > WATCH_TIMEOUT_CEILING:\n680\t        print(f\"error: --timeout must be at most {WATCH_TIMEOUT_CEILING} seconds\", file=sys.stderr)\n681\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n682\t\n683\t    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n684\t    if not resolved:\n685\t        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n686\t        return EXIT_USAGE\n687\t    path = Path(resolved)\n688\t    try:\n689\t        obj = _load_json_file(path)\n690\t    except LocalRelayError as exc:\n691\t        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n692\t        return EXIT_USAGE if str(exc).startswith(\"no such file\") else EXIT_INVALID\n693\t    errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n694\t    if errors:\n695\t        print(f\"error: {path} fails validation, refusing to watch: {'; '.join(errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n696\t        return EXIT_INVALID\n697\t\n698\t    baseline = len(obj[\"entries\"])\n699\t    deadline = time.monotonic() + args.timeout\n700\t\n701\t    while True:\n702\t        if obj.get(\"next_actor\") == args.for_role:\n703\t            new_entries = [e for e in obj[\"entries\"] if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"seq\", 0) > baseline]\n704\t            print(json.dumps({\"next_actor\": args.for_role, \"entries\": new_entries}, sort_keys=True))\n705\t            return EXIT_OK\n706\t        remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()\n707\t        if remaining <= 0:\n708\t            return EXIT_TIMEOUT\n709\t        time.sleep(min(args.interval, remaining))\n710\t        try:\n711\t            obj = _load_json_file(path)\n712\t        except LocalRelayError:\n713\t            continue  # transient read failure -- try again next iteration, still bounded by deadline\n714\t\n715\t\n716\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n717\t# CLI\n718\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n719\t\n720\tdef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n721\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"local_relay\", description=__doc__)\n722\t    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n723\t\n724\t    p_create = sub.add_parser(\"create\", help=\"open a new relay file with a SESSION_START entry\")\n725\t    p_create.add_argument(\"--start\", required=True, help=\"bare SESSION_START packet JSON file, or - for stdin\")\n726\t    p_create.add_argument(\"--role\", required=True, choices=ROLES)\n727\t    p_create.add_argument(\"--dir\", default=None,\n728\t                           help=f\"defaults to {ENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR} if set, else 'relay'\")\n729\t    p_create.add_argument(\"--slug\", default=None)\n730\t    p_create.set_defaults(func=_cmd_create)\n731\t\n732\t    p_append = sub.add_parser(\"append\", help=\"append one entry; rejected if it is not --role's turn\")\n733\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None,\n734\t                           help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n735\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--role\", required=True, choices=ROLES)\n736\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--marker\", required=True, choices=APPENDABLE_MARKERS)\n737\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--subject\", default=None)\n738\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--text\", default=None)\n739\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--report\", default=None, help=\"SESSION_CLOSE only: bare report JSON file, or -\")\n740\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--outcome\", default=None, choices=gst.OUTCOMES)\n741\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--authorized-by\", dest=\"authorized_by\", default=None)\n742\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--scope\", default=None)\n743\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--supersedes\", default=None)\n744\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--next\", default=None, choices=ROLES)\n745\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--close\", action=\"store_true\")\n746\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--good-to-go\", dest=\"good_to_go\", action=\"store_true\")\n747\t    p_append.add_argument(\"--in-progress\", dest=\"in_progress\", action=\"store_true\")\n748\t    p_append.set_defaults(func=_cmd_append)\n749\t\n750\t    p_status = sub.add_parser(\"status\", help=\"read-only summary of one relay file\")\n751\t    p_status.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None, help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n752\t    p_status.set_defaults(func=_cmd_status)\n753\t\n754\t    p_validate = sub.add_parser(\"validate\", help=\"schema-check one relay file\")\n755\t    p_validate.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None, help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n756\t    p_validate.set_defaults(func=_cmd_validate)\n757\t\n758\t    p_watch = sub.add_parser(\"watch\", help=\"bounded, read-only poll for next_actor to flip to --for\")\n759\t    p_watch.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None, help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n760\t    p_watch.add_argument(\"--for\", dest=\"for_role\", required=True, choices=ROLES)\n761\t    p_watch.add_argument(\"--interval\", type=int, default=WATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT)\n762\t    p_watch.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=WATCH_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT)\n763\t    p_watch.set_defaults(func=_cmd_watch)\n764\t\n765\t    return parser\n766\t\n767\t\n768\tdef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n769\t    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)\n770\t    return args.func(args)\n771\t\n772\t\n773\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n774\t    sys.exit(main())\n775\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a8dd4a7-31e7-434f-89b1-73b3ad9d3b22","uuid":"1d7286b2-86f8-40c5-bca3-5d897cee41a0","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:07:58.386Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/OzanDur/Codo/neXus-nexus-worktrees/NXS-LOCAL-0021/scripts/local_relay.py","content":"\"\"\"GOV.PO.1 -- local, file-based relay transport (stdlib only).\n\n    py scripts/local_relay.py create   --role {po|engineer} --start FILE|- [--dir relay] [--slug SLUG]\n    py scripts/local_relay.py append   --file FILE --role {po|engineer} --marker MARKER [...]\n    py scripts/local_relay.py status   --file FILE\n    py scripts/local_relay.py validate --file FILE\n    py scripts/local_relay.py watch    --file FILE --for {po|engineer}\n                                        [--interval SECONDS] [--timeout SECONDS]\n\nFull contract: docs/design/LOCAL_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md (DRAFT). This is an\nADDITIONAL transport for same-machine, same-checkout Product-Owner/engineer\ncoordination -- it does not amend or replace\ndocs/design/NEXUS_AGENT_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md or the GitHub-based\n`RELAY_READY owner/repository#issue` workflow, which stay exactly as they\nare for cross-machine or human-external-visibility work.\n\nOne tracked JSON file per movement under `relay/`\n(`relay/NXS-LOCAL-<4-digit-id>-<slug>.json`), an append-only `entries`\narray reusing `NEXUS_AGENT_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md`'s five markers\n(`RELAY_ACK`/`RELAY_NOTE`/`RELAY_QUESTION`/`RELAY_DECISION`/\n`RELAY_CORRECTION`) plus `GOV.SESSION.1`'s two packet types\n(`SESSION_START`/`SESSION_CLOSE`), and a top-level `next_actor` field\n(`\"po\"`/`\"engineer\"`/`null`) enforcing single-writer-at-a-time turn\nownership: `append --role <r>` is rejected unless `<r>` equals the file's\ncurrent `next_actor`.\n\nThis module imports `scripts/gov_session_transfer.py` (same directory) to\nvalidate `SESSION_START`/`SESSION_CLOSE` `report` objects against its\nexisting, unchanged schema (`_REPORT_SCHEMA_BY_TYPE`, `_validate_node`,\n`OUTCOMES`) -- reused directly, never re-derived, so the two transports can\nnever drift into two different ideas of what a valid report looks like.\n\n`watch` is a bounded, blocking, read-only poll of one relay file's\n`next_actor` field -- never a background daemon (a hard `--timeout`\nceiling makes that impossible by construction). It never writes, appends,\nor mutates the watched file; a detected `next_actor` flip is only ever\nreported to the invoking session, which still needs the human's explicit\nwritten authorization before acting on any `RELAY_DECISION`-class content,\nexactly as today.\n\nCanonical-location resolver (GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md,\nFROZEN, section 3.6): a git worktree checks out its own copy of `relay/`,\nso a bare relative `--file`/`--dir` argument resolved against an engineer\nworktree's own cwd would silently read/write that worktree's copy instead\nof the one physical file the Product Owner's session reads -- never the\nlive channel. Two environment variables let a caller omit `--dir`/`--file`\nentirely and always resolve to the one canonical location the orchestrator\nsets when it spawns an engineer process, with no change to behavior when\nneither is set (today's cwd-relative default, unchanged byte-for-byte):\n`NEXUS_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR` (an absolute path) is `create`'s `--dir`\ndefault when `--dir` is omitted; `NEXUS_RELAY_FILE` (an absolute path to\none exact relay file) is `append`/`status`/`validate`/`watch`'s `--file`\ndefault when `--file` is omitted. An explicit `--dir`/`--file` argument\nalways wins over either variable.\n\nShared append lock: `append`'s existing optimistic re-read-and-compare\n(below) never corrupts or silently loses an entry, but leaves a losing\nconcurrent writer to be retried by whoever called it -- fine when a human\nis present, not when the orchestrator and an unattended engineer process\ncan both legitimately touch the same canonical file for the same movement\nwhile both are alive. `append` now wraps its whole read-validate-build-\nwrite sequence in a real advisory file lock (`fcntl.flock` on POSIX,\n`msvcrt.locking` on Windows -- stdlib only, no third-party dependency) on\na sidecar `<file>.lock`, bounded by a wait timeout; the existing hash\ncompare stays as defense-in-depth underneath it, unchanged.\n\nOffline, synchronous. No network, daemon, credential, or device access.\nExit codes: 0 success, 1 invalid/rejected (schema violation, wrong-turn\nappend, concurrent-write conflict, append to a CLOSED movement), 2 usage\nerror (bad arguments, missing file, an out-of-range `watch` `--interval`/\n`--timeout`), 3 `watch` timed out with no qualifying `next_actor` change --\nthe same convention `gov_session_transfer.py` uses, extended with 3 for\n`watch` only.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport gov_session_transfer as gst  # noqa: E402\n\ntry:\n    import fcntl as _fcntl\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- Windows\n    _fcntl = None\ntry:\n    import msvcrt as _msvcrt\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover -- POSIX\n    _msvcrt = None\n\nEXIT_OK, EXIT_INVALID, EXIT_USAGE, EXIT_TIMEOUT = 0, 1, 2, 3\n\n#: GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md section 3.6: an absolute\n#: canonical relay directory / exact relay file, set by the orchestrator in\n#: every engineer process it spawns so every worktree resolves to the one\n#: physical location the Product Owner's own session reads -- never a\n#: per-worktree copy. Unset in every session that does not opt in (the\n#: Product Owner's own interactive session, today); default behavior is\n#: then byte-for-byte unchanged from before this variable existed.\nENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR = \"NEXUS_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR\"\nENV_RELAY_FILE = \"NEXUS_RELAY_FILE\"\n\n#: How long `append` waits for the shared file lock before giving up.\n#: Module-level so tests can shrink it rather than waiting out the real\n#: default against a genuinely held lock.\nAPPEND_LOCK_TIMEOUT = 30.0\n\n#: `watch` bounds (AC-1/AC-2): a floor on --interval and a ceiling on\n#: --timeout so it can never approximate an unbounded background daemon.\nWATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT = 20\nWATCH_INTERVAL_FLOOR = 5\nWATCH_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT = 1800\nWATCH_TIMEOUT_CEILING = 3600\n\nSCHEMA_VERSION = 1\nID_PREFIX = \"NXS-LOCAL-\"\nID_RE = re.compile(r\"^NXS-LOCAL-(\\d{4})$\")\nFILENAME_RE = re.compile(r\"^(NXS-LOCAL-\\d{4})-[a-z0-9-]+\\.json$\")\n\nROLES = (\"po\", \"engineer\")\nSTATUSES = (\"OPEN\", \"IN_PROGRESS\", \"AWAITING_PO\", \"AWAITING_ENGINEER\", \"CLOSED\")\n\n#: The two GOV.SESSION.1 packet types plus NEXUS_AGENT_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md's\n#: five intermediate markers -- seven total, closed, reused verbatim.\nRELAY_MARKERS = (\"RELAY_ACK\", \"RELAY_NOTE\", \"RELAY_QUESTION\", \"RELAY_DECISION\", \"RELAY_CORRECTION\")\nMARKERS = (\"SESSION_START\", \"SESSION_CLOSE\") + RELAY_MARKERS\n#: Every marker except SESSION_START may be appended -- SESSION_START only\n#: ever exists as entries[0], written by `create`.\nAPPENDABLE_MARKERS = (\"SESSION_CLOSE\",) + RELAY_MARKERS\n#: Markers whose only required fields are `subject`/`text` (RELAY_DECISION\n#: additionally requires authorized_by/scope/supersedes; SESSION_CLOSE\n#: requires report/outcome instead).\nNARRATIVE_MARKERS = (\"RELAY_ACK\", \"RELAY_NOTE\", \"RELAY_QUESTION\", \"RELAY_CORRECTION\")\n\n_COMMON_ENTRY_FIELDS = {\n    \"marker\": (\"enum\", frozenset(MARKERS)),\n    \"actor\": (\"enum\", frozenset(ROLES)),\n    \"timestamp\": (\"str\",),\n}\n\n\ndef _entry_schema(extra: dict) -> tuple:\n    return (\"obj\", {**_COMMON_ENTRY_FIELDS, **extra})\n\n\n#: One closed-shape schema per marker (gov_session_transfer.py's own generic\n#: tuple-based schema kinds, reused directly -- see module docstring).\nENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER = {\n    \"SESSION_START\": _entry_schema({\"report\": gst.SESSION_START_REPORT_SCHEMA}),\n    \"SESSION_CLOSE\": _entry_schema({\"report\": gst.SESSION_CLOSE_REPORT_SCHEMA, \"outcome\": (\"enum\", gst.OUTCOMES)}),\n    \"RELAY_DECISION\": _entry_schema({\n        \"subject\": (\"str\",), \"text\": (\"str\",),\n        \"authorized_by\": (\"str\",), \"scope\": (\"str\",), \"supersedes\": (\"str\",),\n    }),\n}\nfor _marker in (\"RELAY_ACK\", \"RELAY_NOTE\", \"RELAY_QUESTION\", \"RELAY_CORRECTION\"):\n    ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER[_marker] = _entry_schema({\"subject\": (\"str\",), \"text\": (\"str\",)})\n\nTOP_LEVEL_FIELDS = {\n    \"schema_version\", \"id\", \"movement\", \"refs\", \"status\", \"next_actor\",\n    \"created_at\", \"updated_at\", \"entries\",\n}\n\n\nclass LocalRelayError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"A CLI-level request could not be satisfied (bad input, wrong turn,\n    a closed movement, or a concurrent-write conflict).\"\"\"\n\n\ndef _utc_now_iso() -> str:\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\")\n\n\ndef _slugify(text: str) -> str:\n    slug = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"-\", text.strip().lower()).strip(\"-\")\n    return (slug or \"movement\")[:40]\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Structural validation (pure -- no filesystem access)\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _validate_entry(entry: Any, index: int, errors: list[str]) -> None:\n    path = f\"entries[{index}]\"\n    if not isinstance(entry, dict):\n        errors.append(f\"{path}: must be an object\")\n        return\n    marker = entry.get(\"marker\")\n    if marker not in ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER:\n        errors.append(f\"{path}.marker: must be one of {sorted(ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER)}\")\n        return\n    working = dict(entry)\n    seq = working.pop(\"seq\", None)\n    good_to_go = working.pop(\"good_to_go\", None)\n    if seq != index + 1 or isinstance(seq, bool) or not isinstance(seq, int):\n        errors.append(f\"{path}.seq: must equal {index + 1}\")\n    if good_to_go is not None and not isinstance(good_to_go, bool):\n        errors.append(f\"{path}.good_to_go: must be a boolean\")\n    gst._validate_node(working, ENTRY_SCHEMA_BY_MARKER[marker], path, errors)\n\n\ndef _validate_shape_and_order(entries: list, errors: list[str]) -> None:\n    if not entries:\n        errors.append(\"entries: must be a non-empty list\")\n        return\n    if not (isinstance(entries[0], dict) and entries[0].get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_START\"):\n        errors.append(\"entries[0].marker: must be SESSION_START\")\n    starts = sum(1 for e in entries if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_START\")\n    if starts != 1:\n        errors.append(f\"entries: exactly one SESSION_START required, found {starts}\")\n    for i, entry in enumerate(entries):\n        if isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_START\" and i != 0:\n            errors.append(f\"entries[{i}]: SESSION_START may only appear at position 0\")\n        if isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" and i != len(entries) - 1:\n            errors.append(f\"entries[{i}]: SESSION_CLOSE may only be the last entry\")\n    closes = sum(1 for e in entries if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_CLOSE\")\n    if closes > 1:\n        errors.append(f\"entries: at most one SESSION_CLOSE allowed, found {closes}\")\n\n\ndef _validate_turn_state(obj: dict, errors: list[str]) -> None:\n    entries = obj.get(\"entries\")\n    if not isinstance(entries, list) or not entries or not isinstance(entries[-1], dict):\n        return  # already reported by _validate_shape_and_order\n    last = entries[-1]\n    next_actor = obj.get(\"next_actor\")\n    status = obj.get(\"status\")\n    closed = last.get(\"marker\") == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" or next_actor is None\n    if closed:\n        if next_actor is not None:\n            errors.append(\"next_actor: must be null once the movement is closed\")\n        if status != \"CLOSED\":\n            errors.append(f\"status: must be CLOSED when next_actor is null, got {status!r}\")\n        return\n    if next_actor not in ROLES:\n        errors.append(f\"next_actor: must be 'po', 'engineer', or null when CLOSED, got {next_actor!r}\")\n        return\n    if len(entries) == 1:\n        if status != \"OPEN\":\n            errors.append(f\"status: must be OPEN with only the SESSION_START entry present, got {status!r}\")\n        return\n    expected = \"AWAITING_PO\" if next_actor == \"po\" else \"AWAITING_ENGINEER\"\n    if status not in (expected, \"IN_PROGRESS\"):\n        errors.append(f\"status: must be {expected} or IN_PROGRESS when next_actor is {next_actor!r}, got {status!r}\")\n\n\ndef validate_relay_object(obj: Any) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Structural + internal-consistency validation of one relay file's\n    already-parsed JSON object. Pure -- takes no filesystem path, proves\n    shape and internal consistency, never that a filename matches `id`\n    (the CLI layer checks that separately, where it has a real path).\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(obj, dict):\n        return [\"must be a JSON object\"]\n\n    errors: list[str] = []\n    for field in sorted(set(obj) - TOP_LEVEL_FIELDS):\n        errors.append(f\"{field}: unknown top-level field\")\n    missing = TOP_LEVEL_FIELDS - set(obj)\n    for field in sorted(missing):\n        errors.append(f\"{field}: missing required field\")\n\n    # Only type-check a field that is actually present -- an absent field\n    # was already reported above; re-checking its (nonexistent) type would\n    # just double-report the same defect under two messages.\n    if \"schema_version\" in obj and obj[\"schema_version\"] != SCHEMA_VERSION:\n        errors.append(f\"schema_version: must be {SCHEMA_VERSION}\")\n    if \"id\" in obj and not (isinstance(obj[\"id\"], str) and ID_RE.match(obj[\"id\"])):\n        errors.append(f\"id: must match {ID_RE.pattern}\")\n    if \"movement\" in obj and not (isinstance(obj[\"movement\"], str) and obj[\"movement\"]):\n        errors.append(\"movement: must be a non-empty string\")\n    if \"refs\" in obj:\n        gst._validate_node(obj[\"refs\"], (\"list_str\", True), \"refs\", errors)\n    if \"status\" in obj and obj[\"status\"] not in STATUSES:\n        errors.append(f\"status: must be one of {STATUSES}\")\n    for field in (\"created_at\", \"updated_at\"):\n        if field in obj and not (isinstance(obj[field], str) and obj[field]):\n            errors.append(f\"{field}: must be a non-empty string\")\n\n    if \"entries\" in obj:\n        entries = obj[\"entries\"]\n        if not isinstance(entries, list):\n            errors.append(\"entries: must be a list\")\n        else:\n            _validate_shape_and_order(entries, errors)\n            for i, entry in enumerate(entries):\n                _validate_entry(entry, i, errors)\n\n    if not ({\"next_actor\", \"status\", \"entries\"} & missing):\n        _validate_turn_state(obj, errors)\n    return errors\n\n\ndef _id_matches_filename(obj_id: str, path: Path) -> bool:\n    match = FILENAME_RE.match(path.name)\n    return bool(match) and match.group(1) == obj_id\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Filesystem helpers\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _next_id(relay_dir: Path) -> int:\n    if not relay_dir.is_dir():\n        return 1\n    best = 0\n    for candidate in relay_dir.glob(f\"{ID_PREFIX}*.json\"):\n        match = re.match(r\"^NXS-LOCAL-(\\d{4})-\", candidate.name)\n        if match:\n            best = max(best, int(match.group(1)))\n    return best + 1\n\n\ndef _resolve_relay_dir(explicit: str | None) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"`create --dir`'s effective value: the explicit flag always wins;\n    otherwise `NEXUS_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR` when set; otherwise today's\n    unchanged cwd-relative default.\"\"\"\n    return Path(explicit or os.environ.get(ENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR) or \"relay\")\n\n\ndef _resolve_relay_file(explicit: str | None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"`append`/`status`/`validate`/`watch --file`'s effective value: the\n    explicit flag always wins; otherwise `NEXUS_RELAY_FILE` when set;\n    otherwise None (caller reports a usage error, exactly as an absent\n    required argument would have before this resolver existed).\"\"\"\n    return explicit or os.environ.get(ENV_RELAY_FILE)\n\n\ndef _dump(obj: dict) -> str:\n    return json.dumps(obj, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef _atomic_write(path: Path, text: str) -> None:\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    fd, tmp_name = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=str(path.parent), prefix=f\".{path.name}.\", suffix=\".tmp\")\n    try:\n        with os.fdopen(fd, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            fh.write(text)\n        os.replace(tmp_name, path)\n    except BaseException:\n        try:\n            os.unlink(tmp_name)\n        except OSError:\n            pass\n        raise\n\n\nclass FileLockTimeout(LocalRelayError):\n    \"\"\"A real advisory lock on a relay file could not be acquired in time --\n    a genuinely concurrent writer (not merely the wrong-turn/hash checks\n    above) is holding it.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass _FileLock:\n    \"\"\"Real, cross-platform (stdlib-only) advisory exclusive lock on a\n    sidecar `<path>.lock` file, bounded by `timeout` seconds. `fcntl.flock`\n    on POSIX, `msvcrt.locking` on Windows; degrades to a no-op (documented,\n    not silent -- see module docstring) on a platform with neither, which\n    leaves the existing optimistic hash-compare in `append` as the only\n    concurrency guard, exactly as before this class existed.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, target: Path, timeout: float = 30.0) -> None:\n        self._lock_path = Path(str(target) + \".lock\")\n        self._timeout = timeout\n        self._fh = None\n\n    def __enter__(self) -> \"_FileLock\":\n        self._lock_path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        self._fh = open(self._lock_path, \"a+b\")\n        deadline = time.monotonic() + self._timeout\n        while True:\n            try:\n                if _fcntl is not None:\n                    _fcntl.flock(self._fh.fileno(), _fcntl.LOCK_EX | _fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n                elif _msvcrt is not None:\n                    self._fh.seek(0)\n                    _msvcrt.locking(self._fh.fileno(), _msvcrt.LK_NBLCK, 1)\n                else:  # pragma: no cover -- no known stdlib primitive on this platform\n                    break\n                return self\n            except OSError:\n                if time.monotonic() >= deadline:\n                    self._fh.close()\n                    raise FileLockTimeout(\n                        f\"could not acquire lock {self._lock_path} within {self._timeout}s\")\n                time.sleep(0.05)\n\n    def __exit__(self, *exc_info: object) -> None:\n        try:\n            if _fcntl is not None:\n                _fcntl.flock(self._fh.fileno(), _fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n            elif _msvcrt is not None:  # pragma: no cover -- exercised on Windows only\n                self._fh.seek(0)\n                _msvcrt.locking(self._fh.fileno(), _msvcrt.LK_UNLCK, 1)\n        finally:\n            self._fh.close()\n\n\ndef _load_json_file(path: Path) -> Any:\n    if not path.is_file():\n        raise LocalRelayError(f\"no such file: {path}\")\n    try:\n        return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        raise LocalRelayError(f\"invalid JSON: {exc}\") from exc\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# create\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _cmd_create(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    try:\n        raw = gst._read_input(args.start)\n    except gst.PacketError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    try:\n        start_obj = json.loads(raw)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: invalid JSON: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    if start_obj.get(\"message_type\") is None:\n        start_obj = dict(start_obj)\n        start_obj.setdefault(\"protocol_version\", 2)\n        start_obj.setdefault(\"message_type\", \"SESSION_START\")\n    errors = gst.validate_fields(start_obj)\n    if start_obj.get(\"message_type\") != \"SESSION_START\":\n        errors.append(\"message_type: must be SESSION_START (local relay files always open with one)\")\n    if errors:\n        print(f\"error: {'; '.join(errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    relay_dir = _resolve_relay_dir(args.dir)\n    next_id = _next_id(relay_dir)\n    full_id = f\"{ID_PREFIX}{next_id:04d}\"\n    slug = _slugify(args.slug or start_obj[\"movement\"])\n    target = relay_dir / f\"{full_id}-{slug}.json\"\n    if target.exists():\n        print(f\"error: {target} already exists\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    now = _utc_now_iso()\n    other_role = \"engineer\" if args.role == \"po\" else \"po\"\n    file_obj = {\n        \"schema_version\": SCHEMA_VERSION,\n        \"id\": full_id,\n        \"movement\": start_obj[\"movement\"],\n        \"refs\": start_obj[\"refs\"],\n        \"status\": \"OPEN\",\n        \"next_actor\": other_role,\n        \"created_at\": now,\n        \"updated_at\": now,\n        \"entries\": [{\n            \"seq\": 1, \"marker\": \"SESSION_START\", \"actor\": args.role,\n            \"timestamp\": now, \"report\": start_obj[\"report\"],\n        }],\n    }\n    internal_errors = validate_relay_object(file_obj)\n    if internal_errors:  # pragma: no cover -- defensive; construction above should always be valid\n        print(f\"error: internal consistency check failed: {'; '.join(internal_errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    _atomic_write(target, _dump(file_obj))\n    print(str(target))\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# append\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _build_entry(args: argparse.Namespace, seq: int, timestamp: str) -> tuple[dict | None, str | None]:\n    marker = args.marker\n    entry: dict[str, Any] = {\"seq\": seq, \"marker\": marker, \"actor\": args.role, \"timestamp\": timestamp}\n    if args.good_to_go:\n        entry[\"good_to_go\"] = True\n\n    if marker == \"SESSION_CLOSE\":\n        if not args.report:\n            return None, \"--report is required for SESSION_CLOSE\"\n        try:\n            report_obj = json.loads(gst._read_input(args.report))\n        except gst.PacketError as exc:\n            return None, str(exc)\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n            return None, f\"--report is not valid JSON: {exc}\"\n        if not args.outcome:\n            return None, \"--outcome is required for SESSION_CLOSE\"\n        report_errors: list[str] = []\n        gst._validate_node(report_obj, gst.SESSION_CLOSE_REPORT_SCHEMA, \"report\", report_errors)\n        if report_errors:\n            return None, \"; \".join(report_errors)\n        entry[\"report\"] = report_obj\n        entry[\"outcome\"] = args.outcome\n        return entry, None\n\n    subject = args.subject or (\"good to go\" if args.good_to_go else None)\n    text = args.text or (\"good to go\" if args.good_to_go else None)\n    if not subject or not text:\n        return None, \"--subject and --text are required (or pass --good-to-go for the fast path)\"\n    entry[\"subject\"] = subject\n    entry[\"text\"] = text\n\n    if marker == \"RELAY_DECISION\":\n        for field, value in ((\"authorized_by\", args.authorized_by), (\"scope\", args.scope), (\"supersedes\", args.supersedes)):\n            if not value:\n                return None, f\"--{field.replace('_', '-')} is required for RELAY_DECISION\"\n        entry[\"authorized_by\"] = args.authorized_by\n        entry[\"scope\"] = args.scope\n        entry[\"supersedes\"] = args.supersedes\n    elif marker not in NARRATIVE_MARKERS:\n        return None, f\"{marker} cannot be appended (SESSION_START only via create)\"\n\n    return entry, None\n\n\ndef _cmd_append(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n    if not resolved:\n        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    path = Path(resolved)\n    try:\n        with _FileLock(path, timeout=APPEND_LOCK_TIMEOUT):\n            return _cmd_append_locked(args, path)\n    except FileLockTimeout as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n\ndef _cmd_append_locked(args: argparse.Namespace, path: Path) -> int:\n    try:\n        raw_before = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: no such file: {path} ({exc})\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    try:\n        obj = json.loads(raw_before)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {path} is not valid JSON: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n    if not _id_matches_filename(obj.get(\"id\", \"\"), path):\n        errors.append(f\"id {obj.get('id')!r} does not match filename {path.name!r}\")\n    if errors:\n        print(f\"error: {path} fails validation, refusing to append: {'; '.join(errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    if obj[\"status\"] == \"CLOSED\":\n        print(f\"error: {path} is CLOSED; no further entries may be appended\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    if obj[\"next_actor\"] != args.role:\n        print(f\"error: not {args.role}'s turn (next_actor is {obj['next_actor']!r})\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    if args.marker not in APPENDABLE_MARKERS:\n        print(f\"error: {args.marker} cannot be appended (SESSION_START only via create)\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    if args.close and args.in_progress:\n        print(\"error: --close and --in-progress are mutually exclusive\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    if args.marker != \"SESSION_CLOSE\" and not args.close and not args.next:\n        print(\"error: --next {po|engineer} is required unless --close is passed\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    if args.marker == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" and (args.next or args.close):\n        print(\"error: --next/--close are redundant with SESSION_CLOSE, which always closes\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n\n    now = _utc_now_iso()\n    entry, build_error = _build_entry(args, len(obj[\"entries\"]) + 1, now)\n    if build_error:\n        print(f\"error: {build_error}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    closing = args.marker == \"SESSION_CLOSE\" or args.close\n    obj[\"entries\"].append(entry)\n    obj[\"updated_at\"] = now\n    if closing:\n        obj[\"next_actor\"] = None\n        obj[\"status\"] = \"CLOSED\"\n    else:\n        obj[\"next_actor\"] = args.next\n        obj[\"status\"] = \"IN_PROGRESS\" if args.in_progress else (\"AWAITING_PO\" if args.next == \"po\" else \"AWAITING_ENGINEER\")\n\n    internal_errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n    if internal_errors:  # pragma: no cover -- defensive; construction above should always be valid\n        print(f\"error: internal consistency check failed: {'; '.join(internal_errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    try:\n        raw_now = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: file disappeared before write: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    if raw_now != raw_before:\n        print(f\"error: {path} changed since it was read -- a concurrent write occurred; \"\n              f\"re-run against the latest state\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    _atomic_write(path, _dump(obj))\n    print(json.dumps({\"status\": obj[\"status\"], \"next_actor\": obj[\"next_actor\"], \"seq\": entry[\"seq\"]}))\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# status / validate\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _cmd_status(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n    if not resolved:\n        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    path = Path(resolved)\n    try:\n        obj = _load_json_file(path)\n    except LocalRelayError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE if str(exc).startswith(\"no such file\") else EXIT_INVALID\n    errors = validate_relay_object(obj) if isinstance(obj, dict) else [\"must be a JSON object\"]\n    entries = obj.get(\"entries\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None\n    last = entries[-1] if isinstance(entries, list) and entries and isinstance(entries[-1], dict) else {}\n    print(json.dumps({\n        \"valid\": not errors,\n        \"errors\": errors,\n        \"id\": obj.get(\"id\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n        \"movement\": obj.get(\"movement\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n        \"status\": obj.get(\"status\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n        \"next_actor\": obj.get(\"next_actor\") if isinstance(obj, dict) else None,\n        \"entry_count\": len(entries) if isinstance(entries, list) else 0,\n        \"last_marker\": last.get(\"marker\"),\n        \"last_actor\": last.get(\"actor\"),\n        \"last_timestamp\": last.get(\"timestamp\"),\n    }, sort_keys=True))\n    return EXIT_OK\n\n\ndef _cmd_validate(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n    if not resolved:\n        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    path = Path(resolved)\n    try:\n        obj = _load_json_file(path)\n    except LocalRelayError as exc:\n        if str(exc).startswith(\"no such file\"):\n            print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return EXIT_USAGE\n        print(json.dumps({\"valid\": False, \"errors\": [str(exc)]}))\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n    errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n    if isinstance(obj, dict) and not _id_matches_filename(obj.get(\"id\", \"\"), path):\n        errors.append(f\"id {obj.get('id')!r} does not match filename {path.name!r}\")\n    print(json.dumps({\"valid\": not errors, \"errors\": errors}, sort_keys=True))\n    return EXIT_OK if not errors else EXIT_INVALID\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# watch\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _cmd_watch(args: argparse.Namespace) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Bounded, blocking, read-only poll of `--file`'s `next_actor` field.\n    Never a daemon (AC-2): `--timeout` has a hard ceiling and this function\n    always returns once it elapses. Never writes (AC-3): every filesystem\n    touch below is a read.\"\"\"\n    if args.interval < WATCH_INTERVAL_FLOOR:\n        print(f\"error: --interval must be at least {WATCH_INTERVAL_FLOOR} seconds\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    if args.timeout > WATCH_TIMEOUT_CEILING:\n        print(f\"error: --timeout must be at most {WATCH_TIMEOUT_CEILING} seconds\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n\n    resolved = _resolve_relay_file(args.file)\n    if not resolved:\n        print(f\"error: --file is required (or set {ENV_RELAY_FILE})\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE\n    path = Path(resolved)\n    try:\n        obj = _load_json_file(path)\n    except LocalRelayError as exc:\n        print(f\"error: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_USAGE if str(exc).startswith(\"no such file\") else EXIT_INVALID\n    errors = validate_relay_object(obj)\n    if errors:\n        print(f\"error: {path} fails validation, refusing to watch: {'; '.join(errors)}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return EXIT_INVALID\n\n    baseline = len(obj[\"entries\"])\n    deadline = time.monotonic() + args.timeout\n\n    while True:\n        if obj.get(\"next_actor\") == args.for_role:\n            new_entries = [e for e in obj[\"entries\"] if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get(\"seq\", 0) > baseline]\n            print(json.dumps({\"next_actor\": args.for_role, \"entries\": new_entries}, sort_keys=True))\n            return EXIT_OK\n        remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            return EXIT_TIMEOUT\n        time.sleep(min(args.interval, remaining))\n        try:\n            obj = _load_json_file(path)\n        except LocalRelayError:\n            continue  # transient read failure -- try again next iteration, still bounded by deadline\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CLI\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"local_relay\", description=__doc__)\n    sub = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n\n    p_create = sub.add_parser(\"create\", help=\"open a new relay file with a SESSION_START entry\")\n    p_create.add_argument(\"--start\", required=True, help=\"bare SESSION_START packet JSON file, or - for stdin\")\n    p_create.add_argument(\"--role\", required=True, choices=ROLES)\n    p_create.add_argument(\"--dir\", default=None,\n                           help=f\"defaults to {ENV_CANONICAL_RELAY_DIR} if set, else 'relay'\")\n    p_create.add_argument(\"--slug\", default=None)\n    p_create.set_defaults(func=_cmd_create)\n\n    p_append = sub.add_parser(\"append\", help=\"append one entry; rejected if it is not --role's turn\")\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None,\n                           help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--role\", required=True, choices=ROLES)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--marker\", required=True, choices=APPENDABLE_MARKERS)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--subject\", default=None)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--text\", default=None)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--report\", default=None, help=\"SESSION_CLOSE only: bare report JSON file, or -\")\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--outcome\", default=None, choices=gst.OUTCOMES)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--authorized-by\", dest=\"authorized_by\", default=None)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--scope\", default=None)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--supersedes\", default=None)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--next\", default=None, choices=ROLES)\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--close\", action=\"store_true\")\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--good-to-go\", dest=\"good_to_go\", action=\"store_true\")\n    p_append.add_argument(\"--in-progress\", dest=\"in_progress\", action=\"store_true\")\n    p_append.set_defaults(func=_cmd_append)\n\n    p_status = sub.add_parser(\"status\", help=\"read-only summary of one relay file\")\n    p_status.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None, help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n    p_status.set_defaults(func=_cmd_status)\n\n    p_validate = sub.add_parser(\"validate\", help=\"schema-check one relay file\")\n    p_validate.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None, help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n    p_validate.set_defaults(func=_cmd_validate)\n\n    p_watch = sub.add_parser(\"watch\", help=\"bounded, read-only poll for next_actor to flip to --for\")\n    p_watch.add_argument(\"--file\", default=None, help=f\"defaults to {ENV_RELAY_FILE} if set\")\n    p_watch.add_argument(\"--for\", dest=\"for_role\", required=True, choices=ROLES)\n    p_watch.add_argument(\"--interval\", type=int, default=WATCH_INTERVAL_DEFAULT)\n    p_watch.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=WATCH_TIMEOUT_DEFAULT)\n    p_watch.set_defaults(func=_cmd_watch)\n\n    return parser\n\n\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n    args = build_parser().parse_args(argv)\n    return args.func(args)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":775,"startLine":1,"totalLines":775}}}
