 ClusterXL monitoring command); Evidence category F (link/control health) and/or the split-brain category. (2) SAFE RETAINED FIELDS ONLY -- the raw table carries per-interface IP addresses and MAC addresses: the parser must retain NO address, NO MAC, NO interface name; only bounded counts/booleans: number of cluster interfaces observed, number on which BOTH members are seen, number on which the peer member is absent, and whether the local member is seen on every required interface (cross-referenced only by count against CP-A4's `Required interfaces:`). Structural skeleton diagnostic applies if the shape is unrecognised. (3) READINESS MAPPING (PO decision, not to be invented): candidate checks are `no_split_brain` (peer absent on a required cluster interface = CCP not exchanged = election risk) and `control_sync_link_health` (per-interface CCP reachability, stronger than link state). The classification of 'peer row absent on a required interface' -- FAIL versus INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE -- must be decided against the frozen 'never KNOWN_BAD from absence' law: here the absence is inside the device's own positively-reported table, which is a different thing from a read that produced nothing, but the contract must say so explicitly before the code does. (4) VSX: physical/VS0 context only unless a per-VS semantic is separately established. (5) Tests: parser fail-closed on unknown shape; value-free retained fields (no IP/MAC survives); one call per member in the same shell; battery order and S4 command authority unchanged. Until this item is implemented, the readiness contract keeps its current (weaker) control-link evidence: link state, not CCP exchange.\"\n684-    },\n685-    {\n686-      \"id\": \"ha_entity_operational_lock\",\n687-      \"category\": \"Safety / Architecture\",\n688-      \"title\": \"Per-HA-entity operational lock -- the CLASS 2 lock grain does not exist\",\n689:      \"status\": \"done\",\n690-      \"priority\": \"P0 -- before CLASS 2\",\n691-      \"target\": \"OP.2.B (architecture FROZEN 2026-09-04 in docs/history/phase/OP_2_0_CONTROLLED_HA_OPERATION_ARCHITECTURE.md)\",\n(eval):1: == not found"}
