hand each time: op0b entry kept as the current/newest build, gov_po_3_resume_canonical_relay_access_fix (PR #130), m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers (PR #131) and m10_2_capability_state_resolver_core (PR #132) folded in as predecessors, INDEX.md regenerated via scripts/build_history_index.py, CURRENT_STATE.md kept <=200 lines). Full one-shot regression re-run after the final merge and the tooling fix: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto --dist worksteal` = 2943 passed, 25 skipped, 2 failed -- both pre-existing/unrelated (tests/test_dev_0_5b_auth_consumer_canonical_config.py's own DLP self-check false positive against project/build_history.json's own prose, documented since gov_po_1_local_relay_watch_command). S7+S6 both orders re-confirmed post-merge: 110 passed each. tests/test_architecture_convergence.py: 22 passed. scripts/build_history_index.py --check: up to date. git diff --check: clean.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"None for the S7/S6 fix itself. The interpreter-resolution fix is scoped to scripts/nexus_engineer_tool_gate.py's merge-lock re-validation call sites only, per the PO's own authorization (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0016 seq 3); it does not touch the hook's other sys.executable use (the merge-lock acquire/release orchestrator.py subprocess call), which was not reported broken and was left as-is.\"\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"m10_2_capability_state_resolver_core\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"M10.2 -- capability-state resolver core (stage 0, result algebra, primary ladder, qualifiers)\",\n  \"summary\": \"New utils/capability_state_resolver.py implements resolver stages 0-3 of docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md section 5, as pure typed-input functions with no I/O and no device contact: resolve_union_tag() decides the RESOLVED/OMITTED tag from D1 alone (Resolved and Omitted are structurally distinct dataclasses -- OMITTED carries only reason + optional diagnostic, never a None-filled capability output); evaluate_stage1()/evaluate_ri1_comparability() implement the CX1/RI-1/RI-2 contradiction-and-inconsistency gate, reusing utils.registry_evidence_reconciliation.detect_ri2 (M10.1) for RI-2 rather than reimplementing it, and the K1-K6 comparability precedence table for RI-1, in the frozen row order; resolve_primary_status() implements the twelve-rank primary ladder (ranks 0-11) first-match-wins; resolve_qualifiers() implements the seven independent CapabilityQualifier facets. The nine-value CapabilityState and seven-value CapabilityQualifier vocabularies are proven lexically disjoint from the console job lifecycle (X1), the OP.2 action-state vocabulary (X2) and utils.action_taxonomy tokens; to_wire() serializes only under the capability_state/capability_qualifiers keys the contract's namespacing rule (4.4) names.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"M10\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"SESSION_START relay/NXS-LOCAL-0008, dispatched into this movement's own git worktree; read docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md sections 3.3/4/5 in full before writing code, per the SESSION_START's own requirement. New tests/test_m10_2_capability_state_resolver.py (134 tests): stage 0's four union-tag cases V-A..V-D plus OMITTED/Resolved structural-distinctness checks (AC-1); exactly-nine/exactly-seven vocabulary checks plus lexical-disjointness parametrized tests against console/jobs.py TERMINAL_STATES, utils/operate/states.py ActionState and utils/action_taxonomy.py ACTION_CLASSES, plus a to_wire() namespacing test (AC-2); CX1 from I10, the full K1-K6 precedence table one row at a time plus two mixed-ordering cases, and RI-2 reuse via detect_ri2 (AC-3); one test per primary-ladder rank 0-11 plus the rank-8-vs-9 fail-closed-ordering case and a D5=POLICY_UNKNOWN-never-reaches-rank-11 case (AC-4); one test per qualifier plus the four 4.1.5 inference-ban negative test