al_relay.py`, which this per-tool directory allowlist does not gate -- nothing guaranteed a resumed session would route the same way. Fix (AC-3): `scripts/orchestrator.py::_spawn_engineer` now passes `--add-dir <canonical_relay_dir>` identically for a fresh dispatch and a resume, so access no longer depends on which tool a session happens to pick.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"GOV\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Relay relay/NXS-LOCAL-0015-resume-canonical-relay-access-fix.json, validated protocol-v2 SESSION_START. AC-4 real reproduction (not a simplified proxy): dispatched a throwaway scratch movement (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0017-gov-po-3-resume-fix-ac4-repro-postfix.json, now CLOSED) through the real `scripts/orchestrator.py` -- fresh dispatch posted RELAY_ACK+RELAY_QUESTION and exited; a RELAY_DECISION was posted; a real orchestrator resume (no simplified proxy) re-read the canonical relay file fresh from disk and quoted the RELAY_DECISION's subject verbatim in its own RELAY_NOTE, reproducing and closing the exact gap found live in relay/NXS-LOCAL-0012. AC-5 (no regression): fresh-dispatch access was exercised in the same real run and still works, and tests/test_orchestrator.py::test_spawn_engineer_grants_add_dir_for_the_canonical_relay_directory_on_fresh_dispatch asserts the fresh-dispatch argv shape explicitly. New tests/test_orchestrator.py (+2): fresh-dispatch and resume both get the identical `--add-dir <canonical_relay_dir>` grant, resume argv ending in `--resume <session_id>` unchanged otherwise. This branch reconciled two concurrent merges to origin/main during integration: relay/NXS-LOCAL-0013 (gov_po_3_orchestrator_observability, PR #129 -- both movements changed `_spawn_engineer`'s argv construction, reconciled by hand so `--add-dir` and `--output-format stream-json --verbose` coexist, and this movement's two tests updated to read the engineer process's own Popen call now that a second, summary-tailer Popen call is also made) and relay/NXS-LOCAL-0010 (m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers, PR #131 -- unrelated files, bookkeeping-only conflict). Full one-shot suite `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto --dist worksteal` (post-merge): 2699 passed, 25 skipped, 2 failed -- both pre-existing/unrelated (tests/test_dev_0_5b_auth_consumer_canonical_config.py's own DLP-collision self-check against repository prose, same documented false positive as prior builds). git diff --check clean.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"In passing, this movement's engineer session found (documented, NOT fixed here -- out of scope per this movement's own invariant against other orchestrator.py behavior changes): `scripts/orchestrator.py` never persists the real `claude` session_id (always None), so its 'resume' path never actually passes `--resume` to the `claude` CLI; it currently works only because a fresh re-spawn into the same worktree/branch behaves equivalently for this task shape. A follow-up movement should fix session-id persistence itself.\",\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"agreement\": \"scripts/orchestrator.py\"\n  }\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"M10.3 -- D2 entity-applicability and D3 vendor/platform-support producers\",\n  \"summary\": \"New utils/capability_applicability.py (resolve_d2) and utils/capability_vendor_support.py (resolve_d3): pure, offline, closed-table producers for CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md section 3.3 D2 (APPLICABLE/NOT_APPLICABLE/APPLICABILITY_UNKNOWN, from NAVIGATION_INFORMATION_ARCHITECTURE.md section 5.2's eight logical entity types) and D3 (SUPPORTED/UNSUPPORTED/SUPPORT_UNKNOWN, from real repository collector/adapter evidence). Every APPLICABLE/NOT_APPLICABLE/SUPPORTED entry cites its exact repository or doc source; every pair with no citable source resolves the UNKNOWN value naming the gap, never a guess (section 7.3, section 8.2 point 1). No UNSUPPORTED entry is populated: the review found no citable positive evidence of vendor non-support for any of the seven PCP.0 capabilities, only evidence of what is and is not yet implemented (utils/operate/adapter.py carries zero concrete vendor adapter and is the D3-cited input for controlled_operations; no telemetry or diagnostics producer exists anywhere) -- an absent producer is SUPPORT_UNKNOWN, never UNSUPPORTED, superseding PRODUCT_CONTROL_PLANE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 8's own informal worked-example wording. Neither module imports or extends utils/capability_registry.py.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"PRODUCT\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Branch feature/m10-3-entity-and-vendor-support-producers from origin/main. Read docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md sections 3.3 (D2, D3), 4 (vocabulary), 7.3 (positive-evidence rule), 8.2 (fail-closed/honest-unknown); docs/design/NAVIGATION_INFORMATION_ARCHITECTURE.md sections 5.2, 6.4, 7.2; docs/design/PRODUCT_CONTROL_PLANE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 8; docs/design/FAILOVER_ENGINE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 10.2; console/registry.py; application/cli.py; application/workflows/checkpoint.py; application/workflows/recovery.py; checkpoint/cp_runner.py, checkpoint/vsx_runner.py, checkpoint/checkpoint_recovery_collector.py; panorama/panorama_runtime_runner.py, panorama/panorama_recovery_collector.py; configuration/checkpoint_config_collector.py, configuration/panorama_config_collector.py; utils/failover/assessment.py; utils/operate/adapter.py -- before writing either table, per this movement's own requirements. D2's entity-applicability table: inventory/configuration_collection/backup APPLICABLE for all eight entity types (nav contract section 6.4, entity types: all); ha_readiness APPLICABLE for CP ClusterXL cluster/VSX host-cluster/virtual system (VSLS VSID)/