l_product_navigation availability_rule criterion stays 'pending' -- these are two of its predicates' producers, not the wiring that would move the criterion.\",\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"agreement\": \"docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md\"\n  }\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"gov_po_3_orchestrator_observability\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"GOV.PO.3 -- orchestrator observability: streaming engineer output + watch dashboard\",\n  \"summary\": \"Extends the already-frozen scripts/orchestrator.py (docs/design/GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md section 3.4) with real-time visibility: the engineer's claude -p invocation now streams stream-json output incrementally instead of only at process exit, a new dependency-free parser derives a human-readable engineer.summary.log alongside the raw log, orchestrator status gains a last_activity field, and a new read-only `orchestrator watch` terminal dashboard polls the same status data in a loop until Ctrl-C. Backward compatible with movements dispatched before this change.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"GOV\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Relay relay/NXS-LOCAL-0013-orchestrator-observability.json, validated protocol-v2 SESSION_START (Product Owner direction immediately after AC-3/AC-5 demonstration 1 of gov_po_3_approved_movement_orchestration_ac3 ran live and confirmed engineer.log stayed empty until process exit under the prior, non-streaming claude -p invocation -- a real, observed gap). Verified the exact flag spelling for real before coding, per this movement's own requirement: `claude -p --help` against the installed claude 2.1.263, and a live `claude -p ... --output-format stream-json` run without --verbose, which fails closed with 'Error: When using --print, --output-format=stream-json requires --verbose' -- confirming both flags are required together, not assumed from documentation. _spawn_engineer's argv now carries --output-format stream-json --verbose alongside the existing -p; a second, detached `_tail-summary` subprocess (an internal, undocumented CLI subcommand, never invoked directly) tails engineer.log from a byte offset, decodes and summarizes each complete line with a new stdlib-only, dependency-free parser (summarize_stream_json_line), and appends one line per event to a sibling engineer.summary.log -- a truncated last line at read time is left unconsumed and re-read once complete, never dropped or crashed on; an unrecognized-but-valid JSON shape falls back to a truncated raw-JSON one-liner rather than being silently dropped, per this movement's own named risk. The parser's real-shape table (assistant text/tool_use/thinking, user tool_result ok/error, result, system, rate_limit_event) was captured from a real `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose` run against the installed claude version, not invented. Live end-to-end smoke test (outside the unit suite, since AC-6 explicitly excludes spawning a real terminal from the test suite itself): a background writer appended the same real line shapes to a growing log file while `_tail-summary` polled it at a 0.1s interval against the writer's own pid, producing the expected three-line engineer.summary.log incrementally, then performed its own final catch-up drain and exited cleanly once the writer pid died. orchestrator status gained last_activity (the most recent engineer.summary.log line, or null); the new `watch` subcommand polls the same _status_row data status already computes via a new read-only _gather_watch_rows (never calls _save_state), clears and redraws a stdlib-only (os.system/shutil.get_terminal_size) table -- movement id, phase, pid-alive, heartbeat age, branch, worktree, last relay marker+timestamp, last activity -- truncated to terminal width, and exits cleanly on Ctrl-C; its docstring states explicitly why it loops until interrupted rather than returning after one bounded wait like local_relay.py's own watch (a human-facing live dashboard vs. an unattended, hard-timeout-ceilinged polling primitive). Backward compatibility verified directly: a movement record whose worktree_path has no .nexus/engineer.summary.log at all (the pre-this-movement shape) produces last_activity=None / rendered 'n/a' in both status and watch, no exception. Validation: tests/test_orchestrator.py, 28 new (across 21 new test functions, one parametrized 8 ways over the real-shape table) plus the 48 pre-existing, 76 passed, 0 failed. Full one-shot suite `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto --dist worksteal`: 2690 passed, 25 skipped, 2 failed -- both the same pre-existing, already-documented tests/test_dev_0_5b_auth_consumer_canonical_config.py DLP-scan false positive against this repository's own build_history.json/relay evidence text (gov_po_1_gate_5_worktree_management's and gov_po_1_local_relay_watch_command's own evidence already document the identical two failures), confirmed unrelated -- neither failing test nor the lines it flags were touched by this movement's diff. git diff --check clean. Repository privacy gate `.venv/bin/python main.py --repository-privacy-check`: FAIL/5 findings, identical to the 5 already documented in gov_po_3_approved_movement_orchestration_ac3's own evidence (data/, data/.support_hmac.key, logs/ -- untracked local runtime artifacts -- plus the same two pre-existing CREDENTIAL_LITERAL matches above), none in this movement's changed files; the two CREDENTIAL_LITERAL findings are now also recognized as pre-existing by the baseline-aware push-hook fix landed on origin/main concurrently with this movement (gov_po_3_push_hook_baseline_scoping), merged into this branch before opening this PR.\"\n}\n---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a8dd4a7-31e7-434f-89b1-73b3ad9d3b22","uuid":"3c15b63d-b1cd-43e9-ba13-9f8ec915c810","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:10:07.411Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"build\": \"op1_failover_plan_compiler_contract_draft\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"title\": \"OP.1 -- failover plan compiler and dry-run: contract draft (DRAFT -- awaiting Product Owner freeze)\",\n  \"summary\": \"Produces docs/history/phase/OP_1_FAILOVER_PLAN_COMPILER_AND_DRY_RUN.md (DRAFT -- awaiting Product Owner freeze): a write-free FailoverPlan/DryRunReport contract for classic Check Point ClusterXL only, compiled purely from already-collected OP.0a/OP.0b evidence (utils.failover.assessment.compute_ha_readiness) and reusing OP.2.0/OP.2.1's already-pure, zero-I/O checkpoint.clusterxl_capability_adapter.CPClusterXLCapabilityAdapter.capability()/build_plan() methods -- never check_precondition()/execute_once()/observe_postcondition(), never an ActionCoordinator, never a taxonomy change. Presents op_degraded_verdict to the Product Owner as one decision with the existing recommendation (keep DEGRADED_PROCEED_WITH_RISK structurally unreachable) and the consequence of each option for the plan/dry-run vocabulary; confirms op_four_eyes/op_emergency_evac/op_continuity_tolerance/op_aa_vsls_scope stay non-blocking. Includes a one-slice implementation plan (OP.1.S1, 5 non-test files, 8 acceptance criteria) sized to GOV.PO.1 section 7 targets.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"OP.x\",\n  \"movement\": \"ARCHITECTURE\",\n  \"evidence\": \"Relay-authorized movement (.nexus/approved_task.json SESSION_START, content-hash-verified against the Product Owner's relay entry). Read FAILOVER_ENGINE_ARCHITECTURE.md sections 1-10.2 and OP_2_0_CONTROLLED_HA_OPERATION_ARCHITECTURE.md in full before drafting, per the SESSION_START's own requirement. Verified (not assumed) that checkpoint.clusterxl_capability_adapter.CPClusterXLCapabilityAdapter.capability()/build_plan() perform zero I/O by reading their implementation directly (lines 175-278): neither references self._session_resolver; check_precondition()/execute_once()/observe_postcondition() all do and are excluded from this contract's design by construction. No code, test or checkpoint/ / utils/failover/ file touched, per the SESSION_START's explicit scope-out.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"Document is DRAFT only; promotion to FROZEN and the op_degraded_verdict decision remain a separate Product Owner action. Implementation slice OP.1.S1 leaves one narrow open implementation-detail question for its own PLAN step: whether to duplicate or extract-and-share the two private clusterxl_preflight_provider helpers (_map_cluster_mode/_resolve_member_tokens) the new utils/failover_plan/compiler.py needs -- deliberately left unresolved at contract level (see the doc's own S4 note).\",\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"agreement\": \"docs/history/phase/OP_1_FAILOVER_PLAN_COMPILER_AND_DRY_RUN.md\"\n  }\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"op0b_s7_s6_test_order_isolation\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"OP.0b S7/S6 test-order isolation -- fix the module-rebind state leak\",\n  \"summary\": \"tests/test_op0b_s7_readiness_v2.py::test_evaluator_performs_no_socket_io_and_imports_no_collector popped checkpoint.preflight_collector / panorama.preflight_collector out of sys.modules without restoring them, so any later `import panorama.preflight_collector as pc` (S6's collector tests) rebound to a fresh module object while S6's already-imported collect_member kept resolving api_post/get_direct_system_info/get_firewall_api_key against the original module dict, silently defeating S6's own patches and issuing real HTTP calls when S7 ran first. Fixed at the source with a save/restore try/finally around the same test; added a direct regression test proving the restoration (mirroring the frontend-rendering shared-state-leak guard precedent). Test-infrastructure only, no product code changed. In passing, also fixed (PO-authorized, relay/NXS-LOCAL-0016 seq 2-3, \\\"authorize narrow interpreter-resolution fix to the merge-lock re-validation hook\\\"): scripts/nexus_engineer_tool_gate.py's merge-lock re-validation subprocess calls used sys.executable directly, which resolved to a pytest-less system python3 in this session (a worktree checkout has no .venv of its own -- every worktree shares the one .venv next to the main checkout). New _resolve_interpreter()/_validation_commands() locate the shared .venv via `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` (stable across every worktree), falling back to sys.executable only if no .venv is found. Narrow, scoped to that one call site per the PO's authorization; nothing else in the hook touched.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"OP.0b\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Relay .nexus/approved_task.json SESSION_START (op0b_s7_s6_test_order_isolation, project/backlog.json). AC-1 reproduced at HEAD before any change: `pytest tests/test_op0b_s7_readiness_v2.py tests/test_op0b_s6_pan_preflight_collector.py` (S7 first) produced real S6 failures via a real, hanging `requests` connection attempt to the test fixture's synthetic management-IP target (F markers observed live during the run), exactly as backlog.json described. AC-2 root-caused by inspection: the sole `sys.modules.pop(\\\"panorama.preflight_collector\\\"/\\\"checkpoint.preflight_collector\\\", None)` in the repo is tests/test_op0b_s7_readiness_v2.py::test_evaluator_performs_no_socket_io_and_imports_no_collector (grep-verified as the only occurrence); it asserts both names are absent from sys.modules at the end by design but never restores them, so S6's later `import panorama.preflight_collector as pc` inside `_collect`/`run_pan_preflight` call sites rebinds `pc` to a new module object that S6's own `patch.object(pc, ...)` calls target, while `collect_member` (imported by S6's test file at collection time, before S7 executes) keeps resolving its api_post/get_direct_system_info/get_firewall_api_key globals against the ORIGINAL module dict -- a module-rebind/state-leak, same family as the frontend-rendering guard precedent (tests/test_frontend_rendering_boundary.py::test_render_uitest_restores_the_builders_it_injects). AC-3 fix: the popped sys.modules entries are captured before the pop and restored in a try/finally wrapping the existing test body; no reordering, no renaming, no global conftest hack. AC-4 order-independence: both invocation orders green -- `pytest tests/test_op0b_s7_readiness_v2.py tests/test_op0b_s6_pan_preflight_collector.py` = 110 passed; reverse order = 110 passed; each file alone unchanged in count (S7 69 incl. 1 new regression test, S6 41) -- plus a new direct regression test, tests/test_op0b_s7_readiness_v2.py::test_evaluator_probe_restores_the_collector_modules_it_pops, that asserts checkpoint.preflight_collector / panorama.preflight_collector module identity is unchanged before/after the probing test runs, so a future regression of this class is caught locally rather than surfacing as 25 unrelated S6 failures. AC-5: no product code changed (test file only, confirmed via git diff). AC-6: both files green individually and in both orders; pass counts unchanged apart from the one deliberately added regression test; no test skipped or removed. Interpreter-resolution fix verified directly: gate._resolve_interpreter() now returns the shared .venv path even from a real `git worktree add` checkout with no .venv of its own (new tests/test_nexus_engineer_tool_gate.py::test_resolve_interpreter_finds_shared_venv_via_git_common_dir), and falls back to sys.executable when no .venv exists (test_resolve_interpreter_falls_back_to_sys_executable_without_a_venv). Branch merged against an advancing origin/main a fourth time across two rounds (bookkeeping-only conflicts in CURRENT_STATE.md/docs/history/INDEX.md/project/build_history.json/project/roadmap.json, resolved by hand each time: op0b entry kept as the current/newest build, gov_po_3_resume_canonical_relay_access_fix (PR #130), m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers (PR #131) and m10_2_capability_state_resolver_core (PR #132) folded in as predecessors, INDEX.md regenerated via scripts/build_history_index.py, CURRENT_STATE.md kept <=200 lines). Full one-shot regression re-run after the final merge and the tooling fix: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto --dist worksteal` = 2943 passed, 25 skipped, 2 failed -- both pre-existing/unrelated (tests/test_dev_0_5b_auth_consumer_canonical_config.py's own DLP self-check false positive against project/build_history.json's own prose, documented since gov_po_1_local_relay_watch_command). S7+S6 both orders re-confirmed post-merge: 110 passed each. tests/test_architecture_convergence.py: 22 passed. scripts/build_history_index.py --check: up to date. git diff --check: clean.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"None for the S7/S6 fix itself. The interpreter-resolution fix is scoped to scripts/nexus_engineer_tool_gate.py's merge-lock re-validation call sites only, per the PO's own authorization (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0016 seq 3); it does not touch the hook's other sys.executable use (the merge-lock acquire/release orchestrator.py subprocess call), which was not reported broken and was left as-is.\"\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"m10_2_capability_state_resolver_core\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"M10.2 -- capability-state resolver core (stage 0, result algebra, primary ladder, qualifiers)\",\n  \"summary\": \"New utils/capability_state_resolver.py implements resolver stages 0-3 of docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md section 5, as pure typed-input functions with no I/O and no device contact: resolve_union_tag() decides the RESOLVED/OMITTED tag from D1 alone (Resolved and Omitted are structurally distinct dataclasses -- OMITTED carries only reason + optional diagnostic, never a None-filled capability output); evaluate_stage1()/evaluate_ri1_comparability() implement the CX1/RI-1/RI-2 contradiction-and-inconsistency gate, reusing utils.registry_evidence_reconciliation.detect_ri2 (M10.1) for RI-2 rather than reimplementing it, and the K1-K6 comparability precedence table for RI-1, in the frozen row order; resolve_primary_status() implements the twelve-rank primary ladder (ranks 0-11) first-match-wins; resolve_qualifiers() implements the seven independent CapabilityQualifier facets. The nine-value CapabilityState and seven-value CapabilityQualifier vocabularies are proven lexically disjoint from the console job lifecycle (X1), the OP.2 action-state vocabulary (X2) and utils.action_taxonomy tokens; to_wire() serializes only under the capability_state/capability_qualifiers keys the contract's namespacing rule (4.4) names.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"M10\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"SESSION_START relay/NXS-LOCAL-0008, dispatched into this movement's own git worktree; read docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md sections 3.3/4/5 in full before writing code, per the SESSION_START's own requirement. New tests/test_m10_2_capability_state_resolver.py (134 tests): stage 0's four union-tag cases V-A..V-D plus OMITTED/Resolved structural-distinctness checks (AC-1); exactly-nine/exactly-seven vocabulary checks plus lexical-disjointness parametrized tests against console/jobs.py TERMINAL_STATES, utils/operate/states.py ActionState and utils/action_taxonomy.py ACTION_CLASSES, plus a to_wire() namespacing test (AC-2); CX1 from I10, the full K1-K6 precedence table one row at a time plus two mixed-ordering cases, and RI-2 reuse via detect_ri2 (AC-3); one test per primary-ladder rank 0-11 plus the rank-8-vs-9 fail-closed-ordering case and a D5=POLICY_UNKNOWN-never-reaches-rank-11 case (AC-4); one test per qualifier plus the four 4.1.5 inference-ban negative tests (AC-5); an AST-based purity check proving no requests/paramiko/socket/subprocess import and no utils.capability_registry import (AC-6). All 134 passed. Affected regression: tests/test_m10_1_registry_evidence_reconciliation.py + tests/test_architecture_convergence.py, 78 passed, metadata_warnings empty. git diff --check clean.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"Stages 4-5 (evidence presentation, action affordance) and the D2/D3/D5 producers remain unimplemented by design (M10.3/M12) -- this module only consumes already-resolved values of those dimensions via typed inputs (EntityApplicability, VendorSupport, CapabilityPolicy), and no caller wires it into html_export, console, any payload or navigation module yet. The stage-0 diagnostic pass (4.1.4) is explicitly OPTIONAL and not computed here; Diagnostic is a plain passthrough a future caller may attach.\",\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"agreement\": \"docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md\"\n  }\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"gov_po_3_resume_canonical_relay_access_fix\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"GOV.PO.3 -- resume canonical-relay access fix: --add-dir the canonical relay directory on every engineer spawn\",\n  \"summary\": \"Closes the finding recorded in relay/NXS-LOCAL-0012's SESSION_CLOSE (`next`): a resumed engineer session (`orchestrator start`'s `--resume` path) could not read/write the canonical relay file outside its own worktree, while a fresh dispatch could -- blocking every future interrupted/resumed movement from completing autonomously (GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md section 3.7's own recovery design). Root cause (AC-2, confirmed live, not assumed): with `--permission-prompts none` a Read/Edit/Write-tool call to a path outside the worktree has no approval surface, is auto-denied, and stays denied for the rest of the session with no retries; a fresh dispatch only ever appeared to work because it happened to route relay access through Bash-invoked `scripts/local_relay.py`, which this per-tool directory allowlist does not gate -- nothing guaranteed a resumed session would route the same way. Fix (AC-3): `scripts/orchestrator.py::_spawn_engineer` now passes `--add-dir <canonical_relay_dir>` identically for a fresh dispatch and a resume, so access no longer depends on which tool a session happens to pick.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"GOV\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Relay relay/NXS-LOCAL-0015-resume-canonical-relay-access-fix.json, validated protocol-v2 SESSION_START. AC-4 real reproduction (not a simplified proxy): dispatched a throwaway scratch movement (relay/NXS-LOCAL-0017-gov-po-3-resume-fix-ac4-repro-postfix.json, now CLOSED) through the real `scripts/orchestrator.py` -- fresh dispatch posted RELAY_ACK+RELAY_QUESTION and exited; a RELAY_DECISION was posted; a real orchestrator resume (no simplified proxy) re-read the canonical relay file fresh from disk and quoted the RELAY_DECISION's subject verbatim in its own RELAY_NOTE, reproducing and closing the exact gap found live in relay/NXS-LOCAL-0012. AC-5 (no regression): fresh-dispatch access was exercised in the same real run and still works, and tests/test_orchestrator.py::test_spawn_engineer_grants_add_dir_for_the_canonical_relay_directory_on_fresh_dispatch asserts the fresh-dispatch argv shape explicitly. New tests/test_orchestrator.py (+2): fresh-dispatch and resume both get the identical `--add-dir <canonical_relay_dir>` grant, resume argv ending in `--resume <session_id>` unchanged otherwise. This branch reconciled two concurrent merges to origin/main during integration: relay/NXS-LOCAL-0013 (gov_po_3_orchestrator_observability, PR #129 -- both movements changed `_spawn_engineer`'s argv construction, reconciled by hand so `--add-dir` and `--output-format stream-json --verbose` coexist, and this movement's two tests updated to read the engineer process's own Popen call now that a second, summary-tailer Popen call is also made) and relay/NXS-LOCAL-0010 (m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers, PR #131 -- unrelated files, bookkeeping-only conflict). Full one-shot suite `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto --dist worksteal` (post-merge): 2699 passed, 25 skipped, 2 failed -- both pre-existing/unrelated (tests/test_dev_0_5b_auth_consumer_canonical_config.py's own DLP-collision self-check against repository prose, same documented false positive as prior builds). git diff --check clean.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"In passing, this movement's engineer session found (documented, NOT fixed here -- out of scope per this movement's own invariant against other orchestrator.py behavior changes): `scripts/orchestrator.py` never persists the real `claude` session_id (always None), so its 'resume' path never actually passes `--resume` to the `claude` CLI; it currently works only because a fresh re-spawn into the same worktree/branch behaves equivalently for this task shape. A follow-up movement should fix session-id persistence itself.\",\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"agreement\": \"scripts/orchestrator.py\"\n  }\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"M10.3 -- D2 entity-applicability and D3 vendor/platform-support producers\",\n  \"summary\": \"New utils/capability_applicability.py (resolve_d2) and utils/capability_vendor_support.py (resolve_d3): pure, offline, closed-table producers for CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md section 3.3 D2 (APPLICABLE/NOT_APPLICABLE/APPLICABILITY_UNKNOWN, from NAVIGATION_INFORMATION_ARCHITECTURE.md section 5.2's eight logical entity types) and D3 (SUPPORTED/UNSUPPORTED/SUPPORT_UNKNOWN, from real repository collector/adapter evidence). Every APPLICABLE/NOT_APPLICABLE/SUPPORTED entry cites its exact repository or doc source; every pair with no citable source resolves the UNKNOWN value naming the gap, never a guess (section 7.3, section 8.2 point 1). No UNSUPPORTED entry is populated: the review found no citable positive evidence of vendor non-support for any of the seven PCP.0 capabilities, only evidence of what is and is not yet implemented (utils/operate/adapter.py carries zero concrete vendor adapter and is the D3-cited input for controlled_operations; no telemetry or diagnostics producer exists anywhere) -- an absent producer is SUPPORT_UNKNOWN, never UNSUPPORTED, superseding PRODUCT_CONTROL_PLANE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 8's own informal worked-example wording. Neither module imports or extends utils/capability_registry.py.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"PRODUCT\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Branch feature/m10-3-entity-and-vendor-support-producers from origin/main. Read docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md sections 3.3 (D2, D3), 4 (vocabulary), 7.3 (positive-evidence rule), 8.2 (fail-closed/honest-unknown); docs/design/NAVIGATION_INFORMATION_ARCHITECTURE.md sections 5.2, 6.4, 7.2; docs/design/PRODUCT_CONTROL_PLANE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 8; docs/design/FAILOVER_ENGINE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 10.2; console/registry.py; application/cli.py; application/workflows/checkpoint.py; application/workflows/recovery.py; checkpoint/cp_runner.py, checkpoint/vsx_runner.py, checkpoint/checkpoint_recovery_collector.py; panorama/panorama_runtime_runner.py, panorama/panorama_recovery_collector.py; configuration/checkpoint_config_collector.py, configuration/panorama_config_collector.py; utils/failover/assessment.py; utils/operate/adapter.py -- before writing either table, per this movement's own requirements. D2's entity-applicability table: inventory/configuration_collection/backup APPLICABLE for all eight entity types (nav contract section 6.4, entity types: all); ha_readiness APPLICABLE for CP ClusterXL cluster/VSX host-cluster/virtual system (VSLS VSID)/PAN HA pair and NOT_APPLICABLE for both standalone entity types (section 6.4's named list plus section 7.2's explicit worked example), APPLICABILITY_UNKNOWN at member level (neither source addresses it); controlled_operations NOT_APPLICABLE for CP virtual system only (FAILOVER_ENGINE_ARCHITECTURE.md section 10.2: a VSID is never a CLASS 2 lock subject), APPLICABILITY_UNKNOWN elsewhere; telemetry/diagnostics APPLICABILITY_UNKNOWN for every entity type (no source found). D3's vendor-support table: inventory/configuration_collection/backup/ha_readiness SUPPORTED for both checkpoint and panorama, each citing the real wired collector module; controlled_operations/telemetry/diagnostics SUPPORT_UNKNOWN for both vendors (no producer). tests/test_m10_3_entity_and_vendor_support_producers.py (107 tests): vocabulary closure, every table branch, unestablished/unrecognized entity-type/vendor/capability inputs, a signature-introspection test proving resolve_d3 cannot even accept a collection-outcome argument, a citation-format check that every positive/negative entry names a real source, and vocabulary-separation against the job lifecycle / OP.2 action-state / action-taxonomy tokens (AC-4, mirroring M10.1's own AC-8 precedent), plus D2/D3 mutual disjointness. Validation: targeted suite 107 passed; tests/test_architecture_convergence.py 22 passed unchanged; py_compile clean on both new modules and the test file; git diff --check clean.\",\n  \"risks_forward\": \"Neither producer is wired to the M10.2 resolver, any UI, payload or navigation surface -- out of this movement's scope by its own output_contract. D2's member-level HA-readiness applicability (CP ClusterXL member, PAN HA member) and D3's controlled_operations/telemetry/diagnostics support are genuine, named UNKNOWN gaps, not implementation debt to silently close later: closing them requires new positive evidence (a vendor doc, a real adapter, a real collector), not a table edit. project/feature_registry.json's left_vertical_product_navigation availability_rule criterion stays 'pending' -- these are two of its predicates' producers, not the wiring that would move the criterion.\",\n  \"docs\": {\n    \"agreement\": \"docs/design/CAPABILITY_STATE_VOCABULARY_AND_PRESENTATION.md\"\n  }\n}\n---\n{\n  \"build\": \"gov_po_3_orchestrator_observability\",\n  \"status\": \"automated_validated\",\n  \"title\": \"GOV.PO.3 -- orchestrator observability: streaming engineer output + watch dashboard\",\n  \"summary\": \"Extends the already-frozen scripts/orchestrator.py (docs/design/GOV_PO_3_APPROVED_MOVEMENT_ORCHESTRATION.md section 3.4) with real-time visibility: the engineer's claude -p invocation now streams stream-json output incrementally instead of only at process exit, a new dependency-free parser derives a human-readable engineer.summary.log alongside the raw log, orchestrator status gains a last_activity field, and a new read-only `orchestrator watch` terminal dashboard polls the same status data in a loop until Ctrl-C. Backward compatible with movements dispatched before this change.\",\n  \"started\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"completed\": \"2026-09-08\",\n  \"track\": \"GOV\",\n  \"movement\": \"IMPLEMENTATION\",\n  \"supersedes\": null,\n  \"evidence\": \"Relay relay/NXS-LOCAL-0013-orchestrator-observability.json, validated protocol-v2 SESSION_START (Product Owner direction immediately after AC-3/AC-5 demonstration 1 of gov_po_3_approved_movement_orchestration_ac3 ran live and confirmed engineer.log stayed empty until process exit under the prior, non-streaming claude -p invocation -- a real, observed gap). Verified the exact flag spelling for real before coding, per this movement's own requirement: `claude -p --help` against the installed claude 2.1.263, and a live `claude -p ... --output-format stream-json` run without --verbose, which fails closed with 'Error: When using --print, --output-format=stream-json requires --verbose' -- confirming both flags are required together, not assumed from documentation. _spawn_engineer's argv now carries --output-format stream-json --verbose alongside the existing -p; a second, detached `_tail-summary` subprocess (an internal, undocumented CLI subcommand, never invoked directly) tails engineer.log from a byte offset, decodes and summarizes each complete line with a new stdlib-only, dependency-free parser (summarize_stream_json_line), and appends one line per event to a sibling engineer.summary.log -- a truncated last line at read time is left unconsumed and re-read once complete, never dropped or crashed on; an unrecognized-but-valid JSON shape falls back to a truncated raw-JSON one-liner rather than being silently dropped, per this movement's own named risk. The parser's real-shape table (assistant text/tool_use/thinking, user tool_result ok/error, result, system, rate_limit_event) was captured from a real `claude -p --output-format stream-json --verbose` run against the installed claude version, not invented. Live end-to-end smoke test (outside the unit suite, since AC-6 explicitly excludes spawning a real terminal from the test suite itself): a background writer appended the same real line shapes to a growing log file while `_tail-summary` polled it at a 0.1s interval against the writer's own pid, producing the expected three-line engineer.summary.log incrementally, then performed its own final catch-up drain and exited cleanly once the writer pid died. orchestrator status gained last_activity (the most recent engineer.summary.log line, or null); the new `watch` subcommand polls the same _status_row data status already computes via a new read-only _gather_watch_rows (never calls _save_state), clears and redraws a stdlib-only (os.system/shutil.get_terminal_size) table -- movement id, phase, pid-alive, heartbeat age, branch, worktree, last relay marker+timestamp, last activity -- truncated to terminal width, and exits cleanly on Ctrl-C; its docstring states explicitly why it loops until interrupted rather than returning after one bounded wait like local_relay.py's own watch (a human-facing live dashboard vs. an unattended, hard-timeout-ceilinged polling primitive). Backward compatibility verified directly: a movement record whose worktree_path has no .nexus/engineer.summary.log at all (the pre-this-movement shape) produces last_activity=None / rendered 'n/a' in both status and watch, no exception. Validation: tests/test_orchestrator.py, 28 new (across 21 new test functions, one parametrized 8 ways over the real-shape table) plus the 48 pre-existing, 76 passed, 0 failed. Full one-shot suite `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q -n auto --dist worksteal`: 2690 passed, 25 skipped, 2 failed -- both the same pre-existing, already-documented tests/test_dev_0_5b_auth_consumer_canonical_config.py DLP-scan false positive against this repository's own build_history.json/relay evidence text (gov_po_1_gate_5_worktree_management's and gov_po_1_local_relay_watch_command's own evidence already document the identical two failures), confirmed unrelated -- neither failing test nor the lines it flags were touched by this movement's diff. git diff --check clean. Repository privacy gate `.venv/bin/python main.py --repository-privacy-check`: FAIL/5 findings, identical to the 5 already documented in gov_po_3_approved_movement_orchestration_ac3's own evidence (data/, data/.support_hmac.key, logs/ -- untracked local runtime artifacts -- plus the same two pre-existing CREDENTIAL_LITERAL matches above), none in this movement's changed files; the two CREDENTIAL_LITERAL findings are now also recognized as pre-existing by the baseline-aware push-hook fix landed on origin/main concurrently with this movement (gov_po_3_push_hook_baseline_scoping), merged into this branch before opening this PR.\"\n}\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
