{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015E4PpSiKXoU9hwVKZAet9b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"GOV.PO.3 -- interactive PO + Orchestrator workbench backend\n2\t(project/backlog.json id orchestrator_interactive_dashboard_app; design\n3\tacknowledged relay/NXS-LOCAL-0021 seq 2-3, FIRST DISPATCH bounded by that\n4\tmovement's own \"PO SCOPE BOUNDARY 2026-09-08\" section).\n5\t\n6\t    py scripts/orchestrator.py dashboard [--port N] [--relay-dir DIR]\n7\t        [--state-dir DIR] [--repo-root DIR]\n8\t\n9\tRead+relay-write only (AC-4): every write route below ends by calling\n10\t`local_relay.py`'s own `append` path (in-process, via its public\n11\t`build_parser()`/`_cmd_append`) with a movement's own already-registered\n12\toperation/args -- this module never runs `git`/`gh` to mutate anything, and\n13\tnever runs a shell string. Read-only `git status --porcelain` / `git\n14\trev-list` / `gh pr list` calls are in scope (the backlog note's own\n15\tRECOMMENDED ARCHITECTURE section (A2) names them) purely for display; no\n16\tbutton here ever triggers one.\n17\t\n18\tReuses `scripts/orchestrator.py`'s own status-computation functions\n19\t(`_status_row`, `_list_state_records`, `pid_alive`, `canonical_json`, ...)\n20\tand `scripts/local_relay.py` directly (AC-6): no new scheduler, no new\n21\tstate model, no third-party dependency, stdlib `http.server` only, bound to\n22\t127.0.0.1.\n23\t\n24\tSecurity (AC-2c, acknowledged relay/NXS-LOCAL-0021 seq 3): one\n25\t`secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` bearer token per process launch, printed once\n26\tas a URL fragment (`http://127.0.0.1:<port>/#t=<token>`), held only in\n27\tmemory (this module's `_TOKEN_HOLDER`, never written to disk), compared\n28\twith `hmac.compare_digest`. Every `/api/*` route -- read or write --\n29\trequires it as an `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header; `GET /` and\n30\tstatic assets do not (no evidence lives in them). `Origin` is checked as\n31\tdefense-in-depth on every state-changing (PUT/POST) `/api/*` route:\n32\trejected if present and not equal to `http://127.0.0.1:<port>` (absence is\n33\tallowed -- the bearer token, not Origin, is the real authorization\n34\tboundary).\n35\t\n36\tAction-id registry (AC-2a): an executable-request card issues a\n37\tdeterministic `action_id = sha256(canonical_json({movement_id, relay_file,\n38\toperation, args, working_directory, source_relay_seq}))[:16]`, stored in\n39\t`<state_dir>/<movement_id>.actions.json` (runtime bookkeeping, same bucket\n40\tas orchestrator.py's own process-state files -- not durable governance\n41\thistory, never under `relay/`). Consuming an id checks it is unconsumed and\n42\tthat the movement's relay entry count still equals `source_relay_seq` (the\n43\tsame \"REVISION_CHANGED_SINCE_DISPATCH\" signal `orchestrator.py::_status_row`\n44\talready computes) before calling `local_relay.py`'s append path with the\n45\tregistered args; `local_relay.py`'s own optimistic-concurrency hash compare\n46\tstays a second, independent guard at the actual write.\n47\t\n48\tBlocker-source tagging: the three-way routing AC-3 requires (already\n49\tauthorized / genuinely new decision / platform policy) is read from an\n50\toptional bracket tag at the start of the blocking `RELAY_QUESTION`/\n51\t`RELAY_NOTE` entry's own `subject` field -- `[AUTHORIZED]`, `[BLOCKED]`, or\n52\tno tag (defaults to a genuine decision, the safe default: an unlabeled\n53\trequest never silently auto-routes). This is plain text inside an existing\n54\tfield, not a new marker or a new file format, matching AC-2b's design.\n55\t\n56\tMessage box (AMENDMENT's \"send a note to this work\" field): appending to\n57\tthe relay is only ever possible on the PO's own turn (the frozen protocol's\n58\tsingle-writer rule, docs/design/LOCAL_RELAY_PROTOCOL.md). When it is not\n59\tthe PO's turn, a message is saved to a small per-movement outbox file\n60\t(`<state_dir>/<movement_id>.outbox.json`, same runtime-bookkeeping bucket)\n61\tand surfaced honestly as not-yet-appended -- never shown as delivered.\n62\t\"\"\"\n63\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n64\t\n65\timport argparse\n66\timport contextlib\n67\timport hashlib\n68\timport hmac\n69\timport io\n70\timport json\n71\timport secrets\n72\timport shutil\n73\timport subprocess\n74\timport sys\n75\tfrom http import HTTPStatus\n76\tfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n77\tfrom pathlib import Path\n78\tfrom typing import Any\n79\tfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlsplit\n80\t\n81\tREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n82\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO_ROOT / \"scripts\"))\n83\timport local_relay as lr  # noqa: E402\n84\timport orchestrator as orch  # noqa: E402\n85\t\n86\tASSETS_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent / \"dashboard_assets\"\n87\tDEFAULT_PORT = 8765\n88\tDEFAULT_CONFIG_FILENAME = \"dashboard_config.json\"\n89\tCONFIG_INTERVAL_MIN = 2\n90\tCONFIG_INTERVAL_MAX = 3600\n91\tLOG_TAIL_DEFAULT = 200\n92\tLOG_TAIL_MAX = 2000\n93\t\n94\tSTAGE_NOT_STARTED = \"not_started\"\n95\tSTAGE_CODING = \"coding\"\n96\tSTAGE_RESOLVING_CONFLICT = \"resolving_merge_conflict\"\n97\tSTAGE_TESTING = \"testing\"\n98\tSTAGE_AWAITING_PO = \"awaiting_po\"\n99\tSTAGE_INTEGRATION = \"integration\"\n100\tSTAGE_MERGED = \"merged\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2940a6ba-1db4-4dd1-973a-c2b7cdc738e2","uuid":"dfefdb83-4195-46ac-8fed-b3b183582153","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:24:11.441Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/OzanDur/Codo/neXus-nexus-worktrees/NXS-LOCAL-0021/scripts/orchestrator_dashboard.py","content":"\"\"\"GOV.PO.3 -- interactive PO + Orchestrator workbench backend\n(project/backlog.json id orchestrator_interactive_dashboard_app; design\nacknowledged relay/NXS-LOCAL-0021 seq 2-3, FIRST DISPATCH bounded by that\nmovement's own \"PO SCOPE BOUNDARY 2026-09-08\" section).\n\n    py scripts/orchestrator.py dashboard [--port N] [--relay-dir DIR]\n        [--