{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016yGLs45LCRX7HgEu6SYL2D","type":"tool_result","content":"175\t   `DRAFT` / `DO NOT FREEZE` is evidence/design work, not authority.\n176\t3. If no build names a contract for your task, there isn't an active one —\n177\t   that itself may mean a `CONTRACT` movement is the actual next step.\n178\t\n179\t---\n180\t\n181\t## SESSION START (produce at the start of every meaningful build/task)\n182\t\n183\tEnglish, no preamble (`AGENTS.md` \"Engineering-output language law\"):\n184\t\n185\t- authoritative product baseline and engineering baseline (from\n186\t  `CURRENT_STATE.md`, never hard-coded),\n187\t- requested build/task and explicit scope (in/out),\n188\t- movement type (`AGENTS.md` \"Mandatory session start\" list),\n189\t- source/tests expected to be inspected,\n190\t- important invariants and risks,\n191\t- context intentionally not loaded,\n192\t- recommended model/reasoning tier for the next action (table below),\n193\t- recommended Git lane for this build (`feature/*`, `build/*`, or direct\n194\t  `main` hotfix),\n195\t- merge-to-`main` gate recommendation and required evidence,\n196\t- deployment direction for this task (`local validation only`,\n197\t  `staging-like`, or `production-gated`).\n198\t\n199\tDo not ask the user to repeat settled project context the repository can\n200\tanswer.\n201\t\n202\t## SESSION CLOSE (produce before declaring a build complete)\n203\t\n204\tUpdate durable project state first (`AGENTS.md` \"Project-state update\n205\trule\"), then report:\n206\t\n207\t- what was completed; what changed vs. what was deliberately preserved,\n208\t- targeted tests and full-regression evidence,\n209\t- privacy gate and state-consistency results,\n210\t- unresolved risks/gaps,\n211\t- roadmap/backlog/build-history changes made,\n212\t- exact next build/task and recommended next movement type,\n213\t- recommended model/reasoning tier for that next step,\n214\t- whether the next chat should continue this session or start fresh,\n215\t- recommended branch/PR target and explicit `main` merge decision\n216\t  (`approved` or `blocked`, with reason),\n217\t- exact non-interactive Git dispatch commands for the recommended path\n218\t  (stage/commit/push/PR base),\n219\t- explicit `main.py`/UI effect note: what should be visible after a normal\n220\t  run, or confirmation that backend-only work produces no visible UI change.\n221\t\n222\tIf implementation is complete but human validation is pending, say so and do\n223\tnot advance durable state beyond the evidence.\n224\t\n225\tWhen this report crosses a session/tool boundary, it transports as one\n226\t`NEXUS_SESSION_PACKET` whose `report` object carries every bullet above,\n227\tfield by field — never a pointer to a narrative said elsewhere, never\n228\tnarrative alongside the packet (`docs/design/GOV_SESSION_TRANSFER_PROTOCOL.md`).\n229\t\n230\t## Reasoning / model routing tiers\n231\t\n232\tRouting is task-driven (`AGENTS.md` \"AI reasoning / movement routing\"); this\n233\tis the concrete tier table. Tool-specific tier *names* (a specific Claude or\n234\tCopilot model) belong only in that tool's own delta file — this table uses"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2940a6ba-1db4-4dd1-973a-c2b7cdc738e2","uuid":"2bfd431b-f8e1-4fa6-95bf-f3ac4b5390ac","timestamp":"2026-09-08T17:25:20.869Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/OzanDur/Codo/neXus-nexus-worktrees/NXS-LOCAL-0021/AI_START_HERE.md","content":"   `DRAFT` / `DO NOT FREEZE` is evidence/design work, not authority.\n3. If no build names a contract for your task, there isn't an active one —\n   that itself may mean a `CONTRACT` movement is the actual next step.\n\n---\n\n## SESSION START (produce at the start of every meaningful build/task)\n\nEnglish, no preamble (`AGENTS.md` \"Engineering-output language law\"):\n\n- authoritative product baseline and engineering baseline (from\n  `CURRENT_STATE.md`, never 