e_gate': \"AC-2's design note needs an explicit Product Owner acknowledgment before AC-3 implementation begins (a design checkpoint, not a full stop on the whole movement). Once AC-3 onward is green, standing relay#13 applies: self-merge, report via RELAY_NOTE.\", 'movement_type': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'objective': 'Build the interactive PO + Orchestrator workbench the Product Owner scoped and bounded in project/backlog.json id orchestrator_interactive_dashboard_app -- a human-action inbox, live movement tracking with a real detail panel, message delivery, and authorized-command routing, all read+relay-write only.', 'output_contract': ['A short technical-design RELAY_NOTE (AC-2), acknowledged before AC-3 begins', 'scripts/orchestrator.py dashboard subcommand + backend + frontend assets (AC-3 through AC-6)', 'Targeted tests (AC-7)', 'Real acceptance-demonstration evidence (AC-8)', 'Project-state bookkeeping in this PR', 'SESSION_CLOSE on this relay file (absolute path)'], 'recommended_reasoning': {'reason': \"New architecture on top of an already-fully-scoped backlog spec -- AC-2's three technical-design questions (action-id registry, relay-write schema, CSRF scheme) are genuine design decisions needing real reasoning; AC-3 onward is deterministic once AC-2 is acknowledged.\", 'tier': \"Sonnet 5, extended thinking (high) for AC-2's design note; Sonnet 5, normal for AC-3 onward implementation\"}, 'requirements': [\"Do not restate or redesign the backlog note's already-decided IN SCOPE/DEFERRED boundary -- implement it\"], 'risks': [\"If AC-2's design questions turn out to need a genuinely new file format or dependency to answer well, stop and report via RELAY_QUESTION rather than silently expanding scope.\"], 'scope': {'in': [\"Everything listed IN SCOPE in the backlog note's 'PO SCOPE BOUNDARY 2026-09-08' section\", \"AC-2's three technical-design questions\"], 'out': ['Everything listed DEFERRED in that same section -- direct git/gh/shell execution buttons, real Evidence-